window.DR_STR_DIALOGUE={"line:0516fe1":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: What'll it be?","line:0999f40":"You enter a squalid shack on the fringe of the marketplace. The familiar smell of fish fills the air. Flies buzz haphazardly around a downcast man behind the counter.","line:0e18b0b":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: You're the new fisherman, eh? Surprised they found a new one so fast.","line:0109e6f":"What happened to the other one?","line:0fceac8":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: He...it takes a certain type of person to last out here. It's not a life for everyone.","line:01993ad":"What's your name?","line:04342c0":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: There's no sense getting familiar. You'll be on your way like the rest of them soon, no doubt.","line:019bd32":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Anyway, to business. I'll pay you for fish. [C1]Bigger and fresher means more money[/C1]. Some species are just worth more, too.","line:0dab4f0":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Other towns on other islands might pay you different...but while you've still got a debt outstanding here, I'd suggest you work on paying it off first.","line:0de3b05":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: So, let's see what you've got.","line:0491b69":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: What've you got for me today?","line:0e13cf8":"The morning light fills your eyes, and you try to sit upright. You're lying on the cold, wet dock where you collapsed the night before.","line:0dcd998":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Welcome to [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0]! I must say, quite the dramatic first impression - I see you've already introduced yourself to the [C2]jagged rocks[/C2] along the bay.","line:0146ec9":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Did you not see the lighthouse? It was shining right at you! Ah well, I'm glad to see our [C0]new fisherman[/C0] upright and breathing.","line:0913b90":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: [C2]Your boat was hopelessly damaged[/C2], but I've had a few of the locals [C1]move your things to one of our old vessels[/C1]. We'll catch up later to discuss more details.","line:0b7cc31":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Finally, I don't suppose I need to say this, but [C2]get back by sundown, before the fog rolls in[/C2]. Keep a close eye on the time. It can really creep up on you.","line:02a6ba8":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: No fish? [C0]Get out there and catch something[/C0] for these hungry townsfolk.","line:00f47b7":"You step onto the dock at Greater Marrow. The Mayor is waiting nearby.","line:0eead93":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Ah, I see you've returned in one piece. Very good. Before you head off to town, we should discuss the matter of [C0]your boat[/C0].","line:0c9b5be":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I understand you may not have the necessary funds on hand, so we'll consider it a [C2]loan[/C2]. But I want to make this easy for you.","line:080b4fa":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: So, to recap, you'll need to sell fish to the local market, paying off your debt and, in turn, keeping the population fed and satisfied. Understand?","line:05f266e":"Selling fish helps the town and pays off my debt. Got it.","line:0b23c1e":"Where do I sell the fish?","line:07bac02":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Our local [C0]Fishmonger[/C0] will appraise and purchase what you catch. He's open all hours.","line:07b4c27":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Off you go then - sell those fish while they're still fresh!","line:0188391":"The Mayor is standing outside the Fishmonger's store.","line:0a951ed":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Excellent work, I have no doubt you'll be able to provide for this town.","line:0df7eed":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Oh, one last thing! Our local [C0]Shipwright[/C0] mentioned she might be able to make some [C1]modifications to your ship[/C1]. You should pay her a visit.","line:0b26c40":"As you walk into the yard, you see the [C0]Shipwright[/C0] making repairs to a damaged hull. She looks up at you briefly before turning back to her work.","line:05dacd2":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: You must be the new fisherman. [C1]I can make improvements to your vessel[/C1] in the yard.","line:0d5bcb2":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Mind you, I'm not in the business of doing favors 'round here - payment is upfront. And [C2]everything takes some time to install[/C2].","line:0fad99b":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Also, if you take on any [C2]damage[/C2] from the rocks or...any damage at all, [C1]I can patch it up[/C1]. Mostly.","line:07a06bb":"She shrugs and gestures towards the hull she's currently attempting to repair. A number of wooden boards - all well above the water line - are splintered and scratched.","line:09e7142":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Take a look 'round. Just remember - [C2]the bigger the equipment, the longer it takes to install[/C2]. So plan ahead.","line:05af3bc":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Just the person I was hoping to see! Will you be sailing out [C0]East[/C0], towards [C0]Little Marrow[/C0]? Would you give this package to the [C0]Dockworker[/C0] there please?","line:03f5d36":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Oh, sorry, all full up? [C0]Come back when you have more space[/C0] on board.","line:0dbe3cc":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Don't forget to check your [C0]Compass[/C0] and [C0]Map[/C0] if you get lost!","line:04a97d8":"The Mayor hands you a small, damp package bound in string. It's dripping slightly.","line:04a804a":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Hmm, what - a delivery? Let's see here...","line:09a297d":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: I was given this old book a few weeks back, but it didn't make much sense to me. You'll surely get more use out of it.","line:0e1047b":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Keep it in your cabin, perhaps you can read it while you're on the water.","line:0550119":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: What is it today?","line:0787c86":"You hand the [C3]grotesque fish[/C3] to the Fishmonger. He grins, raising the fish up to his face before inhaling a deep, stuttering breath.","line:06b2827":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Ahh...now, this is the sort of specimen to liven up my day. Hmm, I wonder...","line:084ecd2":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: It's not the first corrupted fish I've seen in these parts, so I'm sure you'll find more before too long. [C1]I'll pay you well if you find any more[/C1].","line:0cb067d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: So, will you allow me to fit your vessel with dredging equipment? I'll need a few hours.","line:002a5f3":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: An excellent decision. I'll prepare the equipment immediately.","line:03a542a":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I would encourage you to [C0]ask around the towns about shipwrecks or other strange occurrences[/C0] - anything that might be worth investigating.","line:0d69a2b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Hmm. Return when you change your mind.","line:03eaf92":"You enter a brightly lit shop. It's packed with antiques, the shelves full of jewellery and other baubles. An old man peers at you over silver spectacles.","line:0e88dc8":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Hello? Is that...no - ah, I don't believe we've met. Forgive me, my eyes aren't what they used to be.","line:035cade":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: I specialize in antiques and jewellery. I'll [C1]purchase any special trinkets[/C1] you happen to have.","line:0274dcc":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Have you got anything nice with you today, perhaps?","line:063fa4b":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Welcome! Found anything special lately?","line:05e9046":"You explain that you've sold an engraved belt buckle to The Trader.","line:02e5902":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: You - oh. Well, maybe that wasn't his... I'd - I'd better go and check before he melts it down!","line:0245237":"The man hurries away towards the Trader.","line:062dbf7":"You give the belt buckle to the man.","line:0c2822e":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: This is...this is his! Oh, thank you, bless you. You've returned him to me...","line:0235e7f":"You approach a woman sitting on the dockside, staring out to sea. She turns to you.","line:05b49c1":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: What's it like out there?","line:083f261":"It's peaceful.","line:0965a4f":"It's difficult.","line:07cdc4d":"I don't want to talk about it.","line:0a546fe":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: It's got to be a damn sight better than this bloody town. I think I just need to get away for a while -- maybe not come back.","line:0f8eaaa":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Going backwards is a mistake, don't you think? You should always keep moving forward. Moving along.","line:098738b":"It's not so bad here.","line:003bb3b":"I don't want to move along.","line:0604d9c":"I can't go back.","line:0b7cef1":"She's gazing out to sea again, lost in thought.","line:035883b":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Say, if you find me some materials, maybe you can help me move? I mean, really move. There's an island I've heard about, [C0]Steel Point, just to the North[/C0].","line:05f4d8b":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: [C0]Two units of Lumber[/C0] and [C0]Two units of Scrap[/C0] is all I need. I can make a new place for myself out there. You'd be welcome to visit, too.","line:0ab14c8":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Just [C0]stack it up at Steel Point[/C0] when you have anything. I'll pay you when the job's done.","line:0f0069b":"This is the island where the [C0]Builder[/C0] wants materials delivered.","line:077b2f6":"You've delivered all the necessary materials. You should let the Builder know.","line:0f8f688":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: You've done it? Well, no sense in wasting time. Let's get moving.","line:0f2cbb1":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Good riddance to you, [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0]. I'm onward bound.","line:0c66dd4":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: No room on deck? [C0]Come back when you have more space[/C0]. I'll be waiting.","line:0900a52":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Yes...yes, this'll do. Thank you, fella.","line:0a15454":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Give me a short while to get things built here. You're welcome back any time.","line:0b8d9f8":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Take these. Always good to have on hand.","line:01d69e5":"A hunched woman approaches you from the steps to the lighthouse. She stops some distance away and looks at you with concern and visible apprehension.","line:0c19954":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Why are you here?","line:0bf9ebf":"I've come to fish.","line:0584f0b":"I've come to see the area.","line:0e334c6":"I've come to meet people.","line:026ff4d":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: There's nothing here for someone like you anymore. Do yourself a favor and move on.","line:01c39f6":"She turns and shuffles back along the path that leads to the light.","line:08a207e":"You enter the Collector's house. He's standing at the back of the room, still holding the silver and crimson book. He seems impatient.","line:06dd20b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Well? You have something, don't you? Show me.","line:0cd1486":"You hand him the key. The cold metal shimmers a [C3]strange shine[/C3] as he holds it. The shape of the key - the teeth, the head - now somehow seem changed, smaller. Has it always been this way?","line:04e05e8":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Is this all? Where is the lock?","line:04daa09":"The Collector grows agitated.","line:0518433":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: It seems...the pieces we're looking for have travelled further than I anticipated. Much further, I suspect.","line:008c254":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Now go. We have more relics to uncover.","line:0cb4c0e":"The Mayor is walking quickly towards you. He seems to be in a good mood, with a spring in his step.","line:0fcc22c":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Fantastic news - thanks partly to your efforts, [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0] is growing! Our town is sure to be swarming with visitors any day now.","line:0c1e6af":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: In fact, I've granted a consent for the [C1]Shipwright to expand her facilities[/C1]. The old [C0]Dry Dock is operational again[/C0]!","line:0013478":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Keep up the good work. We're glad you've chosen to be here with us.","line:0db2070":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Lousy weather lately - almost makes you not want to get out of bed. But you and I, we've gotta do it, eh? We're what keeps people from going hungry.","line:09d709f":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I don't know how you do it every day. These old bones wouldn't cut it on the high seas.","line:04bd408":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Hope the seagulls didn't get to your catch - those blasted pests.","line:0c338fe":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Don't over-commit yourself - especially when that sun starts going down. Better to come back with a small catch than to not come back at all.","line:0ba7026":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Keep an eye out for larger fish. They'll feed more mouths, so I can pay you more for them.","line:0adc890":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Sorry, sorry, it's a mess in here. I've just been so busy lately, you know how it is. Exhausting.","line:03a939d":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: I've got a good feeling about these engines. They'll take you far away...reliable, too, provided you take care of 'em.","line:0e1da4d":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: You'll want a variety of tackle to catch all the fish out there. Make sure you're prepared for whatever you come across.","line:000fe89":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Damage to your hull is bound to stop engines and such from functioning right. Be careful near rocks.","line:035ed68":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: A single unlucky hit is enough to knock out an engine...and you wouldn't want to be without a motor when the fog rolls in.","line:06f2fdb":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: If any of your equipment stops working, head back here for repairs.","line:0ae169c":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Make sure you check out the specs before you buy this stuff -- once it's installed, no refunds.","line:0a91d49":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:01c27e6":"Do you know of any shipwrecks around here?","line:0d99dde":"Have you heard of any strange things happening?","line:0632eb4":"She eyes you suspiciously.","line:0c071f9":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: ...","line:0f79a7e":"What do you know about the Old Mayor of Little Marrow?","line:0abd290":"I should go.","line:0aa963a":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: There's a spot near the [C0]back of Greater Marrow[/C0] where the current carries in wreckage from the sea.","line:0e63aa4":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:045aa3c":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:04eeae2":"What did you want me to do again?","line:08a20e6":"Why do you want to leave?","line:0936adc":"What do you know about the area?","line:031b3ae":"I'd better get on with it.","line:06f5905":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Bring [C0]Two units of Lumber[/C0] and [C0]Two units of Scrap[/C0] to [C0]Steel Point[/C0], which is an island just to the [C0]North[/C0].","line:07b49a7":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: I want to build a place for myself there.","line:060df63":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: There are...too many painful memories here - I don't want to be living them any more. It's a bit difficult to talk about - you know how it is.","line:016db4e":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: It doesn't do you any good to dwell too deeply on the past.","line:0573001":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Greater Marrow? Well, it was once a bright and thriving little town, if you can believe it.","line:0c713f0":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: There was plenty of work for me and my crew - new houses and shops every other month. We made a fair bit of money out of it too.","line:0e4f3db":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: But-- I don't know, I guess the bubble burst or something. I don't know how these things work. People started leaving. My crew left. I stayed.","line:06d71df":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: How's the day treating ya?","line:01303dc":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: What else can I do for ya?","line:0682d30":"Do you know of any shipwrecks around here?","line:076e259":"What do you know about any strange occurrences?","line:0f4bda4":"What's it like working on the docks?","line:0592bd5":"I'd better go.","line:089de8b":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: I know there were a few 'round the Eastern side of the island. Mostly rotted away by now I'd expect. Or dashed apart by the waves.","line:0b4d396":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Poor souls keep hitting rocks in the fog, I guess. There's a blind spot back there where the lighthouse can't be seen. People get turned around.","line:001d2d7":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Supposedly, some twenty-odd years ago, a fisherman from these parts hauled up an old sealed casket from the seafloor.","line:0dd8252":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: They pried it open and took what was inside for themselves.","line:01a7d23":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: As changeable as the weather, hah! Most days it's pretty quiet. The pay's not too great, but the work's straightforward - that suits me to a tee.","line:0d57d67":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: It's good to get that fresh sea breeze without actually being on the water. No offense, but you wouldn't get me out on those seas every day.","line:098a005":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: What can I do for you?","line:08da1e6":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Now, what else can I do for you?","line:0a4c297":"Do you know of any shipwrecks around here?","line:092e887":"What do you know about any strange occurrences?","line:07822fd":"What happened to the last fisherman?","line:04b1b23":"I should get back to fishing.","line:08eef64":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Hmm? The last fisherman? Oh, he was very unreliable. He'd go out at night, come back with no fish and proceed to sleep all day.","line:0762111":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: He was also a terrible captain. I mean, really terrible. Constantly running aground on the reef - even in broad daylight! The Shipwright almost ran out of wood for repairs.","line:02acc2d":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: No, he was no good. One evening he left and never came back. So long! He shan't be missed by us.","line:0092588":"I'd like to pay off some of my debt.","line:00749b6":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Of course! How much would you like to repay?","line:077872b":"$10.00","line:0f1292c":"Never mind.","line:0ece838":"All of it.","line:0ec0603":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Fantastic!","line:0d9ee35":"$25.00","line:08df58b":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Excellent!","line:03bfc69":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Excellent!","line:0f5788b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Do not bother me with common clutter. I hear that the [C0]Trader[/C0] in [C0]Little Marrow[/C0] deals with such trivialities.","line:00898e0":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Look here, I found this down by the docks - I'm sure someone like you could make something out of it. Why don't you take it?","line:018e832":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I found this [C1]Book[/C1] out back. Could be useful to ya.","line:0f983d7":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: If you're wanting to get a bit more out of your engines, take a look through this book. On the house.","line:0096061":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: A returning customer! Please, take this as a symbol of my appreciation. I'm sure you'll find it useful.","line:08a88b1":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Until your debt is repaid, a [C2]tiny portion of your fish sales[/C2] will go towards paying it off. A small amount of interest will go towards [C1]improving the town[/C1].","line:0e45483":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Return when you have something.","line:08ec80c":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Stop by for a chat any time. I know how lonely it can be.","line:0a08e45":"Give the belt buckle to the man?","line:0931b46":"Yes","line:0b76735":"No","line:0849ca9":"You hold on to the belt buckle for now.","line:08eda34":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Please, take this. I've not any money to pay you, but this might hold some value to you.","line:024b4c6":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: This is the Dry Dock. We can make [C1]significant improvements[/C1] to your vessel here.","line:0b69cb9":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: We're talking [C1]extra space[/C1], [C1]more attachment points for equipment[/C1], and even [C1]superior hulls[/C1].","line:0883b57":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: We'll need a decent stock of hard materials for these projects - [C0]Lumber[/C0], [C0]Metal Scraps[/C0], that sort of thing.","line:0a5f381":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: [C0]Materials assigned towards upgrades here will be stored[/C0]. So don't worry if you only have half of what we need.","line:0c06f23":"How do I get materials?","line:0dc4b7c":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: There's plenty of decent materials around the coast, from various shipwrecks and the like. I'm sure you'll find a way to get at them.","line:0efdf56":"Finding materials will allow you to upgrade my vessel, got it.","line:0fce1fc":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Say...where's your fishing gear? Sure hope you have enough money to buy some replacement tackle.","line:099abde":"Actually, I don't. Could you lend me a rod?","line:01caf7a":"I'll be fine.","line:09835cf":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Hmm. That's a worry. I might have something out back...","line:0fb1a45":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Ah, here we go. Don't worry about giving it back, it's a piece of junk really.","line:07cab72":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Just don't tell the Mayor I gave you something for nothing. He'll lecture me about taxes for an hour.","line:089a3f3":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: If you say so.","line:0170bba":"The lighthouse towers above. Waves crash endlessly against the perilous rocks below.","line:0c503a1":"All creatures - human or otherwise - would have their brittle bodies broken and thrown at its feet.","line:0a7b92f":"You ponder the intrinsic power of this structure, a vast column of stone shouldering the responsibility of countless lives.","line:04e9bde":"How long will it stand? How long until it decays into ruin, its purpose exhausted?","line:06b5a6a":"The lighthouse towers above.","line:0e786ae":"A floating buoy. It serves to mark safe passage past dangerous rocks and obscured hazards.","line:0e0db48":"Its dim light also provides a [C1]brief respite[/C1] in the gloom of the night.","line:0ac9735":"From this position in the center of the bay, you can see a spread of islands.","line:0ef0d77":"Greater Marrow to the West, and its twinned town of Little Marrow to the East.","line:06b622e":"The islands to the North and South are...unfamilar, but are probably marked on your map.","line:0da08cf":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:03edfa3":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:07036e5":"Do you need help with anything?","line:0d204b6":"Here's the aged Conger Eel you asked for.","line:0be893c":"What can you tell me about the cliffs?","line:035f07c":"Do you know of any odd characters around these parts?","line:06b5224":"Where can I sell my fish here?","line:045f20e":"Nothing.","line:0cf3be9":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Many years ago, the cliffs used to be a haven for smugglers and pirates. Legend tells of two pirate lords who used Gale Cliffs as their hideout.","line:0c31ee0":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Supposedly, they got into some disagreement, and a huge battle was fought around the [C0]South[/C0] side of the cliffs. There certainly are a large number of wrecks in that area.","line:029931f":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Both sides were completely destroyed - their [C1]treasure hoards[/C1] left abandoned and unclaimed to this day. I dare say they'd be worth a lot, if anyone knew where to find them...","line:00f2c0e":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: We catch our fish ourselves here, so we don't have much need for buying any.","line:0f52fbf":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: But there's a merchant that travels around, she's usually anchored [C0]across the bay[/C0]. She [C0]buys and sells[/C0] almost anything - and she does [C0]repairs[/C0] too.","line:07cdf27":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: I've been trying to prepare a special meal for my partner, but I've been having some issues.","line:07d7780":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Around here we consider [C2]aged[/C2] [C0]Conger Eels[/C0] to be a particular delicacy. You may say they're '[C2]rotting[/C2]', but they're delicious if prepared correctly.","line:0f43446":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Normally, we bury them in the ground and allow them to mature. But our dog keeps digging them up and eating them.","line:043f835":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: I can't raise the subject without spoiling the surprise. Can you bring me an [C2]aged[/C2] [C0]Conger Eel[/C0]?","line:0852bba":"Yes, I can bring you an 'aged' Conger Eel.","line:07dae27":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Thank you. You'll be decently compensated.","line:0ce33ab":"I'm busy, maybe later.","line:0b4bf9e":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Oh, ok.","line:05f94ab":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: I still need that [C2]aged[/C2] [C0]Conger Eel[/C0], if you would be so kind.","line:0f2920f":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Perfect! This will do wonderfully. I can offer you a small sum, in thanks.","line:0da8539":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Safe travels.","line:08d4468":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: I'm saved! Saved! Oh, you are a sight for these sore eyes.","line:01e1784":"What happened?","line:005f20a":"You look terrible. Are you ok?","line:082862c":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: I bet I do! I've certainly felt better. I've been chewing on seaweed and starfish for longer than I'd like.","line:0d8f80b":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: I washed up here...oh, it must be some two weeks ago now. We were in rough seas, and when a wave hit us broadside I was jostled overboard and swept away.","line:08f65de":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: I thought my crew would've come to find me by now, but yours is the first ship I've seen pass by here.","line:0ef0411":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: Did the boys send you looking for me?","line:04ca29e":"No.","line:0392942":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: Oh, well, I'm sure they're out there lookin' anyways.","line:070a0da":"Yes.","line:0849368":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: That's a relief to hear, I'd thought for sure those sorry sacks would be halfway across the sea with my boat by now.","line:0dd2df4":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: Can you get me to [C0]Little Marrow[/C0], stranger? I should be able to catch them there when they next stop by.","line:0560a5f":"Yes, I'll take you to Little Marrow.","line:0cf7c07":"Not right now.","line:01f6200":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: What, you're just going to leave me here to starve to death?! Curse you!","line:0624595":"The [C0]Castaway[/C0] climbs aboard.","line:06c5651":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: Have you come back for me?","line:0fc383f":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: The sweet, rank smell of civilization. I thought I could never miss it.","line:0518c15":"He turns to you. For someone who has just been saved, he seems gloomy.","line:02f9118":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: I've not got much on me, as you can imagine. And I've a feeling this isn't worth much anymore -- for me, at least. But perhaps it'll be worth something for you.","line:0d888a0":"He removes a [C1]Signet Ring[/C1] from his left hand and presses it into yours. It's emblazoned with a symbol of a captain's wheel.","line:03910de":"CASTAWAY_NAME_KEY: On to better horizons, friend. Farewell.","line:0d5dfe0":"On the shoreline, partially submerged in a rockpool, is the body of a man. The sun and sea have corrupted his features - it's hard to make out much more than that.","line:04625cc":"With a grim reverence, you turn the wheel and continue on your way.","line:0a7ed89":"You approach a hooded figure. Swathed in dark blue robes, their face is barely visible.","line:0eeafb4":"HOODED_FIGURE_1_NAME_KEY: Fisherman...please. Help.","line:03609d9":"Something seems off. The hooded figure is slumped, long robes billowing violently.","line:0f63614":"A short man is shouting orders at a handful of workers disembarking from a boat nearby. The man notices you.","line:002342a":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I'll let you get out there to [C0]catch some fish[/C0]. See if you can fill your cargo while you get your bearings in the light.","line:08e9ed4":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: As I mentioned earlier, your [C2]old boat was too badly damaged to be repaired[/C2]. However, I'm more than happy to sell you that replacement vessel - [C1]yours to own[/C1].","line:0dcc380":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Ahoy there! You're a new face - a fisherman I take it? Perfect! Well, we should get along like a house on fire, ha ha!","line:072f306":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I'm a traveller and a merchant, all rolled into one! If you have any [C0]fish to sell[/C0], I'll take 'em on board and sell 'em at the next town I come across.","line:0401373":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Likewise, I haul a small cargo of [C0]equipment[/C0] between places. You're welcome to peruse the stock and see if there's anything that takes your fancy.","line:0ee47b3":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Come and see me when you're ready to trade!","line:0026f3c":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Are you able to make that delivery for me now?","line:0c4a147":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: The [C0]Dockworker[/C0] will pay you upon delivery. Please be quick about it, [C2]I don't want it to spoil[/C2].","line:0f9c277":"He tears a small hole in the paper and peeks inside. You can't say for sure, but it feels as though he's shielding it from your view.","line:0547c1c":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Yeah, nice and fresh. This'll do nicely. I'm to pay you, I suppose?","line:0ccdc1e":"He hands you some money.","line:0565b4b":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Ugh, this smells foul. You obviously took your sweet time getting here with this.","line:057d358":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: He won't let me pay for a delivery in this state. But, hmm. Maybe I can give you this...","line:0e0c2bb":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Shipwrecks? Unfortunately, there have been quite a few in recent years. The lighthouse helps, but even it struggles to cut through the fog some nights.","line:090f7cd":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: We do our best to salvage and clear any shipwrecks that occur around this side of the island. That should make fishing a bit easier for you!","line:01d8bad":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Well, I heard that my counterpart in Little Marrow met the most unfortunate end.","line:00fd6d5":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: They say he went mad quite suddenly! One day he was normal, the next, he was pacing the shoreline hurling people's belongings into the sea!","line:050d110":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: After some days like this, he disappeared, never to be seen again! Nowadays, \"The Tale of the Old Mayor\" is used to scare children.","line:07f04a2":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Not many remember him, myself included. And those that do remember don't seem to like talking about it. A most unpleasant subject!","line:02cc5df":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: So if you're looking for what I think you're looking for, it's best you just move on.","line:080ca18":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: I see plenty of strange things from atop the lighthouse. Sometimes I don't know whether or not I can trust my own eyes.","line:042cc5d":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Are you really standing here in front of me? Or is this just another of the fog's tricks?","line:009b10d":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: That's...he's...I try not to think about him. It's a painful memory for us all.","line:07d3e12":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: But I know he's gone - and I don't want to talk about it any more.","line:0dce012":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: In that case, allow me to aid your travels.","line:08a946a":"He turns a few pages in his book and mutters something low under his breath.","line:0dbcf44":"He runs his fingers firmly along the length of the fish, as though feeling for something. He pushes from one side of its stomach and a small shape can be seen against the bulging scales.","line:028f13e":"He slices the fish open. From its stomach he pulls a small piece of fabric and spreads it on the counter. It's a [C3]delicately patterned Handkerchief[/C3].","line:031b545":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Well, I've never seen that before in all my days. I'll give you this thing, and I'll pay you for the fish too, of course.","line:0f1f30b":"A man is looking at you through your cabin window. His face is mostly in shadow.","line:03d2dee":"COLLECTOR_UNKNOWN_DOCK_NAME_KEY: I know what you took to the Fishmonger.","line:06440fc":"COLLECTOR_UNKNOWN_DOCK_NAME_KEY: And I'll be clear - I know he extracted an artifact from it. I need to inspect it. But not here.","line:09e511f":"COLLECTOR_UNKNOWN_DOCK_NAME_KEY: Meet me on [C3]Blackstone Isle[/C3]. Head out of this bay and cut [C1]South[/C1]. I have a business proposition that you'll want to hear.","line:006a952":"COLLECTOR_UNKNOWN_DOCK_NAME_KEY: I'll be waiting.","line:048a80c":"The man is standing in a doorway, watching you approach. He's holding an old book in one hand. It's bound in crimson, with silver ribbons.","line:0e4568a":"COLLECTOR_UNKNOWN_HOUSE_NAME_KEY: You came. Good. Allow me to introduce myself.","line:0fc8b29":"COLLECTOR_UNKNOWN_HOUSE_NAME_KEY: I am a collector - of many things; art and artifacts, treasures and truths...and curios that occupy the periphery of desire.","line:05317d8":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: And you have something for me.","line:0137e0a":"You give the [C3]Handkerchief[/C3] to the Collector. He holds it up to the flickering light and studies it.","line:082d5a8":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: These patterns are...unmistakeable...even after all this time. This [C3]Handkerchief[/C3] comes from an old ship I've been searching for. It sank many years ago.","line:03ae562":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: It carried items of great importance. As you can imagine, retrieving them is proving to be challenging. That's where you come in.","line:0cc3882":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: My proposition is this: I will outfit your vessel with equipment that will let you [C3]dredge the wrecks and dark depths[/C3].","line:037d16d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Find me these [C3]lost relics[/C3] and I will [C1]reward you in ways beyond all imagining[/C1].","line:0d26a1c":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: You need not give up your fishing career. I'll merely need a few hours with your vessel to make the necessary alterations. What do you say?","line:0ec0aec":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: That very night, the fog rolled in for the first time - and it has cloaked the seas every night since.","line:036ce09":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: What was in that accursed casket nobody knows. All of the crew that laid eyes on its contents went mad - or worse.","line:0cd230c":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: The casket and crew have since disappeared without a trace. But the fog remains. Crazy stuff, huh?","line:095fc25":"You don't have the [C3]Handkerchief[/C3] with you. The man seemed interested in it, so you should probably bring it to the meeting.","line:0ef2fca":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: I overheard a tale in the tavern some years ago. Sounded pretty strange to me.","line:0143e52":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Hello. Is everything ok?","line:076268d":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Anything else I can help you with?","line:0707a84":"About that belt buckle...","line:0530c5c":"Do you know of any shipwrecks around here?","line:062e9db":"What do you know about any strange occurrences?","line:05168c3":"I'd better go.","line:0e90930":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: I've told you all I know.","line:0b8dc37":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Well, yes, you see...my only son was lost at sea some years ago.","line:088210f":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: He's...still out there, somewhere. In one of those wrecks. All alone in the cold dark water.","line:0de1792":"The man is clearly trying his hardest to remain composed, but tremors of grief rack his body.","line:0d1bccd":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: I was wondering...I notice you have some dredging equipment installed on your vessel...","line:01b1bf3":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: If you're able to retrieve any of his belongings from the wreck...I think he'd feel more at peace if his mementos were with me.","line:073bf7f":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: He wore a [C0]Bronze Belt Buckle[/C0], specially engraved. I'd recognize it anywhere. If there's a chance you could find it, I'd be in your debt.","line:021cdb1":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: I don't get out a lot anymore, so I don't see much of what goes on.","line:0f854de":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: But I do remember the Old Mayor in his final days. What an awful sight it was.","line:05484bb":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Screaming and throwing things into the sea. \"[C3]Throw it back,[/C3]\" he would cry, over and over.","line:020309f":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Begging anyone who would listen. Howling it to the wind. These days, I almost feel like I understand.","line:0f11b81":"You explain that you found the belt buckle, but lost it again.","line:02b72fa":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: You - oh. Well...perhaps that's his way of saying he wishes to remain at sea.","line:0abd1a5":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Thank you for your efforts. Truly.","line:0426e64":"You explain that you found a belt buckle, but it's currently in your storage.","line:0f62901":"GRIEVING_FATHER_NAME_KEY: Please, bring it to me. I need to know if it's his.","line:04ee758":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I'll still buy fish that aren't totally fresh, but if it's completely turned to [C2]Rot[/C2] I can't pay you anything for it.","line:01ee056":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Hey again - come by for a chat?","line:07fcf8b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Is there anything else you want to talk about?","line:0dbf2f7":"Are you always out on the water?","line:0fe5e2a":"Do you ever see strange things out at sea?","line:062a334":"I'll be going now.","line:0825034":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Yeah, always! I like to keep moving along. The merchanting is secondary to the travelling, really. I'm more of a merchanting traveller!","line:027ee43":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I get to see a lot of places, which is nice. I also get to meet a lot of people, which is only sometimes nice.","line:04f77b2":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Strange things? Plenty! But I try not to dwell on them. You could go crazy, you know? Hah!","line:0818a2c":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: But, hey, if you're seeing strange things...maybe you're not seeing them the right way? Maybe they're not so strange after all.","line:0120780":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Or perhaps they are, and they're incredibly dangerous. Better not risk it!","line:0a5959e":"She holds the lantern up so that it shines brightly onto your face.","line:0461c24":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Some nights I still think I can hear the hum of his engines sailing past the bay...","line:0dc55db":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I've had a special order come through from a customer. If you can fulfil it, I'll pay you above normal prices.","line:0632ae2":"Tell me about the order.","line:0861169":"Maybe later - I'm just here on regular business.","line:077f1ad":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: They asked for [C0]one Gulf Flounder[/C0] and [C0]one Grey Eel[/C0]. Just bring 'em in when you have them.","line:0e70ef3":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: You'll need to have a rod that can handle [C0]Shallow[/C0] water fish in order to catch those. The shipwright should be able to sort that for you.","line:07dfad5":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Have you got any fish for that order?","line:0e83f73":"Yes.","line:0b0b665":"Not right now.","line:0ae71d1":"The Fishmonger wraps up the fish and hands you some money.","line:09bdaab":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Good, good. They should be pleased with these.","line:03c0571":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I've got another order here. This one's a little more curious. They want [C0]a couple of Squid[/C0] and [C0]a whole Black Grouper[/C0].","line:022606e":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Don't see many people fishing squid these days - [C0]they only feed at night[/C0], and well, you know what nights are like 'round here. Good luck.","line:01b0176":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Have you got any fish for that order?","line:0445fe3":"Yes.","line:0d1d3af":"Not right now.","line:09b0da1":"The Fishmonger wraps up the fish and hands you some money.","line:0667f0f":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I didn't think you had it in you; night fishing is a tall order.","line:0640414":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Been meaning to talk to you about a new business venture I've been considering - [C0]Crab Pots[/C0].","line:00bbaa0":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Should be pretty straightforward. Just [C0]drop it out at sea anywhere[/C0], then come back after a day or two to check on it.","line:047905b":"The Fishmonger wraps up the crabs and hands you some money.","line:0002356":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: These'll do. Glad you got some use out of that old pot. You can always [C0]buy more here[/C0], or [C1]repair damaged ones at the Shipyard[/C1].","line:05a1464":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I have one final request for you. As you've seen, some fish around here can develop odd...[C3]deformities[/C3].","line:0d1203e":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: What do you think happens to a person that eats the flesh of one of these mutants?","line:0fdeff7":"Nothing.","line:0654b01":"They go mad.","line:09c2a9b":"They get sick.","line:08ba9e0":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Well...perhaps. But I want to know for sure. Bring me a mutant fish - any will do. Just...keep this between the two of us.","line:08b1e1d":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Have you got any of those mutants with you now?","line:0084f55":"Yes.","line:060c074":"Not right now.","line:075cd99":"The Fishmonger takes the aberrated fish from you. He clutches it close to his chest, wringing his hands around its slimy body.","line:0b4d8b2":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Yes...this should do nicely. Here's what the fish is worth. And why don't you take these too - they're of no use to me.","line:0138701":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Hmm? Do you hear that? It sounds like...the [C3]faintest whispering[/C3]...","line:061b09a":"You listen.","line:069a725":"Silence.","line:048145e":"In the stillness of the room, the Fishmonger's hands begin to tremble.","line:0965cf2":"His face grows anguished.","line:0c57485":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Please. Sell what you need, then leave. I must deal with this creature. Quickly now!","line:0bbaf15":"The Fishmonger's door slams behind you. You hear the heavy scraping of a metal bar sliding across it.","line:0f1a6f7":"The Fishmonger's door is barred from the inside.","line:08ae5c9":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Ugh...blinding headache today. Did you come by yesterday? I don't recall... Anyway, what can I do for you?","line:073b8c4":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Alright.","line:05a2bb2":"You hold on to the fish for now.","line:0d92e28":"You hold on to the fish for now.","line:09d1b28":"You hold onto the aberration for now.","line:0b915f0":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Have you heard the tale of Magran? He was an old whaler from these parts.","line:0a49f18":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: As the whales got more scarce, the crews spent longer and longer at sea trying to find them. Magran, it seems, wasn't cut out for this.","line:042fed1":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: He formed an...unnatural attachment to a scroll he found on one of these trips.","line:054405c":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: He says the scroll told him how to become immortal by eating mutated fish. People started calling him \"[C0]Magran The Fishman[/C0]\".","line:0ab9dcb":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: One day, the town awoke to find all the boats' nets and lines had been slashed in the night. And old Magran was nowhere to be found - nor has he been seen since.","line:0c0b77a":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Hello again...what can I do for you?","line:0f0133f":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: What else do you want to know?","line:0d15aea":"This place doesn't seem safe. Why do you live here?","line:042754f":"Your brother forgives you. He's found you a place to stay.","line:0e651c9":"Do you know of any shipwrecks around here?","line:038f294":"What's happening to these cliffs?","line:01a24d3":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Someone that used to live here kept their ship moored at the base of the cliff...until it was struck by some falling rocks and sunk to the bottom.","line:064cad9":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: They were devastated at the loss - we all were - it was a beautiful boat, decorated with all manner of memorabilia from their travels.","line:04e1c7b":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: At low tide, I can still see what's left of the masthead, poking through the waves.","line:09af0c7":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: They're being consumed from the core by that [C3]hateful serpent[/C3] - have you seen it?","line:048b969":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Nobody believed me. Not until it started devouring our foundations, opening up chasms beneath our homes.","line:0c62b39":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: It was nightmarish - waking in the night to the sound of a creature slithering somewhere underneath.","line:0751497":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: It seems to have turned its attention elsewhere...but not before it took everything from me.","line:090068f":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Aye...I've been stubbornly holding out here for quite some time. Truth be told, I've been reconsidering my position lately.","line:0d7aea1":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: I have been happy here for so long. My wife and I had such a beautiful life. Until the collapse.","line:06fe7c4":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Now I'm alone, and cut off by land and sea - left only with these trembling rocks on all sides.","line:09e6e8a":"I could help you move to Ingfell.","line:038ef4b":"I'm sorry to hear that.","line:01808e6":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Hmmph.","line:023d198":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Right. Well. I'm packed, and ready to go.","line:019dde8":"The Hermit climbs aboard with all of his belongings.","line:028ec73":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Not enough space for me and my things? I can wait for you to make some room.","line:017067a":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:0bc764c":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:06eb052":"Where did you say the explosives were?","line:01ca68b":"Are there any shipwrecks around here?","line:05dc22b":"Have you heard about any strange things in the area?","line:0013088":"What can you tell me about Ingfell?","line:052647e":"Nothing. See you.","line:09e3444":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: The real wreck around here is the settlement at Gale Cliffs.","line:063c7df":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Some time ago, just after the last whale was brought in, there was a sudden exodus from Gale Cliffs.","line:0dd3733":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Dozens of ships sailed past, packed up and hurrying away north as fast they could.","line:0037673":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: They were waving and shouting something at us from their boats - but we couldn't make it out.","line:0bc4582":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Never did see or hear of them since.","line:03b9563":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Ingfell used to be a whaling town - emphasis on the \"used to be\". We would go out, bring in a carcass and then the rest of the town would get to work.","line:0e24095":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: But the whales got scarce some twenty years ago - and now look at us. Barely scraping by for a new candle.","line:006308e":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: See, I've been trying to [C0]clear some debris[/C0] in the pathways through the cliffs [C1]to make a shortcut[/C1]. With explosives.","line:00a0f85":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: I was able to set a charge, but the cliffs seemed particularly unsteady that day, so I didn't risk detonating it.","line:03c3775":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: You just need to get in there and set it off. It's not far in - I left some yellow flags nearby, you can't miss it.","line:0d28075":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Head through the rock arch to the [C0]South-East[/C0]. Follow the channel, and you'll see the yellow flags on the right.","line:08b1775":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: You've done it - we heard the blast from here! Gods, the echo. I'm surprised the cliffs didn't come down on your head.","line:0ad8952":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: I've got things ready here. [C0]Go and tell my brother[/C0]...that he can come home.","line:04b10c2":"Nothing, I'll be off now.","line:03abf79":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Come for some more [C0]Packed Explosives[/C0]?","line:03e9ea1":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Come by the old [C0]Whaling Yards[/C0] anytime.","line:0d54fb9":"Do you need help with anything?","line:0a9bfb7":"About those rare fish you wanted me to find...","line:081782b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Assistance from an angler? Absolutely! I've been trying to collect records of where each species of fish is located.","line:0a967c3":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I've figured out most of them on my travels so far, but there are a few I haven't been able to track down. Reckon you could share your info with me?","line:08c7166":"Sure, I can help with that.","line:0906954":"Not right now.","line:0f59283":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I know a little about each species already, so maybe I can point you in the right direction.","line:098d7e5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: What did you want to know?","line:087abaa":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: What about the other fish?","line:06fed02":"Tell me about Oarfish.","line:063cbc5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Given that the [C0]Oarfish[/C0] has a long and fragile body, I suspect they'll live in reasonably deep, but calm water. Maybe the shelter of [C0]Gale Cliffs[/C0] would suit them?","line:0bfe470":"I found an Oarfish.","line:010d4e7":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's great news! I'll add it to my records. Here, take this - I'm sure you'll find some use for it.","line:09b8ff6":"Tell me about Gulper Eels.","line:0a74aa9":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I know that [C0]Gulper Eels[/C0] live at the [C0]deepest depths imaginable[/C0]. You'll have to get some specialist gear to catch one of those.","line:0b104b3":"I found a Gulper Eel.","line:0485590":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's great news! I'll add it to my records. Here, take this - I'm sure you'll find some use for it.","line:0b2950c":"Tell me about Goliath Tigerfish.","line:06eb287":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: These guys are legitimately scary! They hunt in [C0]murky, swampy waters[/C0], using the shade of trees as cover.","line:0681373":"I found a Goliath Tigerfish.","line:0d861cc":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's great news! I'll add it to my records. Here, take this - I'm sure you'll find some use for it.","line:0f8e20c":"Tell me about Coelacanths.","line:07546be":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Actually, I have no idea where [C0]Coelacanths[/C0] might be. But they have a [C0]primordial feel[/C0] to them, don't you think?","line:0deadb9":"I found a Coelacanth.","line:02002f9":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's great news! I'll add it to my records. Here, take this - I'm sure you'll find some use for it.","line:056ba33":"I've got all the information I need.","line:024d26d":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's...that's all of them, wow! I never thought I'd complete these records.","line:0fd5091":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Great! The fish I have left to track down are: [C0]Oarfish[/C0], [C0]Gulper Eel[/C0], [C0]Goliath Tigerfish[/C0] and [C0]Coelacanth[/C0].","line:0704164":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: So you've returned. I wasn't sure you were coming back.","line:03e8fb7":"You drag the massive music box into the room, gouging the wooden floorboards beneath it. The Collector doesn't seem to mind. He's focused on the box.","line:0bf1799":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: You found this at the cliffs, didn't you?","line:04a19ca":"Yes.","line:044502c":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Ah, excellent.","line:04ef5e3":"I don't remember.","line:04e1568":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Curious.","line:07b5561":"It doesn't matter.","line:0bdcd08":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Now, there are yet more relics to find. Keep looking.","line:0f8cad8":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: This should make future return journeys a little more swift. Allow me.","line:07ca7d0":"He selects one of the silver ribbons trailing from the crimson-bound book, opening it to some unseen page.","line:02e08ad":"Turning to catch the dim light, he whispers the words on the page.","line:0a5d847":"After a few seconds, you feel your stomach drop suddenly, as though thrown high by a wave. He closes the book and turns his attention back to you.","line:0fca282":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: And with that, our collection is complete...I must admit, I am surprised. I did not think you had the determination for such a job.","line:09ffc0b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:0e4cba4":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:00810e5":"Where should I look for relics?","line:01b8bc2":"Take a look at these trinkets.","line:016a8ec":"Nothing, I'll be going.","line:01337ff":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: [C0]You should ask around the towns in The Marrows[/C0]. Somebody is sure to know something.","line:0f55fb7":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: My...intuition tells me that the current may have carried some debris to the [C0]South-East[/C0], towards [C0]Gale Cliffs[/C0]. Make that your priority.","line:017f97c":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The reef at [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0] may have caught and accumulated some wreckage. Search around that area.","line:08019ba":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I can imagine all manner of detritus swallowed by the silty muck of [C0]Twisted Strand's[/C0] channels. It's worth investigating.","line:0cf7b18":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I loathe to suggest it, but the abyssal plain on the approach to [C0]Devil's Spine[/C0] is a likely candidate. See what you can find.","line:0bf8798":"A burst of light fills your vision, and you stagger back briefly.","line:034f255":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: He approaches! Drawing closer with...an incessant ticking. You have the pocket watch.","line:0e0776f":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The relics we're looking for are: a [C3]ring[/C3], a [C3]necklace[/C3], a [C3]watch[/C3], and a [C3]music box[/C3] and [C3]key[/C3].","line:018de25":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I'll mark a location on your [C0]Map[/C0] where you can begin your search.","line:0c3bf02":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I've already marked a location on your [C0]Map[/C0] where you can begin your search.","line:0783cf4":"Where can I catch a Conger Eel?","line:02b92d0":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Ah yes, they can be tricky to find. I'm told they [C0]inhabit the holes and burrows within the cliffs[/C0] themselves.","line:0d44481":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: I imagine they've been fished out around the edges, so [C0]you may have to venture into the passageways of the cliffs to find them[/C0].","line:04c7ae8":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Oh, and did I mention that [C0]they only come out at night[/C0]? Yes, I believe they hide during the day.","line:0dac675":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Good luck.","line:07603bf":"Is this your family crest?","line:0588380":"What am I supposed to be doing?","line:0411a53":"What am I supposed to be doing?","line:0198dc2":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: It's not that simple. My brother would never...you see, I used to live in Ingfell with my brother. He was a Whaler, back in the day.","line:055d18f":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Things were bad. We fought a lot. Mostly about how our parents' inheritance should be divided. We were in the prime foolishness of our youth.","line:0c27317":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: When my wife and I decided to move here, I took the [C0]Family Crest[/C0]. I stole it from him. Now, after all this time...I can't return without it.","line:0f0af60":"Where is it?","line:0009687":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: That's where the problem lies.","line:009596f":"Why don't you give it back to him then?","line:0cbd08a":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Again. It's not as simple as that.","line:0983343":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: After the collapse...that creature...it dragged debris from the houses down into its wretched burrows. [C2]The crest went down with it[/C2].","line:0fa5889":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: It's a lost cause, I know. But if you were to find it...it's a large, whale-bone crest. It would mean the world to me.","line:0509488":"I'll look for it.","line:069605d":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Thank you. But please - be careful.","line:0133ff3":"Don't get your hopes up.","line:0e23ff2":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Oh, I won't.","line:043d83a":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: You've found it! I never thought I'd see this beauty again.","line:0412f23":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: But now...I have a further favor to ask. Would you take this to my brother at Ingfell?","line:0c51a07":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Tell him...tell him his brother is sorry, and would like to come home.","line:0ec3b00":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: You were going to keep an eye out for my [C0]Family Crest[/C0]. It was dragged into the tunnels by that creature.","line:0f26ed3":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: You were going to take the [C0]Family Crest[/C0] to my brother at Ingfell and ask if he'll forgive me.","line:0ef2edb":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: He does? That's...a huge weight off my chest. One so old I hardly remembered it was there.","line:07ca451":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Well, here we are-","line:0927bcb":"The Hermit notices the old Whaler standing on the dock, waiting for him.","line:0424c57":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Little brother. You're home.","line:01676c7":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: I - I'm so sorry. I was so foolish.","line:0ce4c8d":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: We both were. Come on inside. Let me get your bags.","line:0171d7f":"The two brothers walk away down the dock. One of them pauses for a moment and turns back to you.","line:0a561f0":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: My brother ditched us and moved on over to those cliffs, years ago. I suspect he's regretting his decision now, the devil.","line:066f0a2":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Gods...I haven't seen this since...hmmph. So he did take it. I knew it.","line:0866cfb":"Your brother's sorry. Will you let him come home?","line:0c9d80d":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Hmm. I don't know if...I was in a right state when he left.","line:03bec92":"He's in real trouble over there. Your brother needs to move back here.","line:04885b5":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: I bet he is. Maybe I can clear the...hmm.","line:04be174":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Ok. Fine. He can stay in my old workshop, at least for the time being. But I'll need some time to clear it out.","line:01326cc":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: While I'm doing that, perhaps you can do something for me.","line:0730185":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Oh, stranger. If you find any more debris that needs clearing...I'm working on making some more [C0]Packed Explosives[/C0].","line:083c5f2":"I believe this crest is yours.","line:04f0a89":"The old Whaler is waiting for you by the docks.","line:0a42566":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: There's something I forgot to mention last time we spoke.","line:09c21f7":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: If you find any more debris that needs clearing...I've got more [C0]Packed Explosives[/C0] out the back.","line:0f29381":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Come by the old [C0]Whaling Yards[/C0] if you need it.","line:00e5f8a":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Oh, and any news from my brother? Don't tell me he's hiding below deck. I'm not still mad at him - I promise!","line:0bac22d":"I'm so sorry. He was lost overboard.","line:009ebb5":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Wh- what? No...how could...","line:00bbe9b":"He stands in silence for quite some time.","line:06f5f50":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: At least...at least the crest is home. He always loved that thing.","line:0db8269":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: When he was a kid, he'd take it off the wall and just look at it. Dad gave him a belting every time.","line:0c4adb7":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: I was never mad that he took it. I was just upset that he left. And I...I should've made more of an effort to fix things.","line:093500b":"He decided to stay on the cliffs.","line:0b6c70c":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Oh. Well...let him know that he's always welcome to change his mind. I'll keep the room made up for him.","line:06fcb6c":"He wanted to move elsewhere.","line:023f2cb":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Oh. Well...I'm glad he moved on, at least. I understand him not wanting to come back here. Too many memories, and all that.","line:077966b":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Thanks for what you've done, all the same. It was...some form of help, in the end.","line:0af80d3":"He walks away down the dock, crestfallen.","line:012a8c3":"A pile of loose debris. It could be cleared to make a shortcut.","line:0d308cb":"\\[Use explosives.\\]","line:042adca":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0357ab5":"A pile of loose debris. Clearing this would take some strong explosives.","line:0c94f2b":"You set the charge and light the fuse...","line:00ae9ed":"The debris crumbles away.","line:00cb116":"A pile of loose debris. In the gaps between the rocks you can see what appear to be large, white teeth.","line:0f31f6e":"There's a long fuse trailing out from the side. This must be the location the Whaler wants cleared for a shortcut. Light the fuse?","line:09cfc49":"Yes.","line:07feee6":"Not right now.","line:09f3253":"You light the fuse...","line:0e9e72b":"The debris crumbles away. You should let the Whaler know.","line:0cba959":"You stand in the center of a campsite. The fire's embers are cool, but ash is still steadily blowing out with the wind.","line:0c44e57":"What do you want to do?","line:005fbb2":"\\[Take a closer look at the campfire.\\]","line:00ea27b":"\\[Look for footprints.\\]","line:0e9a12b":"\\[Check the makeshift tent.\\]","line:065cd6f":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0f9b64f":"A large flat rock sits atop the charred wood of the campfire. A handful of tiny fish bones can be seen poking out of the ashes.","line:05cd306":"You find no footprints, but unfamiliar symbols have been sketched in the dust nearby. Some have been erased with the hasty sweep of a foot.","line:050b495":"The tent is a sheet of cloth suspended over some sticks. There is nothing inside, save for a smoothed hollow in the dirt where someone slept.","line:0db0557":"Is this it?","line:02b43b3":"I've come to pick you up.","line:0cc55db":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: You sure you don't need it? Well, come back if you change your mind.","line:03c6ebd":"I accept.","line:03c483b":"Let me think about it.","line:0b7a5f6":"A slab of rock juts from the water, bearing crude symbols of [C0]curved fish[/C0]. At its base, a rough shape has been chiselled away.","line:064d4b5":"A wave washes over the fish, sweeping them away. When the water recedes, you notice something has lodged against the rock.","line:017451b":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh, hello again. What do you need?","line:0f43597":"About those specimens you're after...","line:0a6c061":"About those specimens you're after...","line:0b64d4b":"I have those Prototype Parts you asked for.","line:05f3a0b":"I need a Sampling Device.","line:0f57c75":"I can take that Repulsion Machine now.","line:0d24ad7":"Tell me about yourself.","line:0b56d67":"What sort of creature attacked you?","line:037527c":"Have you noticed anything else unusual since you arrived?","line:0fd1bfb":"Nothing, I'll be going now.","line:033d870":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Is there anything else?","line:098f67c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh, um, hello - I wasn't expecting visitors. Who are you?","line:00302df":"I'm a fisherman.","line:064eee4":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Ah yes, I thought you had the look. But a fisherman all the way out here? Strange.","line:0a99e82":"I'm a sightseer.","line:0d8c3cc":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: A sightseer - and a fisherman, I presume? I noted the fishing vessel as you docked.","line:0a4c5c3":"I'm nobody.","line:028dc08":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I struggle to believe that! Your ship looks like a fisherman's, and you - you look as though...","line:0a34c39":"She looks you up and down, and her voice cracks. She trails off.","line:0ea4697":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Well, it's a pleasure to meet you, all the same. I've not seen another soul in months. In fact, I could do with your help, if you had the time...","line:04d8375":"What do you need help with?","line:06ebe4c":"I need to get going.","line:006adab":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I need help collecting samples to study. I was originally posted at the [C0]Research Outpost[/C0] on the interior of the basin. But it was [C2]attacked[/C2].","line:004de1f":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: A [C0]large creature[/C0] emerged from the depths and destroyed the outpost. Now it rests in the center of the basin.","line:0328dda":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I fled here and have been making do as best I can. But I had to leave most of my equipment behind, so now my research has come to a halt.","line:07c603c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Take a look at the list of specimens I need - please drop them off here. You might need to [C0]experiment with different fishing strategies[/C0] to collect all of them.","line:0df8fe8":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Very well then...","line:0c60db4":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Ah, you're back. Did you have time to discuss that matter?","line:07d6942":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Thank you, looks like you've caught all of the surface specimens I need.","line:0407e5b":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: But ah, yes, I do also need some from...deeper down. But that's going to be a problem.","line:030a097":"Why is that a problem?","line:082dfa8":"I don't have the equipment to catch anything deeper anyway.","line:0d9ad9d":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I developed a device to retrieve samples from the [C0]Abyssal[/C0] zone. This was over in the other [C0]Research Outpost[C0]. Before the attack.","line:02c720f":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I have an idea of how to keep the creature at bay long enough to collect these samples. But while I work on that, I need you to retrieve some [C0]Prototype Parts[/C0].","line:029479a":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Carefully. I suggest you go during the day. I wouldn't want to be out on the reef at night.","line:04d1d3f":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Excellent. Let me assemble a device for you...","line:06308c8":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: [C1]This should allow you to catch specimens from much greater depths[C1]. It's a little slow, but [C0]you may be able to make some improvements[/C0].","line:0288e47":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh, no room on board? You can come by for it later.","line:00e1931":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Now, I've developed a [C0]Repulsion Machine[/C0] that produces a bright light and emits a high pitched noise -- [C0]it should deter the creature from attacking[/C0]. Or enrage it, I'm not sure.","line:0630b19":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Connect it to the [C0]Research Outpost's Generator[/C0]. You'll have to return and re-engage it every few hours, but other than that, it's completely automated.","line:01cbae3":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Great. Now, take a look at the list of specimens.","line:0bb8193":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh, no room on board? You can come by for it later.","line:0e29c17":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Remember, you'll want to [C0]install and activate the Machine[/C0] before attempting to collect these. You might also need to [C0]improve that equipment I gave you to catch some of these[/C0].","line:05cb24c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I have good news and bad news. Which do you want to hear first?","line:01b46f1":"The good news.","line:014a1c8":"The bad news.","line:0665d99":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: The good news is that I've honed in on what's causing the abnormalities in the ecosystem.","line:083b4b3":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: The bad news is that the samples you retrieved from the basin have dangerously high counts of cellular mutations.","line:0a758c8":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: This all points to one thing: that thing in the basin is [C2]harmful to life at a cellular level[/C2]. It damages everything around it, whether passively or...with intent.","line:03a5c47":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I need to write up a report on my findings - sorry, our findings - immediately. Maybe now they'll take me seriously.","line:01f45cd":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Thanks again for your help. I'd recommend that you avoid the area. It doesn't seem safe to be near the basin.","line:083d7a8":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Uh, ok - I don't think there's much to say...I studied Biological Sciences at Ironhaven college. It was a struggle.","line:0b84d4a":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: There were no other female students in the department that year. Or the year before, or the year before that.","line:024c355":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: It's hard not to feel like an outsider in an environment like that, you know? You probably don't.","line:0a886cf":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: When I graduated, I managed to land a job at the Northern Biological Research Society. And then, well, I was posted here. By myself.","line:0aff3da":"The [C0]Repulsion Machine[/C0] you installed is still connected to the Generator.","line:0b9e93a":"An old generator sputters and ticks over.","line:0bc9da0":"The [C0]Researcher's Repulsion Machine[/C0] could be connected to the [C0]Outpost's Generator[/C0] here.","line:00337d8":"Activate the machine?","line:01616d4":"Yes.","line:0295542":"Not right now.","line:0387cd5":"The [C0]Repulsion Machine[/C0] hums and whirrs to life. A few seconds later, a bright light shoots from the top, and an alarm begins blaring.","line:08056e8":"The [C0]Researcher[/C0] said this should keep the creature at bay - for a time, at least.","line:041bcfb":"After some searching, you find the [C0]Prototype Parts[/C0] that the Researcher needs to assemble the Sampling Device.","line:0004dc1":"You stow the [C0]Prototype Parts[/C0] on board.","line:01618ad":"You walk in and place the jewel-encrusted ring on a table by the Collector. His eyes widen.","line:08f60c5":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We're certainly making excellent progress now. And - I know what you're thinking.","line:0f528a4":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: An item like this would fetch a fortune at any auction. But for us...its value transcends material wealth.","line:0191ddf":"He opens the crimson book, its spine cracking audibly. Selecting a page carefully, he begins to read aloud. The words sound muffled, as though he's speaking through a thick haze.","line:08fcb76":"You hear a growling, crackling in your ears. Suddenly, your vision flares and both of your ears pop. He closes the book.","line:0bd64ff":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We must keep searching. I've been thinking more on where we might find another...","line:00a05cc":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Well, I got the sense that it was attacking the [C0]Research Outpost[/C0] itself, rather than me specifically.","line:0baedf5":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I suspect it was disturbed by some of my monitoring equipment. There were dozens of machines running there, all powered by a noisy generator.","line:05da43c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: It was huge - larger than any other marine species I've studied. It attacked with tentacles, so I'd guess at some sort of octopus or squid. Or an anemone.","line:0d9a7e1":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: One of my research vessels was moored around the back of the station, so I managed to slip away in that while it was tearing apart the front.","line:0755f5c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: There was a lot of valuable data - and equipment - left there. But I'm not going back. I can't - I won't face it again.","line:0d1fcd5":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Now that you mention it...I've been so preoccupied with the attack and having to rebuild here, I'd almost forgotten...","line:02ff842":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I found these letters. From my sister. She'd sent them to me while I was studying, before - before she...","line:068fa38":"The Researcher is quiet for a moment and stares off to the side.","line:0343f17":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Anyway, I kept finding them amongst my papers. I don't remember packing them, but I must have.","line:048024b":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I started finding them more frequently - they turned up in my collection nets. In my sampling tubes.","line:0184d8c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: They were letters I'd never seen before. But they were in her writing. They were in her name.","line:08c9ac1":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: They were saying things...talking about things that happened after she died. I can't explain it.","line:02f08a0":"A slab of rock cuts above the waves. There are [C0]four large, powerful fish[/C0] shapes carved into its face, and four great fissures running through the rock's base.","line:088dcad":"You slide the four sharks into the fissures and they slip down out of sight. Moments later, you spot something rising towards the surface of the water.","line:0d71f75":"This dog needs a home. Do you want it?","line:0ebebf9":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: A dog?! Oh gosh, let me see -","line:091b044":"The dog bounds over to the Researcher. She crouches down to pet the dog, grinning. The dog licks her chin in response.","line:018baa1":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I could definitely take this one off your hands - and I'd love the company. Are you sure?","line:026f44f":"Yes, you should take the dog.","line:0ec7406":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Yes! Thank you! Oh, we're going to be such good friends. He can be my assistant!","line:0eb353a":"On second thought, I'll keep the dog.","line:07acfdc":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Aw, that's ok. He can come by and visit anytime.","line:0225d34":"There is a skinny brown dog leaping around in the shallows. Occasionally it lunges at the water, snapping at some small, silvery fish. Its technique is ineffective.","line:0089f94":"\\[Disembark.\\]","line:095bd76":"\\[Continue sailing.\\]","line:07d9328":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You jump off the boat into thigh-high water. The dog stops chasing fish and focuses on you.","line:006b17d":"\\[Pat the dog.\\]","line:01e3f55":"You're too far away to pat the dog.","line:024e339":"\\[Slowly approach.\\]","line:0c971d4":"\\[Call for the dog.\\]","line:0a07b26":"DOG_NAME_KEY: The dog wags its tail briefly, but doesn't move.","line:084a9cf":"\\[Throw some fish towards the dog.\\]","line:0e50323":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You throw some scraps into the water near the dog. It pounces at the splash, and swallows sea water.","line:0f7c578":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0e0a7d3":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You wade towards the shore. As you get nearer, the dog backs up a little ways. It sits.","line:0a01adb":"\\[Pat the dog.\\]","line:0a48488":"You're too far away to pat the dog.","line:0e1fc25":"\\[Slowly approach.\\]","line:0e3f9d4":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You start to walk closer to the dog, but it runs away nervously and hides in some bushes. After a few moments, it emerges again.","line:01628f2":"\\[Call for the dog.\\]","line:0698588":"\\[Throw some fish towards the dog.\\]","line:0e2ddb5":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You throw some scraps towards the dog, which land in the sand. The dog eats them, along with a mouthful of sand.","line:007417c":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:020c403":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You make soft, encouraging noises, and the dog cautiously approaches. It stops just out of your reach.","line:05ff989":"\\[Pat the dog.\\]","line:0ed5f06":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You extend your arm out towards the dog. It shies away and retreats up the shoreline. It looks at you expectantly, and licks its lips.","line:0748739":"\\[Slowly approach.\\]","line:05be8f0":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You move closer to the dog. It seems startled, and runs back up the shoreline.","line:0398467":"\\[Call for the dog.\\]","line:0e24b68":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You call out to the dog softly, but it doesn't seem to want to come any closer.","line:0300e4e":"\\[Hold out some fish in your hand.\\]","line:0c12fbf":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0d7be14":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You hold out some fish scraps in the palm of your hand. The dog approaches slowly, but soon begins licking at them.","line:04d457f":"\\[Pat the dog.\\]","line:02c7a3d":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0c5af81":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You reach out and gently pat the dog. Its eyes follow your hand, and it seems to understand you're not a threat.","line:06c2cbe":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You pat the dog again. It seems to be enjoying it.","line:04e1ec4":"You make your way back towards the boat. As you're wading out, you hear the sloshing of four legs cutting through the water. You stop and turn around.","line:099117f":"DOG_NAME_KEY: The dog is standing a few paces behind you. It tilts its head questioningly.","line:0ffa269":"\\[Let it follow you.\\]","line:0a917b1":"You continue, this time with the dog alongside. Its tail is wagging so hard it beats the water into a froth behind it.","line:06552d2":"When you get to the boat, you turn around to pull the dog on board.","line:0f04b03":"\\[Shoo it away.\\]","line:0a8fc29":"You shout at the dog and hit the water with your hands. The dog scampers away, out of sight.","line:01c2a34":"You climb back onto your boat, leaving the dog behind.","line:0e1a573":"DOG_NAME_KEY: You lift the dog onto the deck. It walks around briefly, before curling into a ball and looking up at you. Maybe you could find this dog a more permanent home.","line:08c5de3":"You leave the dog treading water beside the boat. After some time, it turns around and swims back to shore.","line:0706f3e":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I thought I would relish the peace and quiet. But I miss having company. I've always had someone, or at least a pet. Out here...it's just machines.","line:047a725":"DOG_NAME_KEY: Suddenly, the dog stands upright and begins to retch, its stomach heaving. Seconds later, it vomits a wet glob onto the floor. [C1]Something glistens through the mucus[/C1].","line:07919d5":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh um, that's...interesting. I suppose that's yours. If you want it.","line:0fc0abf":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I can clean the rest up, don't worry about it.","line:0eda31f":"There are some boxes scattered haphazardly on the shore.","line:031c592":"Look inside.","line:0aab737":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:04933fe":"A curious looking chest is half submerged in the sand.","line:07cb109":"Look inside.","line:0b9d6a3":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0cc2843":"Waves lap at a pile of flotsam collecting on the beach. Nestled in the center is a wooden chest.","line:086f052":"Look inside.","line:0b88100":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0682687":"Lying just beneath the surface of the water is a floating chest, held down by a chain that disappears into the deep.","line:05ece4f":"Open it.","line:04b3111":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0cb9374":"The [C0]Laboratory[/C0] is in ruins, with equipment and research papers strewn about the place.","line:05b7d8a":"Open the cupboards.","line:0e2d605":"Inspect the equipment on the table.","line:0a523cf":"Look around on the floor.","line:0fc80f6":"There are some strange looking [C0]Prototype Parts[/C0] on the table, but you can't see any use for them right now.","line:025bc4b":"You check the cupboards.","line:067bd14":"There's nothing left in the cupboards.","line:09f0bbc":"You empty the cupboards.","line:046c3a7":"You look around on the floor. There are cracks in the base of the structure that grow to large gashes as you follow them along to the walls.","line:0389345":"All that's left are scattered sheets of paper.","line:06376a9":"You pluck an item from a gouge in the floor.","line:058c475":"\\[Kick the ashes.\\]","line:09e4ae8":"\\[Go back.\\]","line:071a300":"There's nothing left to kick.","line:0f4a6c8":"You kick the ashes. Your foot hits something hard at the bottom of the pile. You brush the remnants aside.","line:0fde7ee":"You take it.","line:049e0b3":"Where do you want to look?","line:062183b":"All that's left of this boat is an old husk. You pull a little closer.","line:0724cb6":"Look inside.","line:010bda6":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0a6463c":"A once strong wooden hull lays broken against the shoreline. The stern is completely beached.","line:0c7a2d0":"Try to get inside the stern.","line:08c6237":"You pull a bit closer and manage to clamber into the back of the wreck. You look around.","line:0b49380":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:01a63fa":"A rotten mast lays down on this island, half hidden by the foliage. At its base, an old boat is cracked in two.","line:0547319":"Look inside.","line:0ad9640":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:03dfd9a":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:076a5f2":"She reaches into her toolbox and pulls out a handful of components.","line:0ceb92e":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: How are things going?","line:08776cc":"A large man is watching you through the billowing smoke of a campfire, idly carving away at a wooden stake. He stands as you pull ashore.","line:0001da8":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Stranger. From that look on your face I'd say you've encountered the local [C3]wretches[/C3]. Take a seat.","line:0114866":"You join him by the fire.","line:00f443f":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I've been trying to rid them from this accursed jungle ever since we wrecked here.","line:0166ba5":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I'd ask you for safe passage away from here, but not until after I've [C0]avenged my squadron[/C0].","line:087f03d":"What happened to them?","line:0e954ce":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: A number of us went down in the fog, crashing into trees or ditching into the water. Those that survived rallied here, under the boughs of this giant tree.","line:024e62b":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: But it offered us scant protection. Before help could arrive, our numbers quickly dwindled. Picked off by the fiends and the forest.","line:08f227b":"I'm listening.","line:0a09d82":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I've met a few would-be rescuers over the years. But none would help me in my fight. Are you any different to the rest?","line:010453f":"I can help.","line:0baeff3":"Not right now.","line:059260b":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I expected as such. Stay safe, if you can.","line:02baea9":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Fisherman. Have you found your courage?","line:0fea300":"Yes, I can help you.","line:041e853":"Not right now.","line:0e26eaa":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Hmmph. Be off with you, then.","line:0c3f931":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I figured you'd be up for it. You...you have the look. Listen up.","line:053f824":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: First, we need to [C0]find the lost pieces of my squadron's mortar[/C0]. We'll then use that to bombard the beasts.","line:04775b7":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Other planes went down to the [C0]North[/C0] and [C0]East[/C0] of where we are now. I'll mark the possible crash sites on your map, you go and see what you can salvage.","line:0629962":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Hmm?","line:0923119":"Can you make up some Bait for me?","line:00ece10":"What will you do now?","line:007be6d":"I have a creature corpse to show you.","line:0bfd6bd":"Let's talk about baiting the traps.","line:0ee2673":"I've found parts of the mortar.","line:044ac1f":"What am I supposed to be doing?","line:02d0053":"Are there any shipwrecks around here?","line:08930a7":"Tell me about the 'Mind Suckers'.","line:03a377e":"That's everything.","line:0ab3f52":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Shipwrecks? No. Anything that meets its end here is quickly swallowed by the silt.","line:04fdea6":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Devilish creatures, through and through. They'll stalk you along the waterways and emerge suddenly, [C3]screeching their terrible song[/C3].","line:0003ebc":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: You need to [C0]find the lost pieces of my squadron's mortar[/C0]. I've marked some locations to search on your map. Let me know how you get on.","line:01bd16e":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: You've found one component, but it's still missing a piece. Nearly there; keep looking.","line:03e7666":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: That's the lot. Now, while I work on assembling the mortar, you can get started on the next phase of the plan.","line:03968bc":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: You may have noticed some [C0]contraptions[/C0] in the lagoons around here. I've assembled those traps for the [C3]Mind Suckers[/C3]. We just need to [C0]lure them in[/C0] there.","line:06691e0":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Once they're in, you see, I can [C1]fire on them with our new mortar[/C1]. And that'll be the end of them. No more nightmares.","line:0f5c679":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I'll mark the locations of the traps on your map. Got it?","line:0538e91":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Have you got everything?","line:0c6bfd5":"How do we get the Mind Suckers into the traps?","line:0304127":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: They're attracted to some very specific types of [C1]Bait[/C1]. Your skills will come in handy here yet again.","line:0989b5f":"Is it safe?","line:0985efc":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Of course not.","line:067943e":"How did you make those traps?","line:0904eee":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: With patience. The [C0]creatures only seem to sense movement[/C0]. So whenever one was close, I froze.","line:0ee5fcc":"I understand. So what's next?","line:0680272":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: We need to [C0]make three special Baits[/C0] from different combinations of fish.","line:0ff0c25":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Did you want to know anything else about the [C0]Bait[/C0]?","line:0a65ead":"Let's discuss the Bait for the first one.","line:0a762b1":"Let's discuss the Bait for the second one.","line:06ee9c0":"Let's discuss the Bait for the last one.","line:00abffd":"Where do I put the Bait?","line:0337ea7":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: In one of the [C0]traps[/C0] I've constructed in the lagoons. They're marked on your [C0]Map[/C0].","line:0b8a7f0":"That's all for now.","line:0aeaf04":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: This one takes [C0]three fish[/C0] from the area to make.","line:07d1325":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: This one needs [C0]two fish[/C0] from the area to make.","line:0559557":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: This one requires [C0]two fish[/C0] from the area to make.","line:0433931":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: That should do it. I'll just mix these in...here. [C0]Load this into a trap[/C0], then get well clear from it.","line:02381cf":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: That should do it. I'll just mix these in...here. [C0]Load this into a trap[/C0], then get well clear from it.","line:0284531":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: That should do it. I'll just mix these in...here. [C0]Load this into a trap[/C0], then get well clear from it.","line:043441d":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: [C2]I don't have all the fish for that bait yet[/C2]. Come back when you've got the rest.","line:0bc547a":"A large cage is suspended over the water. A small receptacle is floating underneath.","line:09bb584":"Load the trap with Bait.","line:054eafd":"Leave it alone.","line:0f55e2f":"You load the [C0]Bait[/C0] into the trap. You should probably move away.","line:08d8b2e":"This trap has been baited. Better get to a safe distance and wait.","line:0c06698":"Inside is the obliterated corpse of a [C3]Mind Sucker[/C3]. The Airman will be expecting proof of your success.","line:0bab137":"The rest of the carcass sinks out of sight.","line:03d549d":"You leave it in there for now.","line:0ed3843":"A mangled mess of wood and wire. The trap itself was re-usable, but not after being hit by a mortar.","line:0c53a43":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Let's see it then.","line:0db5672":"You hand the tattered lump of flesh to the Airman. It's almost unrecognizable, but you both know it couldn't have belonged to anything else.","line:0eca831":"He pokes at it with his knife, testing the rubbery meat. He seems satisfied.","line:0706aa0":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Yes...this is one of the beasts. Progress at last. More to go, though.","line:08d384f":"You drop the flesh onto the ground and he gives it a few slashes with the knife. It wobbles a little.","line:0173490":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Another one taken care of. One remains, by my count. Let's finish this.","line:0c9fe02":"You drop the large, bloodied carcass in front of the Airman. His eyes fill with sadistic delight.","line:0f9d21d":"He bends down and plunges his knife into the soft flesh. It falls away before the blade, revealing a [C3]glint of metal[/C3].","line:0a739d1":"With a sickening tear, he wrests it from where it was embedded in the flesh of the creature. He holds it aloft. You recognize it as a [C3]necklace[/C3], glistening in gore.","line:0776f7e":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Well fisherman, some fortune at last. This ought to fetch a decent price from the right collector. Here, why don't you take it.","line:0d176f0":"He stands back from the corpse. A melancholic look comes over his face.","line:0862401":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: And now...well, that's that, I suppose.","line:0459ffa":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Oh, you have more?","line:086a1a6":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I can't say for sure. I thought I'd be asking you for an escort away from this place, but...this has become somewhat of a home to me.","line:0e1cdf5":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: It doesn't feel right to leave my brothers here. I think I shall stay a while longer.","line:0cb4dbe":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: In the meantime, I can make up some special [C0]Bait[/C0] for you. [C1]It ought to help with your fishing[/C1].","line:0a07f55":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I'll need some fish from you first. Any type will do - but [C1]the more you give me, the more Bait I can make[/C1].","line:01c5ffe":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Let me just grind these up...won't be a moment...","line:04796cb":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: This is what I could make. Take it all; it won't keep here.","line:06d226a":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: [C2]You didn't give me enough fish[/C2], so I can't make up any [C0]Bait[/C0] for you.","line:03064ff":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: The boys called them [C3]Mind Suckers[/C3], on account of them, well...affecting the mind. They made us see things...do things...","line:09cd95e":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: The first time it happened to me I saw...shadows of my squadmates. Reaching out to me in a feverish dream.","line:06fd6c6":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: When I finally snapped out of it, I was covered in bloodied scratches - they must've sent me running through the foliage.","line:04f40cf":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Since then I've done my best to avoid the fiends. [C0]Their senses seem to be based on movement[/C0], so move carefully.","line:057e7cd":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: They go crazy for that stuff - day, night, it doesn't seem to matter. All sorts of fish usually show up.","line:022b6e6":"A crooked boulder with a small, simple platform at its base. The [C0]twisted shape of a deformed fish[/C0] is barely recognizable, carved into the rockface.","line:03c57c8":"The waves lap up to the platform where you laid the aberration. As the water makes contact with it, a buzzing sound fills the air.","line:075cdeb":"How will you honor your squadmates?","line:0879e2a":"I found some dog tags.","line:0975a70":"Why were you wanting dog tags again?","line:07a41ac":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I've hung a few of their [C0]Dog Tags[/C0] up on the tree behind me. It seemed fitting enough.","line:0b2a678":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: But I've only got tags from the ones I...you must understand...I never found all of their bodies.","line:089d069":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: If you happened to [C0]find any of their Dog Tags[/C0], I could add them to the tree with their brothers.","line:0adb26e":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I have a number of mechanical doodads that you might find useful. Here, take this one - in good faith. [C1]I'll give you more for each tag you bring me[/C1].","line:0046281":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Let me see.","line:0af84ec":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I...thank you. I'll hang them on the tree. Here, as promised.","line:0ef34cf":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Come back when you've actually got something to show me.","line:0bdccb2":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: I want to hang the Dog Tags of my fallen squadmates on the tree behind me. [C1]I'll give you some componentry for each tag you bring me[/C1].","line:0361b20":"You see a campsite. Some old fish are suspended on a spit over a fire that was never lit. A pile of fabric is gathered at the base of a large tree nearby.","line:0aec3af":"What do you want to do?","line:06f95d4":"\\[Inspect the fish on the spit.\\]","line:0c5e81d":"\\[Check the bundle of fabric.\\]","line:05f97d7":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0a9929c":"Rotten fish hang from the spit. The fire below had been prepared. Someone must've left in a hurry.","line:0ab83b5":"A nest of rags lies at the base of a tree. Somebody slept here. The rags are covered in bark chips - there are symbols carved into the tree trunk above.","line:036352a":"There are three distinct sets of symbols.","line:0b92a28":"\\[Look at the first set.\\]","line:0969557":"\\[Look at the second set.\\]","line:0632bb7":"\\[Look at the third set.\\]","line:0e9cab2":"\\[Go back.\\]","line:01e199e":"There's a book symbol underneath a wave, and then an upwards arrow. A cloud hangs over it all.","line:0e372e9":"Five unfamiliar symbols mark the corners of a pentagram. The shape of a person is lying down in the center.","line:08f81ff":"A book symbol sits above a wave. A downwards arrow points from the book, down through the wave.","line:0f84c31":"The wreckage of an old fighter plane lies buried deep in the sand. You pull a little closer.","line:04d21dc":"Look inside.","line:06ff5eb":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:059e06d":"The fuselage of an old fighter plane sits amidst a mass of broken wings and wheels.","line:094e6fd":"Try to get inside the fuselage.","line:0a3d959":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0c78495":"The previously still water bubbles up and over, obscuring the fish. A few moments later, when the water calms, something else is on the platform.","line:0aa8e10":"What do you know about the silver and crimson book?","line:0da6fae":"She shudders at the very mention of the book.","line:04dca92":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: You're really asking me? After all this time? You know it must be returned.","line:0ab1d38":"She looks at you with deep pity.","line:053082d":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Go and do what's right -- for her. [C3]Throw it back.[/C3]","line:0243a57":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: ...","line:0b0875b":"The door is locked.","line:013f03d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: ...","line:03df026":"Tell me more about that book of yours.","line:04b8d95":"The words you read from that book...what did they do to me?","line:0e05dc5":"How long have you lived here?","line:0d669f6":"What are you doing with these relics?","line:0906417":"What will you do once you have all the relics?","line:0ce6fba":"Do you know who owned these relics?","line:0f7ebbb":"I don't understand...who are you?","line:0f68103":"You mentioned saving someone...","line:0d60b89":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Regardless. You are due a reward.","line:0f6d664":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Quite some time. I used to be a fisherman, as was my father before. But two decades ago I took up residence here. I needed to focus on...other endeavours.","line:0e532c9":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I found that this island has a certain strength to it - those dark basalt columns stretching downwards into the deep.","line:07485f9":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Why, collecting them of course. An investment for times to come.","line:019c78d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I largely don't...but I read the seas. I see the swells that give shape to the formless. I hear the waves that whisper secrets to their witnesses.","line:0cee33b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: And I speak to the currents that hold a memory of all that they claim.","line:028c49f":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Yes.","line:0612c31":"Who?","line:0db1ec9":"He looks at you. For a moment, a look of something like regret flashes in his eyes.","line:0d66540":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: An old friend.","line:076004b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I am what was fractured from you on that day you dredged the depths. I am what could be. I am your breathless self.","line:0e47a57":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Yes. She will rise from the deep. The book describes it.","line:0631cbf":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We almost have all of the pieces. Just one more.","line:050cee7":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Which book? This one here?","line:0261045":"With a wry grin he pulls a dusty tome from the nearest shelf and glances at the cover.","line:0026141":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: There's really not much to be said of \"Histories of The Gray Isles\". It's quite a chore.","line:07786db":"Don't play dumb. You know which book I mean.","line:084d54f":"Forget it.","line:0206698":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Gladly.","line:0a2818c":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Play dumb? Your hypocrisy is wearying. I suppose we must go through this rigmarole yet again.","line:0bf5338":"The [C3]Book of The Deep[/C3] appears in his hands, sheathed in its dirty crimson jacket.","line:0a2adc4":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Go ahead. Ask us.","line:0223e99":"Where did you get it?","line:0345cd1":"Forget it.","line:0995f56":"Sparkling dust motes hang in the air between you.","line:0ea3566":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Don't you remember? You were there.","line:060634c":"The air around the book begins to pulse rhythmically like a quickening heartbeat.","line:041628b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: So was she.","line:02af9e7":"Who?","line:0298d26":"Give me the book.","line:07503e7":"Forget it.","line:04db5d3":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: You wanted to forget. Begged me.","line:07215cc":"The room bristles.","line:0469d9f":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: This is what you asked for.","line:0ced5e1":"Give me the book.","line:034dcb0":"Forget it.","line:0c9d167":"Your words hang in the space between.","line:090c683":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: You won't change a thing. The book is ours.","line:00b8c72":"\\[Step closer.\\]","line:02505f3":"Forget it.","line:08a9dac":"You take a step closer through the crackling room. The Collector lurches forwards in response.","line:0cffe6e":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: What can you possibly hope to achieve?","line:07ca2ed":"\\[Take the book.\\]","line:0ae3a0c":"Forget it.","line:0cc0d03":"You strike out with your right fist, punching hard into the jaw of the Collector. His face shatters and falls to the ground.","line:0b0d37d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: ...","line:0ed213f":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: You're pathetic.","line:0257d50":"[C3]The Book of The Deep is in your hands.[/C3]","line:0ddfc83":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Understand this, plainly, before you sink us into despair. I know how to bring her back. It's all right there on the pages; and now you've seen its power first hand.","line:05ee31a":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We wield the power to release her from her slumber! We can undo everything...undo what you did!","line:00b8ec7":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The book holds power from the deep. I merely...extended its powers towards you. Is there one in particular you wish to know more about?","line:0ae0921":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Are there other powers you wish to know more about?","line:0556a2e":"Haste","line:0372dca":"Manifest","line:0335dc5":"Banish","line:0d497ca":"Atrophy","line:0b0d5f8":"Nevermind.","line:0db26a2":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The words of haste are instant and cruel. They will impart a terrible speed to your vessel.","line:02f9226":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Be warned, however - it may put a great deal of stress on your engines.","line:06e7fee":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Use of these words will induce a trance-like state. While in this state time will pass in the blink of an eye. When it is over, you will find yourself here.","line:0e76213":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: As always, I caution against overusing this. Selectively and strategically utilize it when you need it most.","line:0363249":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The banishing words will provide you a temporary protection from...most things. If spoken swiftly enough, they can be used defensively.","line:0b191a3":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Choose your moment carefully. The more they are spoken, the more they are...understood.","line:0616158":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: This phrase instantly culls the closest shoal of fish, readying them for swift reaping. It can be heard from a great distance, so you need not be close to your victims.","line:0284a77":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: But the population is unlikely to recover from such vile trauma. Use it sparingly.","line:0f7a62b":"You undock next to an old rowboat. Somebody is here. He's hunched over by the campfire, muttering to himself. You cautiously approach.","line:0f106f2":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: [S1]Did you...did you throw it back?![/S1]","line:00a3147":"What?","line:0573a64":"I don't know what you're talking about.","line:0cd8491":"No.","line:0adb574":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: The book!","line:0f40ecc":"I think you've mistaken me for someone else.","line:014da25":"I don't understand.","line:07d7b99":"No.","line:034b58c":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I'm not seeing things! It's really you, isn't it?","line:0d2af55":"Are you ok?","line:0a59bac":"Who do you think I am?","line:08622c4":"No.","line:0cd5252":"He turns away, wringing his hands. He speaks to the fire.","line:03961e9":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: It was him. Him and his damned wife. They dredged up that old book. But something...something cloaked in fog...followed it out. Right through the boat. [S3][C2]BOOM![/C2][/S3]","line:073420d":"The man makes crude explosion noises and motions wide with his hands, still talking to the fire, as though pantomiming a story to a child.","line:01be53b":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: It spoke. It said it was coming for our breath...that we wouldn't be needing it soon. And then darkness crashed down.","line:04cfd63":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: An age later, some of us washed up on the shore. And him. Still clutching that book.","line:0caaa0b":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: \"[C3]THROW IT BACK![/C3]\" We cried, as the fog rolled ashore. We thought...surely...it can still be undone.","line:0697520":"What book?","line:09facb1":"What are you talking about?","line:09769fd":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Silver and crimson! The book - covered in her blood!","line:03ae802":"You're not making any sense.","line:0133fda":"\\[Turn to leave.\\]","line:0fa3e16":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: [S2][C3]THROW IT BACK![/C3][/S2]","line:08406b8":"The man closes his eyes tight as he holds back tears. His voice falls to a whisper.","line:0eeaac4":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Please. The [C0]Lighthouse Keeper[/C0]. She saw. She knows where it came from. Where it...where it needs to go.","line:061345c":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: ...","line:09d0c83":"Tell me more about this book.","line:03da3df":"What do you know about the fog?","line:0546b62":"What does the Lighthouse Keeper have to do with this?","line:01e6ccb":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:01b4194":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Silver and crimson...silver and crimson...","line:085ef94":"He rocks back and forth, staring through the flames.","line:0d466d7":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: It cloaks that calamitous thing...it's evil, haven't you felt it?","line:0bfcc8a":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: She saw it all. That ruinous day.","line:0e2eff7":"OLD_MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Ask her. Beg her. Tell her I...","line:0ce42eb":"He trails off, his face collapsing in sorrow.","line:0ee5e2f":"You enter the house, carrying the ornate necklace. The Collector recognizes it almost immediately.","line:0d32532":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: An excellent find. It demands pride of place in my collection.","line:0b5f209":"He sweeps aside some scraps on a dusty table, candle wax pooling in its corners. He places the necklace carefully in the clearing.","line:0aba8e5":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: And I suppose you'll be demanding recompense as well...","line:00ea005":"Once more he opens the book, dust pouring from the pages as he reads aloud. You begin to feel weak, but you're rooted to the spot - knees on the verge of buckling.","line:0e2fa8b":"As he finishes speaking you feel blood rushing back to your legs. A strange feeling of power grows in your chest.","line:0339a51":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We're...so close. One more remains.","line:0a67962":"Why can't you search for these relics yourself?","line:01cefe1":"What do you know about the Old Mayor of Little Marrow?","line:03d88c6":"How do you know where these relics are?","line:0b9d182":"Are you...human?","line:0678ff4":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The ocean no longer wishes to...cooperate. As the waves are unsafe for me, you will be my surrogate.","line:08541e9":"He ponders for a moment.","line:0c5bbdd":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: It's surprising, isn't it? The attachments we hold towards simple objects. But they are anything but simple. Seemingly mute articles can speak in different ways.","line:00a760d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: If I showed you a childhood toy, you would be awash with forgotten memories.","line:00baf34":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: They hold the power to recall what was once lost.","line:0417c4a":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: That stuttering old fool...yes, I knew him. He'd join us on the water sometimes, but was more hindrance than help.","line:0960b73":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: He never seemed entirely with it. I can't imagine he has fared too well since I last saw him.","line:0c4e55d":"Your inquiry is met with a piercing gaze.","line:00b6bf5":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Why, of course. As human as you are.","line:07ae03b":"A stone shrine. An upright slab bears a carving - [C0]two heavily plated creatures, locked in battle[/C0]. A lower slab holds two shallow grooves.","line:0cdc8ce":"The rock splits with an almighty crack. It crumbles away, revealing its core.","line:07c3031":"A stone shrine. An upright slab bears a carving - [C0]two pale bottom-dwellers, hiding from their fate[/C0]. A lower slab holds two shallow grooves.","line:0289fc7":"The rock splits with an almighty crack. It crumbles away, revealing its core.","line:0d90c85":"A stone shrine. An upright slab bears a carving - [C3]two malformed fish, writhing under the sun[/C3]. A lower slab holds two shallow grooves.","line:0d36761":"The rock splits with an almighty crack. It crumbles away, revealing its core.","line:0920bdc":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:01264e3":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:02b5af7":"What am I supposed to be doing?","line:0ac043f":"The flames are lit.","line:0459f14":"I've lit some of the flames.","line:059fa45":"I'm looking for sunken relics. Are there any shipwrecks around here?","line:051ade0":"What's that scroll you're holding?","line:0f6eeb7":"Are there others that share your...beliefs?","line:0c08f39":"I should go.","line:029c551":"A man meets you as you dock, bracing himself against the wind and spray.","line:032857d":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: O rapturous day, a fresh disciple carried to me atop the waves! Come ashore, weak thing, and rest your weary soul.","line:01263b3":"I'm just passing through.","line:0e9a3a1":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Nonsense!","line:0f6a325":"Uh, alright.","line:03fea56":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Your arrival is providence from the deep itself! I have been calling...and now, you are the answer.","line:0030cf7":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: The rite of purification is almost at hand, and you are to be my replacement.","line:073bfbf":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: The rite of purification is...overdue. Are you ready to begin?","line:0c57a7c":"I'm listening...","line:0b41db9":"I should get going.","line:0312763":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: The sea will return you to me in time.","line:00d83c8":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Your trial begins immediately. Tell me, what does your spirit seek?","line:0ac7fe8":"Happiness.","line:0263a50":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Hah! Merely an excuse to halt the search for something greater. Happiness is, by definition, a compromise.","line:092bfab":"Sadness.","line:04785ce":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Liar. Nobody seeks sadness. Truly, you seek pity.","line:0bc06a4":"Emptiness.","line:048e14b":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Yes. A pure vessel. Only those devoid of mortality can ascend past it.","line:0965094":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: And your flesh. What does it crave?","line:0985ab5":"The warmth of the sun.","line:0f3fabf":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: And yet it eludes you. Darkness is cast over the rest of your days.","line:03e1858":"The sting of the salt.","line:06bb724":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Pain is a trick of the flesh. Do not surrender to it.","line:0e9257e":"The chill of the water.","line:04e42b3":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: I sense it in you...a glimmer of what waits below.","line:0b8f355":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Finally. What does the world deserve?","line:01063d3":"Everything.","line:0a39d64":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: In a way. It deserves all that is washed ashore - freely given from the deep. But no more than that.","line:03284fb":"Nothing.","line:025b57a":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Exactly. And yet it takes, endlessly. Harvesting, draining. But soon it will know that it has taken too much. It is already too late.","line:0ea73b4":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: The trial is concluded. You still have much to learn. But that knowledge will be delivered to you in time.","line:0a9cde6":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Now. Your role, as my initiate, is to act as [C0]Herald of the Purge[/C0]. Just as I was, for the one before me.","line:0c888c3":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: The nearby spires blaze with eternal fire, yet the stone hearths of these three idols lie barren and void.","line:0dd5d62":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Retrieve [C3]three Fathomless Flames[/C3] from the crags behind us and ignite the crucibles.","line:0a71bbf":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Visit the [C0]Shrines of the Deep[/C0]. I will mark them. They will offer further guidance - and I must provide no more.","line:0a94d39":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: I can see that. But we cannot proceed in darkness - all three must be lit.","line:0209964":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Ahh. I can feel it. The chill of the deep touches us now. It is time. Come.","line:0985cb5":"You follow him up the steps of the temple. At the top is a black stone altar. Stacked high upon the altar are layers of dark, damp wood.","line:01f6b3e":"He draws the antique pocket watch from his robe. It sways hypnotically in the breeze.","line:0742c91":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: It is almost yours. May it mark the start of your journey...and the end.","line:0f17c03":"Still holding the pocket watch in one hand, he clambers atop the pyre and raises his scroll. [C3]He begins to chant[/C3].","line:0791a83":"What are you doing?","line:0704f89":"He ignores you.","line:0ef86f2":"\\[Stand back.\\]","line:0c085b6":"You are rooted to the spot.","line:075362e":"\\[Say nothing.\\]","line:0e58bf4":"The wind picks up, swirling sea spray around the altar. A cold blue flame rises from the sodden wood at his feet.","line:0ec2a93":"Stop this!","line:0989b4b":"His chanting grows louder.","line:0647e70":"\\[Look away.\\]","line:089986f":"You can't.","line:01118fa":"\\[Say nothing.\\]","line:0bb5d4c":"The freezing blaze climbs his legs. His chanting continues, no pain detectable in his voice.","line:05e9401":"He lifts his arms skyward. Seconds later, the inferno engulfs him.","line:0cc947a":"It rages for a moment, then abruptly dies away. A cold mist pools around the floor of the temple briefly before the wind sweeps it into the sea.","line:0ebacf9":"No trace of the Fanatic remains.","line:0c6ce59":"The pyre is cold and damp.","line:0293e34":"\\[Inspect the pyre.\\]","line:09b60ed":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:03dafcf":"You take the pocket watch - it's freezing cold. It vibrates in your palm, clock hands spinning wildly below the cracked face.","line:02f8683":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: You are to prepare the ritual. You must light the stone crucibles around the temple with [C3]three Fathomless Flames[/C3].","line:05f6f93":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: You will receive further illumination at the [C0]three Shrines of the Deep[/C0]. They are scattered about not far from here.","line:0413ac4":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: Relics, you say? Perhaps...one such as this?","line:09fc501":"He pulls an antique pocket watch from inside his robe. [C3]Droplets of sea spray crackle and seethe in the air around it[/C3].","line:0c9aa05":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: You are drawn to it too, I see. It found me during my rite of proving as I scavenged for creatures of power.","line:087597d":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: It sapped at my spirit when I first recovered it. But I came to appreciate its strange nourishment, with time.","line:044fb04":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: As will you. When the ritual is prepared, it will be yours to carry forth.","line:0cf2285":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: There are pretenders. Failures that make a mockery of the deep. I tried...correcting their ways.","line:07f1e90":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: But I soon saw that they had lost the path. I left them to their ceaseless hunger.","line:0e97272":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: I found it...at the end of my other life. It washed ashore, as all great gifts do.","line:026ec6a":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: It took some time for me to decipher the runes. It speaks of an incomprehensible door.","line:023a9ef":"FANATIC_NAME_KEY: And those wretched, twisted fish that swam through...their flesh is the closest thing to a key.","line:029760c":"The statue holds a stone crucible. It's empty.","line:024393f":"The statue holds a stone crucible. It's empty.","line:00b0218":"The statue holds a stone crucible. It's empty.","line:0222402":"A cold flame roars in the statue's hands.","line:0a6deb2":"The statue is lit with a cold flame.","line:0bf3027":"A stone shrine, split open.","line:082ed54":"A stone shrine, split open.","line:08d5d93":"A stone shrine, split open.","line:05eb148":"Preparations are complete. The Fanatic awaits.","line:0668eb3":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Not all schools of fish are the same. Some contain...[C3]abnormal specimens[/C3]. Sometimes you can even tell just looking from the surface.","line:0d22b92":"The Fishmonger reaches under the counter and hands you a damp, battered book. A few shimmering fish scales are stuck to the cover.","line:0e5555e":"She pulls a [C1]Book[/C1] from a toolbox nearby and hands it to you. A few of the pages are stuck together with grease.","line:0be0996":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Your boat's looking a bit banged up. I can [C1]repair[/C1] that here if you like.","line:0de2ca1":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Looks like some of your [C0]equipment could use some fixing[/C0]. We can [C1]repair[/C1] that here.","line:0c12b7c":"He pulls a crumpled [C1]Book[/C1] from his back pocket and hands it to you. A number of the pages are folded over.","line:01879d4":"He pulls a [C1]Book[/C1] from a stack sitting on his desk and hands it to you. It's covered in dust, but otherwise seems in good condition.","line:0c969d9":"I've got a Conger Eel here.","line:058924f":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Let me see - oh, hmm. That's a [C0]Conger Eel[/C0] alright, but it's not sufficiently [C2]aged[/C2]. If I take it now, the dog is sure to snatch it before it ages fully.","line:0bfb451":"INGFELL_RESIDENT_NAME_KEY: Please, come back after it's had some time to mature.","line:0999a3c":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Just leave whatever you have here. I'll keep the order on ice until it's all ready to go.","line:0602a38":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Alright, come back when you have everything. Now, to regular business, eh?","line:0c678b9":"You don't have any [C0]Packed Explosives[/C0]. Perhaps the [C0]Whaler[/C0] at [C0]Ingfell[/C0] has some more.","line:0651486":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Just leave whatever you have here. I'll keep the order on ice until it's all ready to go.","line:02cb88a":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Alright, come back when you have everything. Now, to regular business, eh?","line:0389a20":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I've got one here for you, in fact. It's a bit [C2]banged up[/C2], but you could get it [C1]fixed at the Shipwright[/C1].","line:041981c":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Here's that [C0]Crab Pot[/C0] I was going to give you earlier.","line:075aa42":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: You can come by and grab it later, I guess. To regular business then.","line:0f8fb5e":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I've got a customer after [C0]a Fiddler Crab[/C0] and [C0]a Common Crab[/C0]. Both species can be found around here.","line:0dc4a6c":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Have you got any crabs for that order?","line:02bb489":"Yes.","line:07b1ae4":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Don't forget, if your [C0]Crab Pots[/C0] get a bit [C2]worn out[/C2], the [C1]Shipwright should be able to patch 'em up[/C1].","line:0590c42":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Alright, come back when you have everything. Now, to regular business, eh?","line:071e6c1":"Not right now.","line:04158f1":"You hold on to the crabs for now.","line:0a17a25":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: I'll let you know when I get more orders in. For now, on to business as usual.","line:0b7a7b4":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Remember, any [C3]aberrant[/C3] will suffice. I suspect they're all the same...underneath.","line:0eb08d1":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Alright, come back when you have one for me. Now, to regular business, eh?","line:02aec44":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I've also allocated some money to [C1]improve the Fishmonger's services[/C1]. He might have something to talk to you about soon.","line:068d0d0":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: There's something else I wanted to - hmm...","line:084d2af":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: No. Forget it.","line:06e6efa":"You disembark and take the package over to the Dockworker. He's standing motionless on the docks, staring down at the water.","line:0931c4c":"You press the package into his hands - his fingers slowly gripping it is the closest thing to a response you get.","line:0706408":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: ...","line:03e78a7":"I've got a package here for you.","line:0769a4b":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: A delivery, eh? Oh, it's a big one. Let me see...","line:0462077":"He takes the large package and examines it gently with his hands. He lifts it to one ear and listens for a while. He seems satisfied.","line:046a154":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Much appreciated, friend. Now, if you'll excuse me...wish me luck!","line:0c3012e":"He turns and hurries off down the dock without another word to you - or compensation.","line:0bf4f57":"The [C0]Dockworker[/C0] is standing motionless on the edge of the dock, staring down at the water. He seems paralyzed by fear at what he sees.","line:0236646":"\\[Stay with him.\\]","line:0cc3797":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0ce48e4":"You stand with him for a while. Occasionally, a tremor shakes his body and his breathing becomes labored.","line:02a3ad6":"\\[Stay with him.\\]","line:08fb9a7":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:032833b":"He strains, clenching his fists - eyes shut tight with the effort. A tear rolls down his cheek.","line:062a33b":"\\[Stay with him.\\]","line:07126e6":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:01e8fe0":"His body relaxes suddenly and his eyes snap open again. They are cloudy and expressionless. Fluid rattles through his lungs.","line:065cd0f":"A [C3]drop of dark ooze[/C3] falls from one of his ears and lands on the dock. It slips between the boards and disappears into the water below.","line:0ba5372":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:09e4b9a":"You pull up alongside a boat at anchor. There are signs of life on board, but nobody appears to greet you.","line:02369cf":"\\[Call out.\\]","line:07a9d9c":"Almost immediately, a small slot in the door snaps open. A pair of frantic eyes peer out at you.","line:0fda6d3":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: [S1]Who goes there?[/S1]","line:0a65646":"A fisherman.","line:0e83319":"A monster.","line:0612edb":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Very funny.","line:01a1a51":"Nobody.","line:046772e":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0e0394c":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: What do you want?","line:0b547cb":"I was just checking to see if you're ok.","line:007a8fc":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Do I seem ok?! No, I am very much NOT ok. I'm supposed to be [C0]delivering this package to Little Marrow[/C0]. But I'm being stalked!","line:0eaf454":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: A [C3]huge leviathan[/C3] lurks in these deep waters - I've seen it! It hung in the water, its gaping mouth just below the boat!","line:0e2c2f4":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: It would've swallowed this vessel whole if I hadn't bolted for the shallows. I'm not going any further into this accursed island chain!","line:0a6eef8":"I could deliver the package to Little Marrow for you.","line:020d017":"I'd better get going.","line:08edbdd":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: You would? Well, that would work, I guess.","line:0dac5e7":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Oh, you won't take it after all? Just my luck.","line:03da132":"The Courier pushes a lumpy brown package through the doorhole. It squelches slightly as you take it in your hands. [C3]Dark fluid oozes[/C3] from one corner.","line:0fc2215":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Thank you, stranger. This is bound for the [C0]Dockworker at Little Marrow[/C0].","line:02af8f9":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: I'm not sure what's inside, but...listen, I know this sounds crazy...sometimes I think I can hear the [C3]faintest of whispers[/C3] coming from it.","line:03fb036":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Now, I'm not supposed to be transporting live goods - don't have the equipment for it. So just...be careful with this thing, whatever it is.","line:0877744":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Here, why don't you take this, too.","line:002187f":"Again, an item emerges from the doorhole. This time, a [C1]Book[/C1] is pushed through and thuds onto the deck below. You pick it up.","line:076cf6e":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: I'll be on my way whenever the coast is clear. Safe travels.","line:0df7ae6":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: Hmmph.","line:07a16e4":"Suddenly, the slot snaps shut.","line:0296efb":"COURIER_NAME_KEY: You again. What is it?","line:0c94324":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Ah, um, hello. What can I do for you today?","line:07d7379":"\\[Show him the stone tablet.\\]","line:0c62896":"I'm just here with some trinkets.","line:07ebf8b":"The Trader takes the [C0]Stone Tablet[/C0] from you and inspects it closely, turning it over in his hands.","line:01ccf4d":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Some years ago I...acquired this other piece.","line:017f2b9":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: You found this near those [C0]ruins in Devil's Spine[/C0] didn't you?","line:03c82f1":"Yes.","line:0af0665":"I don't remember.","line:04de657":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Ah, well I suspect there will be [C0]more out there[/C0]. I'll hold onto this for now and study it further while you search for the other fragments.","line:086532b":"The Trader takes the [C0]Stone Tablet[/C0] from you and lays it on a table next to the others.","line:0793c71":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Hmm...judging by the age of the stone and the shape of the glyph, these are part of the same set.","line:0442218":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: I'll keep this for now until you come across any others. It looks like they join together to form a square, so hopefully there's just [C1]one more to find[/C1].","line:054d442":"The Trader takes the [C0]Stone Tablet[/C0] from you and places it alongside the others. He turns them over and arranges them together in a square.","line:0b635b7":"On the undersides of the tablets, new glyphs begin to form, casting an [C3]eerie light[/C3] onto the low ceiling.","line:0a42b18":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Mhmm...yes. Go on...","line:06850a8":"He begins transcribing the glyphs onto an old scrap of parchment. Each stroke appears to demand excruciating concentration.","line:0f7a257":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: I only know of one \"[C0]guiding light[/C0]\", but these tablets predate the lighthouse at Greater Marrow by centuries.","line:0c00524":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: The fragments are fused together now. Why don't you take this back? In theory, they should open a lock somewhere. But where? Hmm...","line:091b712":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: An intriguing mystery - do let me know if you make any progress.","line:0e77884":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Oh, no room? Come back whenever you like - I'll hold onto it for you.","line:00d5138":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Oh, you've got another? Wonderful. Please, let me see.","line:023d40f":"You climb the many steps leading up to the [C0]Ancient Lighthouse[/C0]. At its base is a solid stone door.","line:0ff3761":"You can't see a handle, but there's a large socket carved into the face of the door.","line:0925fa1":"The door remains shut.","line:0ea96e6":"The [C0]Fused Tablet[/C0] clicks into place and the door rumbles before sliding aside.","line:02371b8":"\\[Step inside.\\]","line:09d1a1d":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:05b5f43":"You step through the doorway of the [C0]Ancient Lighthouse[/C0]. The stairway to the top has collapsed - this is as far as you're going to get.","line:0556645":"Around you are a number of dusty objects. Some of them look valuable.","line:03074ce":"The room is empty. You turn around and leave.","line:04aebdc":"You take everything from the room.","line:09a43f7":"You take what you can and leave.","line:08607cf":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: In the meantime...do you have any trinkets for me to appraise?","line:02b0503":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Excellent! Lets see what you have.","line:0e1ee9e":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: It opened a door in that ruined lighthouse? Yes, that makes sense... Well, I hope you found some interesting items for me to take a look at!","line:04f5ac3":"Next to the dock is a derelict campsite. Strange symbols are scratched into the sand. What do you want to do?","line:01a8c53":"What do you want to do?","line:038f47f":"\\[Search the campsite.\\]","line:00ee3f5":"\\[Inspect the symbols in the sand.\\]","line:002b134":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0892fae":"An extremely rough and worn sheet of fabric is collapsed at the base of some wooden supports. There's nothing remarkable about it.","line:026311b":"The symbols span the breadth of the camp, twisting this way and that. Some are grouped together into what must be words.","line:0071ede":"Fresh footprints tread carefully around each symbol. The last symbol trails off hurriedly and looks unfinished.","line:0e35ad7":"\\[Inspect the last symbol more closely.\\]","line:0fedc37":"\\[Inspect the footprints.\\]","line:0ac9b97":"\\[Go back.\\]","line:0623fc4":"There's nothing else here.","line:060e6b0":"A glint of metal shines up through the sand.","line:0f0feb8":"You leave it alone for now.","line:04f7c79":"You take it for yourself.","line:0aa9ba2":"Whoever left the footprints was barefoot. The prints are large and wide, perhaps indicating they were left by a man - but you don't know much about footprints.","line:0e786de":"In the dim light of the cave you can make out some paintings on both walls.","line:031c6b2":"\\[Check the left wall.\\]","line:0f00fc2":"\\[Check the right wall.\\]","line:0de6905":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0492f3c":"These paintings depict the birth of a civilization. A great beacon of light is shown repelling a tentacled figure emerging from the sea.","line:03fdf7b":"These paintings depict the fall of a civilization. A volcanic eruption tears through a tall lighthouse. Monstrous shapes devour people as buildings turn to ruin.","line:0e4b392":"I want to ask about the wider region.","line:0e66e75":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Certainly. Is there somewhere in particular you wish to know more about?","line:023021e":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Is there another area you'd like to discuss?","line:0f6f4dd":"Blackstone Isle.","line:0a1d450":"Gale Cliffs.","line:000fffb":"Stellar Basin.","line:060118e":"Twisted Strand.","line:08c2e91":"Devil's Spine.","line:0d3bb09":"That's all for now.","line:02f0710":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Hmm, I don't know a great deal. It technically falls under the jurisdiction of Little Marrow. I believe it was sold to a private owner some twenty years ago.","line:09b635c":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: They must've had a special arrangement - such a sale is quite uncommon. Very complicated paperwork involved, you see.","line:0a1b1e4":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I've not met the owner; I suspect they don't live around here. The island seems quite uninhabited.","line:0f32d29":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Well, the main port over there is a place called [C0]Ingfell[/C0]. It's right on the approach to the cliffs, you can't miss it.","line:0545e25":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: It's a whaling town, but I haven't heard much talk of it these days. I think quite a few people have left, one way or another.","line:04bf3cb":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Quite a popular tourist destination. There's a resort on the atoll, built on top of a [C0]beautiful coral reef[C0].","line:05dedfa":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I'm sure there's a wide variety of fish there. Maybe you fancy getting your hooks into some of those?","line:057dd22":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Hmm, I don't think there's much to tell. It's just a tangled mass of trees.","line:092eaef":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: It's often blanketed in a thick fog, even during the day. You'd want some [C0]good lights[/C0] and a [C0]good sense of direction[/C0] if you're to go exploring there.","line:08099c0":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Ah yes, it's quite exciting really. An active volcano amongst a city of ancient ruins!","line:0a92970":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: [C2]I must caution against sailing there, however[/C2]. The ruins lie low in the water and would surely tear through your hull.","line:0c58fa4":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Not to mention the aforementioned volcano could erupt at any moment! You can occasionally hear it rumbling from here.","line:09ead74":"Who lives on Blackstone Isle?","line:0c8403f":"What's with the fog around here?","line:095b6c1":"Have you seen anything significant from the lighthouse recently?","line:0182f9a":"I've been finding relics for the Collector.","line:0e1cfdf":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: I see a lot from up here, you know. I saw that ill-fated boat return. I chose to look the other way.","line:001296d":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: I watched an unnatural glow flicker through those windows. Whatever you've got planned, I hope you know what you're doing out there.","line:0933823":"Do you ever process shipments for Blackstone Isle?","line:00aa3d7":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: That old ruin? Doubt it. Uh, let's see.","line:0a0cad0":"He flicks through a large log book. It appears to be a record of shipping manifests.","line:0273ede":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Thought so. It doesn't even have a shipping address. As far as I know, nobody lives there.","line:075a2aa":"What do you know about Gale Cliffs?","line:06bbdc5":"What do you think of Stellar Basin?","line:06150c8":"What can you tell me about Twisted Strand?","line:01f8b99":"What was this place?","line:068bc9f":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Well there's [C0]Ingfell[/C0] just across the bay, which is a dreary little whaling town. The folks there are always in need of something, which keeps me in business.","line:04a6b6f":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: The residents are always talking about the cliffs. Most seem afraid. Frankly, I'm not sure why they stay.","line:068f693":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Occasionally I hear deep rumblings from within the rocks. I don't hang around here for long.","line:0fe5be5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: What beautiful, crystalline water! It's a shame I can't take my boat too much further in - I've run aground on the coral a few times.","line:0b9478c":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Have you checked out the abandoned resort to the [C0]East[/C0]? It's pretty impressive. There's probably some decent salvage to be had there.","line:0048a67":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: It's kind of amazing how quickly it all falls to ruin without people around to maintain it. In a few years, these pontoons will probably go the same way.","line:0b0e27b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's just the way of things, I guess.","line:09fcd80":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Not much, to be honest. I've gone inside just the once. I sailed into that lagoon behind us and saw I could go left, right, or straight ahead.","line:0a6ad46":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Something about the place seemed off. Through the fog, it looked like the trees were...[C3]moving[/C3]. I can't explain it. I turned around and sailed right back out.","line:07d11db":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I sometimes use this spot to rest up for a few days - the sunrises are particularly striking through the haze. Never do any regular business here of course.","line:0bc9ca4":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Some kind of ancient civilization must've lived here. Judging by the state of the buildings, things didn't go so well for them.","line:05bff9d":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I can't imagine they built all this around an active volcano. So the volcano must've become active some time after they founded their city.","line:06702a8":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I'd guess that the volcano caused them to leave - or wiped them out, one way or another.","line:05659a5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: All in all, it's a pretty inhospitable place. I'm not really sure why I come here.","line:0b142c1":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Nobody knows. It's changed recently. It lingers in the mornings now, where before...it didn't seem to have the strength.","line:08eedb9":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Even in the midday sun I feel it. A malice concealed in shadows, waiting for night to sweep the island.","line:0024439":"She glances up at the lighthouse.","line:0164f49":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: If this light should ever falter...then gods help us.","line:0ec0c59":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: The fog...it's behaving...it's as though it's reacting to the lights that cut through it. It swirls and crashes against the edges.","line:01a6ebb":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: From the top of the lighthouse I can see [C3]dark figures seething in the thickest tracts[/C3], out beyond [C0]Little Marrow[/C0] where the lights dwindle.","line:0e39b3c":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Of all that I've seen, your lights seem to anger them the most.","line:0bb355b":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: [C3]Relics[/C3]? [C3]Collector[/C3]? I'm not sure what you're hoping to achieve with this...character.","line:0c79d87":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Do you even know? Have you stopped to consider it?","line:0e28301":":On the other side of the table you find a hastily scrawled note. It reads: \"[C0]Not safe. Expect retaliation imminently. Evacuating to fort.[/C0]\"","line:0776d94":"Something extremely large and powerful created these holes. You slowly reach your arm into one...","line:0d694d2":"You can barely hear their rasping whisper above the wind and waves.","line:0b33bdc":"HOODED_FIGURE_1_NAME_KEY: Fulfill...the hunger.","line:0d9230c":"The hooded figure unfurls an old paper scroll. They point to a shape shown at the top. It appears to be a [C0]Blue Mackerel[/C0].","line:0d81e2b":"With expert precision they plunge their hands through the gullet of the fish and tear out the heart. They stuff it into their mouth unceremoniously.","line:02394d9":"HOODED_FIGURE_1_NAME_KEY: More. Still...empty.","line:0e3adf3":"They point to another shape on a second scroll. This one looks like a [C0]Tiger Mackerel[/C0].","line:0365ce6":"Again they rip into the flesh of the fish, drawing out its heart. It's consumed as quickly as the first.","line:0da6f14":"HOODED_FIGURE_1_NAME_KEY: Almost. Fulfilled.","line:02b5ba0":"They point to a fish on the final scroll. This one is a [C0]Snake Mackerel[/C0].","line:0feb0b9":"The fish has barely left your hands before splintered nails begin peeling at its scales. The heart is extracted and devoured.","line:08d3e1d":"Their head tilts upward to look at you. They take a [C1]Book[/C1] from inside their robe and hand it over.","line:0443ad5":"HOODED_FIGURE_1_NAME_KEY: Hunger...sated. Now...I wait.","line:03e6641":"They cross their arms and appear to fall into a deep sleep.","line:0c12304":"You watch from a distance for some time but see no movement. You turn around and leave quietly.","line:0a72279":"You approach a hooded figure. Dirty gold robes obscure all features except for a pair of withered and blackened hands.","line:04da3c4":"HOODED_FIGURE_2_NAME_KEY: Fisherman...deep. Calls. Respond.","line:0bc9016":"Their voice gurgles with the sound of fluid in their lungs.","line:01846f1":"HOODED_FIGURE_2_NAME_KEY: An answer...","line:0235f83":"The hooded figure holds out a scroll. They tap at a shape depicted. It looks like a [C0]Red Snapper[/C0].","line:07f1b63":"They rip through the throat of the fish and tear out its heart. It's in their mouth before you have time to process what you just saw.","line:012e649":"HOODED_FIGURE_2_NAME_KEY: Another. A sacrifice.","line:0d25ad3":"They point at another shape on a scroll. This one looks like a [C0]Fangtooth[/C0].","line:0b6b417":"They bring this small fish up to their mouth and bite at where the heart is. Their cracked lips part to reveal a row of sharpened teeth.","line:0be8d8f":"HOODED_FIGURE_2_NAME_KEY: Sense...an opening.","line:000b350":"They unfurl the final scroll. This one shows a [C0]Blue Crab[/C0].","line:0aefbaa":"They crack and bend the crab's legs apart and feast on the flesh inside.","line:089dbf0":"Lips still covered in crab flesh, they take a [C1]Book[/C1] from inside their robe and hand it to you.","line:0e29437":"HOODED_FIGURE_2_NAME_KEY: Answer...given. We await. Summons.","line:042e65f":"They cross their arms and appear to fall into a deep sleep.","line:0e2fedc":"Something's wrong. The hooded figure is slumped, long robes billowing violently.","line:0eda799":"You watch from a distance for some time but see no movement. You turn around and leave quietly.","line:07b4dfc":"You approach a hooded figure. Deep violet robes mask their face completely.","line:0e9e80f":"HOODED_FIGURE_3_NAME_KEY: Fisherman...feed...","line:01fe320":"The person appears to forget the rest of what they were about to say.","line:0cd31a8":"HOODED_FIGURE_3_NAME_KEY: Feed. The mouth.","line:01d5b90":"The hooded figure reveals a scroll. They gesture to a picture shown at the top. It's a [C0]Tarpon[/C0].","line:0eee4b5":"They hold the fish in front of their face, studying it with a tightening grip. After a few seconds, the fish collapses in on itself under the pressure.","line:0941ca9":"The figure looks through the gory mess and picks out the heart, placing it onto their tongue.","line:0e4ddd6":"HOODED_FIGURE_3_NAME_KEY: Sustain. The mind.","line:0245c22":"They show you another scroll. This one shows a [C0]Horseshoe Crab[/C0].","line:0f55943":"The figure turns the crab over to expose its soft underbelly. They scoop out its innards with sharp fingernails, consuming them blindly.","line:099ebf1":"HOODED_FIGURE_3_NAME_KEY: Consume. The sky.","line:05c72bb":"The figure slowly reveals the final scroll. This one holds a picture of a [C0]Barreleye[/C0].","line:04a19c1":"The figure begins to consume the fish head first, gnashing teeth searching for the heart of the thing. When the fish is halfway gone, they stop and throw it aside.","line:0184bf3":"They take a [C1]Book[/C1] from inside their robe and give it to you.","line:0a277d6":"HOODED_FIGURE_3_NAME_KEY: Sky. Will fall.","line:0d6eee4":"They cross their arms and appear to fall into a deep sleep.","line:04976c1":"Something seems off. The hooded figure is slumped, long robes billowing violently.","line:0ad7ef6":"You watch from a distance for some time but see no movement. You turn around and leave quietly.","line:0b3368d":"You approach a hooded figure. They are standing expectantly, vermillion red robes blowing in the wind.","line:0692758":"HOODED_FIGURE_4_NAME_KEY: Fisherman. Serve.","line:05d66b0":"The voice from the hood cuts through the humid air.","line:0f65741":"HOODED_FIGURE_4_NAME_KEY: Deliver the vessel.","line:021b875":"The hooded figure produces an old paper scroll. They point at a shape on it - a [C0]Cusk Eel[/C0].","line:08df11e":"The figure draws a ceremonial knife from their robe and slices into the fish, cutting out the heart. They place it on a stand in front of them.","line:07c70b6":"HOODED_FIGURE_4_NAME_KEY: Bring down the sky.","line:049437f":"Another shape on a scroll. This one looks like a [C0]Sailfish[/C0].","line:03a61c4":"The ceremonial knife comes out again, and the large heart is extracted. It's placed on a stand beside the first.","line:08b6c0f":"HOODED_FIGURE_4_NAME_KEY: Raise the deep.","line:061ec8e":"The figure points to a shape on the last scroll. This one is a [C0]Frilled Shark[/C0].","line:0b013af":"They drag the shark's body around to find the right angle before plunging the knife in and pulling out the heart. They place it on a stand beside the others.","line:0bfa052":"Without looking at you, they take a [C1]Book[/C1] from inside their robe and throw it into the sand at your feet.","line:0a69583":"The figure kneels before the fish hearts and becomes still. You leave before they decide they need any more hearts.","line:0ec437d":"Something seems off. The hooded figure is slumped, long robes billowing violently.","line:0e1c641":"You watch from a distance for some time but see no movement. You turn around and leave quietly.","line:0fdce12":"An altar breaks through the waves at the base of the cliff. [C0]Three crab-like creatures[/C0] are carved into it. The largest is covered in rocks and other strange shapes.","line:0cc173c":"The three crabs shudder, legs clicking into strange angles. Though long-dead, some unseen power commands their corpses into action.","line:008fb04":"The crabs scuttle over the altar, disappearing into cracks in the stone. Suddenly the rock splits in two, revealing a sunken chamber at its core.","line:0bd4409":"Which statue do you want to look at?","line:0391638":"Left.","line:0e9621c":"Middle.","line:08d52e5":"Right.","line:04be9a2":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:09ab612":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: Hey, thanks again for helping me move out here. I've managed to get myself set up now.","line:04b8b5a":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: If you ever need to use the dock or [C0]store[/C0] stuff here, be my guest.","line:03ca267":"You pull up to a wreck with a familiar looking hull. It's almost identical to the ship given to you by the Mayor - except this one has a huge breach in one side.","line:068aefb":"You're tied up alongside the old wreck.","line:0006c05":"Look in the cabin.","line:0410aa3":"Check out the cargo.","line:0483f62":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:08ef796":"You're in the cabin.","line:0bb74b5":"Look in the cupboards and drawers.","line:09fecba":"Try to find a loose floorboard.","line:000afd9":"Check the overhead electrical equipment.","line:02555c8":"\\[Go back.\\]","line:0b5c373":"The cupboards have been completely and methodically emptied. All the drawers are missing.","line:0a49c7f":"There aren't even any floorboards left.","line:0ba7204":"You've already looked over the equipment pretty thoroughly.","line:020ad3c":"The equipment is all still there, though surely exposure to the elements has fried the internals. You angle the overhead radio down to get a closer look.","line:0f87d33":"A [C1]note[/C1] slips off the top. You put it in your pocket to read later.","line:0550e76":"You've already emptied the cargohold.","line:005b543":"You poke through the cargohold. A few items remain, not yet lost to the sea.","line:0cc936a":"You take out the watch. Its once frozen hands are now inexplicably twitching in a rhythmic struggle, trying but failing to move forwards. You place it in front of the Collector.","line:095999a":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Though it has been some decades since I last laid eyes upon this...the sound of its mechanisms has grown no less unpleasant.","line:03fb43a":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Nevertheless. A reward is owed.","line:0e684ab":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Now...with these [C3]five relics[/C3] in our possession...only one thing remains.","line:005e3d3":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We will see her again soon. It will all be worth it. You know this.","line:0610a0d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: I suspect you know by now.","line:0ab3704":"I know.","line:0e026f2":"Know what?","line:05adfe6":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: It will become apparent soon enough.","line:0d2ff6a":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We must make one final voyage. This time, I will be with you.","line:081ddbe":"I'm ready.","line:00b3883":"[C2]WARNING[/C2] - you are entering the final phase of the game. Your progress will not be saved from this point onwards. Do you wish to continue?","line:085e387":"Yes.","line:0c4d1cc":"[C2]WARNING[/C2] - one more time. Your progress will not be saved from this point onwards. Are you sure you wish to continue?","line:09b7b83":"Yes.","line:070317b":"No.","line:092d255":"No.","line:0d96fc3":"I need some time to prepare.","line:07d222d":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Now. Our destination is the open expanse to the [C0]West[/C0] of [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0]. It's marked on the [C0]Map[/C0].","line:0e318bd":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: We [C2]must not tarry[/C2] on the open waters, not with such a significant cargo. Make haste!","line:0e9abb0":"The Collector is aboard your vessel.","line:0098bce":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: So be it. Return when you are prepared.","line:05f84d1":"I'm ready.","line:0621b3e":"[C2]REMINDER[/C2] - your game will not be saved at this dock.","line:0e10e24":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: There's no time for this. We must get back out to sea immediately. [C0]West[/C0] of [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0] - that's where we must go.","line:00c9d0c":"I'm ready. Show me where I need to go.","line:03324dc":"I should go.","line:0edba1c":"I have the book.","line:0875902":"I should go.","line:087db58":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: You have to move on. For her sake as well as yours. Take control...be rid of that thing once and for all.","line:03f0352":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: You've had it this whole time, have you not? It doesn't matter. Make the most of this window of lucidity. Now is the time to act.","line:087cf6c":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Do you still remember where it happened? In that gloomy darkness behind the bay. When you are ready, I'll point the way.","line:0d83cb1":"I'm ready.","line:00f8f8f":"I need time to prepare.","line:0353a96":"[C2]WARNING[/C2] - you are entering the final phase of the game. Your progress will not be saved from this point onwards. Do you wish to continue?","line:04b8974":"Yes.","line:0988604":"[C2]WARNING[/C2] - one more time. Your progress will not be saved from this point onwards. Are you sure you wish to continue?","line:0393139":"Yes.","line:0dd2a4a":"No.","line:09a9327":"No.","line:0360386":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: We must wait until night is thickest. Until the ocean is as it was...all those years ago.","line:0f3cb5b":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: I understand. Do what you must. But do not delay this any longer than is necessary.","line:0ddaf07":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Return to me when you can. I will point the way.","line:084dd61":"There's nobody here.","line:067f9d9":"Nothing, I'll be going.","line:0cc7e45":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: The relics are coming with us. We should wait for the fog to thicken. With luck, the seas will remain unaware of our intentions...","line:0cb96af":"His shape disappears from the mirror. A chill rises in your body as you turn to leave. The Collector is with you.","line:0ea858c":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: This is the place.","line:0baa0a5":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: This is where she was taken from us...and where we can at last bring her back.","line:022cd30":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Only here. And only because of what we've achieved.","line:005429c":"He opens the book and begins to read aloud.","line:0c26b97":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: To release a lost one, frozen in time...","line:01737f3":"He throws the [C3]pocket watch[/C3] overboard.","line:0621a1b":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: ...and tethered by chains in the deep...","line:02f97b8":"He throws the [C3]necklace[/C3] overboard.","line:0d98523":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: ...bind them to this world once more.","line:025f90d":"He throws the [C3]ring[/C3] overboard.","line:0882b50":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: Open the door to the starry heavens...","line:097b863":"He slots the [C3]key[/C3] into the lock of the [C3]music box[/C3].","line:036f3d4":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: ...and lay the weary world to rest.","line:07555b3":"He throws the [C3]music box[/C3] overboard, its [C3]key[/C3] left unturned.","line:03883d7":"You open the book. Its pages are frosted with ice and a chill mist rises around your fingers. You begin to read aloud.","line:0e4a243":"PLAYER_NAME_KEY: To release a lost one, frozen in time...","line:09d5dae":"You throw the [C3]pocket watch[/C3] overboard.","line:0559f2d":"PLAYER_NAME_KEY: ...and tethered by chains in the deep...","line:0d30aac":"You throw the [C3]necklace[/C3] overboard.","line:005328e":"PLAYER_NAME_KEY: ...bind them to this world once more.","line:07e1f67":"You throw the [C3]ring[/C3] overboard.","line:097b165":"PLAYER_NAME_KEY: Open the door to the starry heavens...","line:0d6e57c":"You slot the [C3]key[/C3] into the lock of the [C3]music box[/C3].","line:09b4cc0":"PLAYER_NAME_KEY: ...and lay the weary world to rest.","line:0685d1c":"You throw the [C3]music box[/C3] overboard, its [C3]key[/C3] left unturned.","line:00c7660":"This is the place.","line:0037d32":"Throw it back.","line:0e8fbb1":"The book struggles in your grasp, its weight somehow shifting from side to side. Silver ribbons flail pathetically against your fingers.","line:0ac19f4":"Throw it back.","line:0da381b":"You hold it high above your head. A low groan rumbles from the book, echoed by another from the depths.","line:09f9508":"Throw it back.","line:075b7a3":"You throw it into the foaming water.","line:06affe5":"Tell me more about that book of yours.","line:06e49d4":"[C2]REMINDER[/C2] - your game will not be saved at this dock.","line:0bb389f":"The Lighthouse Keeper is guiding you out to sea - the lighthouse beam is focused on a dark patch of water [C0]West[/C0] of [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0].","line:0c38be1":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: It's time. I'll point the way.","line:04f4454":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: [C0]Follow my light[/C0].","line:03b60d2":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Hmm. Haven't seen that [C3]strange red light[/C3] in a while. Wonder what it was.","line:07cafd6":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Have you seen that [C3]strange red light[/C3] at night? It seemed to be rising from the [C0]West[/C0].","line:01d1251":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: If you're ever hunting for specific species, check your [C0]encyclopedia[/C0]. It could have the information you need.","line:0bc0fc8":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Some fish prefer [C0]deeper[/C0] water, while others stick to the [C0]shallows[/C0]. If you're looking for something specific, it's important to know what [C0]depth[/C0] you're working with.","line:0f5e53d":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: That [C3]crimson glow in the sky[/C3] seems to have gone away. The air feels quieter now...more settled. Have you noticed?","line:0b592bb":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: The skies were lit up with a weird [C3]crimson glow[/C3] the other night...did you see it?","line:00c84be":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Around the back though...it's a little harder to get to. There are still some [C0]wrecks[/C0] towards the [C3]deeper patches[/C3]...you'll want to avoid that area.","line:00eb191":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Some nights you can see an...[C3]unnatural glow[/C3] rising from that patch of dark water. I can't imagine what's down there in the deep...","line:0a1033b":"Do you know how I could clear the debris around here?","line:09f957f":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: It patrols the passageways of the cliffs, but it's lair is somewhere towards the center, [C0]by the large waterfall[/C0].","line:0cd4a0f":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: I've marked the area on your map. Perhaps you could look there for it...but if it's too troublesome, don't worry about it.","line:08359fb":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Hmm, you'd probably need some explosives to shift those rocks. My brother at [C0]Ingfell[/C0] used to make explosives...","line:04e96eb":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: For the whaling operations, you see. Nasty stuff. But with the whales all gone...I can't imagine he's still in business.","line:03565e8":"I heard you used to make explosives.","line:0205c22":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Aye, I did. Sometimes the carcasses needed breaking up. It wasn't the most efficient...or the more pleasant, but it got the job done.","line:0857b96":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: I've been thinking about getting back into it - I might be able to rustle up something strong enough to [C0]clear those debris piles[/C0] in the cliffs...","line:0d49fb7":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Ah...but I'm not sure. I don't have the energy these days.","line:0c842a0":"I'd have a use for some explosives like that.","line:08c6b51":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Alright, I'll think on it some more. But I make no promises.","line:0f5b500":"I see.","line:0f24813":"An old man emerges from one of the nearby broken buildings and hobbles towards you.","line:01ce463":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Oh, ah, greetings! Don't get many visitors around here...what is it that you need?","line:0cb4f14":"A rotten chest sits atop a pile of rubble at the back of the cave.","line:0650928":"Look inside.","line:0df53da":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0b188c4":"A rotting chest peeks out from the skeleton of a wrecked ship.","line:063c228":"Look inside.","line:0798f09":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:073d3f6":"A small structure sits on the island. Nearby is an abandoned campfire. What do you want to do?","line:0618ccb":"What do you want to do?","line:00b9f62":"\\[Examine the structure.\\]","line:0d106e1":"\\[Check the campfire.\\]","line:0afcc35":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0fc1c86":"An old stone structure is built around a statue. The statue has its arms raised towards the lighthouse at Devil's Spine.","line:06c444a":"Whether it gestures in fear or praise, you cannot tell.","line:0d2f8de":"The campfire itself is unremarkable, but you wonder who would choose an island such as this to make camp.","line:0bce5d4":"Nearby, you spot a piece of paper flapping in a bush. A [C0]note[/C0] is written on it. You put it in your pocket to read later.","line:0199ea1":"The stone columns of the temple are carved with ancient pictures and text. Which carving do you want to look at?","line:06f5c8e":"The swarm of small creatures.","line:0c31346":"The large eyeless beast.","line:02c0bfd":"The bubbling vent.","line:02f81a3":"The carving shows a bubbling underwater vent. \"The breath of salvation. It burns those that mean harm. Only the pure remain.\"","line:020efff":"Beneath these words, somebody has added a crudely scratched note. \"[C0]Protection. Follow the magma. Find them. [/C0]\"","line:0fd890a":"The carving shows a swarm of small fish surrounding a boat. \"The ravenous children. Alone they are nothing. Together they summon her.\"","line:01cd3d6":"Beneath these words, somebody has added a crudely scratched note. \"[C0]Do not let them grip you. Burn them away.[/C0]\"","line:022f215":"The carving is of a large fish with crossed-out eyes. \"The unseeing mother. When the starving cannot eat, she approaches.\"","line:005d501":"Beneath these words, somebody has added a crudely scratched note. \"[C0]Blind but can hear her children. Avoid at all costs.[/C0]\"","line:02c96f8":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:086f6d9":"COLLECTOR_NAME_KEY: But all the same, they must be found. I never said this would be easy. I suppose we'll see if you have what it takes, soon enough.","line:0df48f1":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: That's all of them...that I can remember, anyways. I can't picture their faces too clearly any more.","line:0262ae4":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Make sure you're getting enough [C0]rest[/C0]. Tired eyes won't fare well in these waters.","line:0a5c1ad":"FISHMONGER_NAME_KEY: Don't let yourself get too worn down. We need you [C0]well-rested[/C0] to provide for this town.","line:076e596":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: You're looking a bit worse for wear. When's the last time you had a good night's [C0]sleep[/C0]?","line:05c0d45":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: I'd caution against operating a vessel if you're feeling [C0]overtired[/C0]. Your reaction times are slowed - rocks and things will seem to jump out at you.","line:0e8cf96":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Oh my, you look exhausted! You're not forgetting to get some [C0]sleep[/C0], are you?","line:07d1de2":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: As I always say: taking frequent breaks is an important part of being productive!","line:0a1a08c":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Fisherman! What is it? You look a touch troubled - is the fog starting to get to you?","line:0190ee0":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Completely normal around here, and nothing to worry about! With a good night's [C0]rest[/C0], you'll be right as rain by morning!","line:021e2e6":"The Mayor appears in front of you on the dock. His face swims before your eyes, and his words blur with the waves crashing around you.","line:0652b63":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Are ... ok? If ... see ... fog ... shapes ... [C0]rest[/C0]. Careful ... [C3]nightmares[/C3].","line:0bb1047":"You stumble past him into town.","line:0037140":"The Lighthouse Keeper emerges from the dark forest that flanks the town. She walks towards the dock with a confused look on her face.","line:068607f":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Oh...it's you.","line:0308f31":"Who were you expecting?","line:0399a6e":"Excuse me?","line:0f4fe4a":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Your engine, it sounds like...I'm sorry, I mistook it for the vessel of an old friend.","line:08fb8e7":"Dejected, she turns and walks back towards the lighthouse.","line:0416777":"The Lighthouse Keeper is waiting for you on the dock, looking displeased.","line:0ceebca":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: I saw you sailing out towards the horizon. Crossing that deep expanse. Do you really think that's wise?","line:030c501":"It was fine.","line:0668642":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Maybe this time. You need to be more careful.","line:04ebf23":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Even you, with all of your experience, cannot truly know the ocean. Nobody can.","line:02461d7":"What's the problem?","line:0d536b6":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: It feels a bit like tempting fate, does it not?","line:0328ed0":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Things are bad enough around here without your provocations.","line:0144c85":"Abruptly, she walks away. Her eyes scan the water as she walks along the dock.","line:0fab458":"The Lighthouse Keeper approaches you on the dock wearing a questioning expression.","line:07e461b":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: You must've been around most of the islands by now. Have you found whatever it is you're looking for?","line:0e5ce01":"Almost.","line:028399e":"She shifts her weight and leans hard against her staff.","line:0eaf0b8":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: How can you be so sure? The last time you thought you knew...and look what happened.","line:0b295d8":"I'm not sure.","line:0bae618":"Her face softens.","line:08d0cc3":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Remember that you are in control. If you're having doubts, it's foolish to blindly persevere. You can always look for alternative paths.","line:06b86de":"I'm just fishing.","line:0202b07":"She recoils from your flagrant lie.","line:0e0118a":"LIGHTHOUSE_KEEPER_NAME_KEY: Why do you mistrust me so? What have I done to warrant such suspicion?","line:09801ba":"She turns from you, shaking her head and muttering. She heads back towards the lighthouse.","line:08eda27":"What's wrong?","line:00de6af":"He stares ahead in silence.","line:0115da3":"Are you alright?","line:0a83f26":"He seems unable to respond.","line:095a02f":"What happened?","line:0abbd6d":"You notice his neck and overalls are covered in a dark fluid - the same dark fluid that was leaking from the package you delivered earlier.","line:0d755b8":"What was that?","line:066c969":"A trembling head turns ever so slightly towards you. His breathing grows heavy in anger until you step backwards, leaving him standing there on the dock.","line:02af842":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Woah, you don't look so great, friend. When's the last time you got a good night's [C0]sleep[/C0]?","line:0ac33fa":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Are you alright there? You're looking a little...jittery. You're free to [C0]rest[/C0] here anytime.","line:0c8c8fb":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Your hull's got a few holes that need patching. We can [C0]repair[/C0] those here, remember.","line:02e843e":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Did you run aground on rocks or something? We should make some [C0]repairs[/C0] - I can see right through your hull!","line:043dd28":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Your boat's sprung a leak! We should [C0]fix[/C0] that.","line:0ee8b87":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You should really be more careful! I don't have a limitless supply of [C0]repair[/C0] materials, you know.","line:0f3e3fa":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I suppose you're going to say you \"couldn't avoid\" the rock that \"appeared out of nowhere\"? Yeah yeah, I've heard it all before. Let's get you [C0]fixed[/C0] up.","line:074e8b1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I'm going to have to start carrying more materials soon aren't I? I've got enough to make [C0]repairs[/C0] for now, at least.","line:0b2281c":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: If you have some worn out [C0]Crab Pots[/C0] or [C0]Trawl Nets[/C0], we can fix them here.","line:0637bce":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: [C0]Trawl Net[/C0] fraying? Crabs cutting themselves out of your [C0]Crab Pots[/C0]? Why don't we [C0]fix[/C0] them up here?","line:0dc8765":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Don't forget - [C0]Crab Pots[/C0] and [C0]Trawl Nets[/C0] both need repairing every now and then.","line:06e0ced":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: [C0]Crab Pots[/C0] and [C0]Trawl Nets[/C0] won't work if they're completely worn out, so best to [C0]repair[/C0] them regularly.","line:075becc":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I'll buy all sorts of fish here - and I can pay the most for [C1]fresh[/C1] ones.","line:0975825":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Not all fish are traded equally! Smaller species can sometimes be more delicious - and more valuable - than the larger ones.","line:02a18f4":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: The most successful captains know how to push their vessels to the limit. Is yours running at peak efficiency?","line:086642b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: There's nothing wrong with combining different engine types - do anything you can to get more speed out of the space you have.","line:06eff16":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Having a variety of fishing tackle on board means you'll be prepared to catch whatever you come across.","line:0d76bc1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Installing a [C0]Trawl Net[/C0] is a great way to earn some passive income while exploring the islands.","line:0815fd5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: When [C0]Trawling[/C0], pay attention to how [C0]deep[/C0] the water is. Not every type of fish likes deep water! Check your [C0]Encyclopedia[/C0] if you're not sure.","line:0a1aee0":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: [C0]Crab Pots[/C0] can be quite profitable if you can find a good place to drop them. Just don't forget where you put them!","line:0297e75":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You'll need to pick up your [C0]Crab Pots[/C0] every now and then and bring them in for repairs.","line:0d48311":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Not every crab can be found at every [C0]depth[/C0]. When finding a spot to drop your [C0]Crab Pots[/C0], maybe check your [C0]Encyclopedia[/C0]?","line:082698a":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I hope you're being careful out there. Seeing your boat sail over puts a smile on my face every time.","line:0235a70":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You and I, we've got to avoid risks as much as we can. There's no crew to bail us out if things go south.","line:03340de":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You don't have to try to grab everything you see out there. That wreck salvage isn't going anywhere fast.","line:0f9a948":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I love the sound of rain against the roof of my cabin. Is there anything better?","line:07a3aab":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You'll need to put a few more engines on that thing if you want it to be as fast as mine, hah!","line:0ad7b3f":"Tell me more about the creature that lives in the cliffs.","line:0c75889":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: It's been burrowing tunnels through the base of the cliffs. You can see the [C0]gigantic holes[/C0] it leaves just below the surface.","line:009a4db":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: As it forces its way out, it often causes [C0]rock falls[/C0]. So if you plan on going in there...keep an ear out.","line:0ff96ee":"HERMIT_NAME_KEY: Should it catch sight of you, well, you should be able to outrun it - it's [C0]quite slow[/C0] - provided you can navigate the passageways.","line:0087a6f":"What am I supposed to be doing now?","line:0488b28":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: We're making [C0]special bait[/C0] to lure the [C3]Mind Suckers[/C3] into the [C0]traps[/C0] I've built in the lagoons.","line:0db53bb":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Once we've trapped them, I'll fire on them with the mortar. Then you'll [C0]bring back proof[/C0] that they're dead.","line:0c50852":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: When the trap springs, I'll fire upon it with the mortar. Make sure you [C0]bring back proof[/C0] that the thing's really dead, you hear?","line:0196f67":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: When the trap springs, I'll fire upon it with the mortar. Make sure you [C0]bring back proof[/C0] that the thing's really dead, you hear?","line:014ecbf":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: When the trap springs, I'll fire upon it with the mortar. Make sure you [C0]bring back proof[/C0] that the thing's really dead, you hear?","line:0f7b72d":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Here, this was left over from the other bait we made.","line:0166f35":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Did you want that leftover bait now?","line:022b7d0":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Right, now, we can make some fresh stuff if you like.","line:067fc06":"SOLDIER_NAME_KEY: Don't want it right now? Well, come back if you change your mind.","line:0e152bb":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Don't want them right now? Well, come back if you change your mind.","line:035d650":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: I hope you can put them to good use...wherever you find cause for it.","line:00ae1fb":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Did you want those explosives now? I held onto them for you.","line:0380204":"RETIRED_WHALER_NAME_KEY: Here, this is on the house - for all your help.","line:0b9d59b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You look tired. If you don't get some sleep, you'll start seeing things! Why don't you [C0]rest[/C0] up before heading back out?","line:03d6cc4":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Everything ok? You've just been standing there for a while...need to have a [C0]rest[/C0]?","line:0b50d85":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I know that look on your face. Too long on the open water, eh? Yeah, you start to feel a little mad after a while. Nothing a good [C0]sleep[/C0] won't fix.","line:0fa6bf2":"BUILDER_NAME_KEY: I found this while I was unpacking. You should take it.","line:0b15dc4":"She hands you a [C1]Book[/C1]. The cover is dusty, but in otherwise good condition.","line:0740ab1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I've got a surprise for you! A gift, for my most loyal customer. Here, I want you to have this.","line:06ca83a":"She takes a [C1]Book[/C1] from a nearby shelf and hands it to you. Flicking through it, you see page corners turned in and handwritten notes in the margins.","line:0e93674":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh, how rude of me. You've done all of this for me and...I've not got much to say thank you with. Um, you should have this.","line:04d0c6d":"She opens a drawer and pulls out a [C1]Book[/C1]. Sheepishly, she hands it to you.","line:06cc659":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: This is something I wrote during my studies. I think it'll be useful to you.","line:054a79f":"The stone trembles before you. Unknown symbols glow from within.","line:0882b6c":"\\[Place your hand on the stone.\\]","line:0bcc9c9":"A sudden chill rushes through the marrow of your bones, surging up your arm, your neck. A [C3]deep vision[/C3] enters your mind.","line:05916c9":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:07c7a96":"The stone hums quietly, sending ripples through the air around it. Faint shapes dance upon its surface, vanishing before your eyes can focus on them.","line:01c87f5":"\\[Place your hand on the stone.\\]","line:0dcd1c8":"The cold stone does not respond to your touch.","line:01468c3":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0303e7b":"The town of Greater Marrow burns. The lighthouse lies collapsed, its light extinguished.","line:023e4ac":"A red glow fills the sky behind a cyclone that drains the world.","line:08a8781":"A ship, tossed by waves in the night. Fog unfolds like a blanket from the deck, spilling across the ocean and crashing against the land.","line:09f27f3":"A distant lighthouse flickers a signal.","line:0e7c767":"Dark rocks erupt from the earth, piercing through buildings and trees. Through sand and crashing waves. Through the basalt pillars of this island.","line:0c655d4":"The newborn structures crackle with an unknown energy, crimson lightning arcing between them.","line:0d3288f":"A blustery wind screams through the cliffs, diving and turning. It passes over a large wooden ship at anchor, all flags filling suddenly.","line:00a8216":"A skinless face appears on the fluttering fabric. A wail of terror rises from the crew.","line:0b06b02":"A heart of stone wrapped in a twisting tail. A serpentine body uncoils, teeth rasping at its earthen shell.","line:0bcf448":"Larger now. Bursting through the cliffs, sending rocks tumbling into the water. An eye opens to this new world.","line:0a19ece":"A spore floats in the water, adrift in the current. Fish feast in a frenzy above, devouring its kin. The spore lands in the thick silt of the sea floor.","line:0014931":"Its roots stretch down into the seabed, growing - extending towards what lies beneath.","line:0c87117":"The green glimmer of an aurora blooms in the night sky above the resort. A distant boom shakes the thatched rooves and rouses dreamers from their sleep.","line:06b080f":"The waters withdraw, exposing the coral to the warm air. Confused creatures chitter and seek out their hiding places.","line:04ad30a":"A man flees through the trees, bloodshot eyes wide with terror. He runs into a dead end; cornered by the murky waters and his pursuer, he turns.","line:0ab203a":"A wooden spear flies and finds its mark.","line:079f8a4":"A parasite burrows into a large snakelike carcass. It feeds, growing fat and multiplying. Tendrils sprout from the head of the body and sense the water around it.","line:023decb":"The host corpse shudders reluctantly. With a cry that resounds through the forest, it rises once again.","line:0e3538c":"A leviathan raises its vast grey head, stretching up, up until it sits level with a bright flame cradled at the top of the ancient lighthouse.","line:0308c60":"It watches the fire for a while, tilting its head and calling softly to it with a guttural song.","line:0254c1a":"Appearing satisfied, the beast slinks down into the water, gliding back to the depths.","line:02236aa":"Blackness.","line:0ed8344":"A crimson rift opens in the void.","line:097794d":"Dreadful silhouettes drift through in a procession of teeth and tentacles.","line:08988b9":"After the last grotesque figure emerges, a membrane spreads over the fissure.","line:007fe01":"SHIPWRIGHT_NAME_KEY: Remember, you don't have to have all the materials at once - you can [C0]store[/C0] whatever you have right here at the [C0]dry dock[/C0].","line:0224258":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: When the sky mistakes the stars,<br>And the air grows thick with night,<br>The deep will open its scars,<br>Protect us, O guiding light.","line:063847a":"The earth shifts once more and the stones lie still.","line:0119756":"Moments later the waters return; crashing, seething, sweeping souls out to sea.","line:0b4c9f4":"A distant groan emanates from the space beyond.","line:0b58756":"After a few minutes, he puts down his pen and reads aloud.","line:00c22b8":"The workshop looks as though it hasn't been used in decades.","line:0ad14fb":"You've already taken the equipment that was stored here.","line:011a315":"Go inside.","line:0de8c5c":"You enter, taking a moment to let your eyes adjust to the dim light.","line:0f7cad0":"It's locked.","line:02e4941":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:09c0dd3":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You might be used to [C0]dry docks[/C0] at other ports, but we can make the same [C1]upgrades to your boat[/C1] here at this [C0]floating dock[/C0]. Check it out!","line:06c0d86":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: On this side of the pontoon I'll [C1]buy any fish[/C1] you want to sell. I also keep a stock of [C0]crab pots[/C0] here for sale!","line:06637e1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Most of this gear is super heavy, so I don't offload it at every pontoon. But come aboard and see what [C1]equipment I've got for sale[/C1]!","line:0ec135c":"TRADER_NAME_KEY: Remarkable...yes, I do believe this is a [C0]fragment of a larger arrangement[/C0].","line:0ddb2a3":"He reaches up to a high shelf and brings down a similar looking stone, albeit one covered with much more dust.","line:0e0e958":"You explain to the Trader that you found a use for the [C0]Fused Tablet[/C0] at the Ancient Lighthouse in Devil's Spine.","line:0ad27b2":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Thanks to the [C0]Retired Whaler[/C0] at [C0]Ingfell[/C0], I'm now carrying a small stock of [C0]Packed Explosives[/C0] - very carefully!","line:0fd76f9":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I met a guy in [C0]Twisted Strand[/C0] who bartered with some buckets of [C0]Mixed Bait[/C0]. I thought they'd be good for your fishing - why don't you take a look?","line:0b5e986":"\\[Deliver the relic.\\]","line:0959ef8":"\\[Conceal the relic.\\]","line:0cf07ad":"You climb the broken steps to the old mansion, the waves swelling and crashing against the basalt columns that surround you. You pause before crossing the threshold.","line:0553f94":"A small object rolls out from under the generator, covered in dried salt.","line:06fcc75":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: You look lost, fisherman. Are you after somewhere to sell your catch? [C0]Greater Marrow[/C0] is on the [C0]West[/C0] side of the bay.","line:023a66e":"DOCKWORKER_NAME_KEY: Keep an eye on the [C0]lighthouse[/C0], eh? Wouldn't want to lose sight of it for too long.","line:08ac465":"What do you want to do in here?","line:0c32bd4":"Pick up items.","line:055ffc9":"Customize boat.","line:0ed01b8":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0d27628":"You find some [C3]horrifying creations[/C3] amongst the detritus.","line:0256597":"Old cans of [C0]paint[/C0] and boxes of dusty [C0]boat accessories[/C0] line the shelves.","line:00c5c0a":"Paint boat.","line:082a9c7":"Change flag.","line:0fd9656":"Adjust bunting.","line:0969466":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0ef3883":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Which area do you want to paint?","line:0a43246":"Roof.","line:0300338":"Hull.","line:0ecf69f":"\\[Back.\\]","line:0769303":"Which color do you want to paint the roof?","line:083c0da":"Seaweed Green.","line:0957317":"Blue Depths.","line:0c4b2f6":"Black Abyss.","line:01e56fc":"\\[Back.\\]","line:037ae3b":"Which color do you want to paint the hull?","line:08ced27":"Seaweed Green.","line:0046243":"Blue Depths.","line:018928b":"Black Abyss.","line:04ef185":"\\[Back.\\]","line:05d231e":"New paint applied.","line:07941e3":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: As you wish...","line:0ab8718":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Which flag do you want to display?","line:0530526":"No flag.","line:0dd4029":"Hook flag.","line:0f26fe9":"Anchor flag.","line:08aed22":"Fish flag.","line:04fd345":"\\[Back.\\]","line:0846d99":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: I can adjust bunting here. I'll use any leftover pigments I have to ensure a cohesive aesthetic.","line:0914209":"Bunting off.","line:0edbd3f":"Bunting on.","line:04f4ad8":"Bunting 3.","line:0f9893e":"No bunting.","line:05ddc33":"\\[Back.\\]","line:0cf1f4d":"Which foghorn do you want to use?","line:063064f":"Regular.","line:0a71d30":"High pitched.","line:05ca751":"Low pitched.","line:049adbc":"\\[Back.\\]","line:05af5a9":"Rusty Red.","line:0466fdd":"Rusty Red.","line:00f9f4c":"\\[Next page.\\]","line:0ebf929":"Sharp Mint.","line:051c787":"Golden Treasure.","line:0e0bcde":"Royal Purple.","line:06aadb4":"Maple Orange.","line:0509ef6":"\\[Previous page.\\]","line:0e2c03d":"\\[Back.\\]","line:01b7c6c":"\\[Next page.\\]","line:0563aa7":"Sharp Mint.","line:0774725":"Golden Treasure.","line:0692291":"Royal Purple.","line:07e84ab":"Maple Orange.","line:062a122":"\\[Previous page.\\]","line:03f37d3":"\\[Back.\\]","line:0f9e0dd":"\\[Next page.\\]","line:056bb84":"Pirate flag.","line:01d4a34":"Eye flag.","line:0824566":"Sea serpent flag.","line:048fbac":"Ouroboros flag.","line:0f9ae17":"\\[Previous page.\\]","line:0591391":"\\[Back.\\]","line:0665fb0":"Which color do you want to paint the roof?","line:0a1ecaf":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: What color do you want to paint the [C0]hull[/C0]?","line:0fb4ef0":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Which flag do you want to display?","line:0c785fc":"A collection of cases have washed up against the shore. Some have already split open and lost their contents to the waves.","line:02556d0":"Look for valuables.","line:0d455dc":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0a51d7b":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Ahem...Hello. Sorry, would you step out of the way for a moment? You're in my shot.","line:01e07f7":"You move to the side. A few seconds later, the Photographer sighs in exasperation and mutters to herself.","line:036d38c":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: No, this simply won't do!","line:03700b3":"What's the matter?","line:0569a06":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:02170e4":"You leave before she asks you to do anything else.","line:025353b":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: The angle of this lens is all wrong! I'll never get a close-up shot of anything with this. And the others...I fear they were lost overboard.","line:0ddc6ae":"She sighs again and looks off to the [C0]West[/C0].","line:0284e47":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I was sailing from [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0] you see, squeezing my boat though a [C0]narrow gap between two islands[/C0] - and then I crashed into some coral.","line:039738d":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I thought I heard something in the water behind me, so I dared not stop. If you were able to [C0]retrieve the lenses[/C0] for me, ah, let me see...","line:0f5b57b":"She rummages through what few belongings survived the trip.","line:0ad894f":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I have a spare [C1]camera[/C1] here that I won't need. You're welcome to it - if you can [C0]find those lenses[/C0].","line:01683c9":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: You have the lenses! Oh, I do hope they've not been damaged by the seawater...","line:09f39f2":"She takes the case from you and inspects each lens carefully.","line:09eb1a7":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: They seem mostly unharmed - nothing that some careful polishing can't remedy, at least.","line:0a833b4":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: As promised, you should take my spare [C1]camera[/C1]. The lens is nothing special, but it should allow you to capture some good shots.","line:007d6a4":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: If you wanted some advice on locating wildlife to photograph, just say the word!","line:0ce7083":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Good day, fisherman. Are you interested in learning about the local wildlife?","line:061774f":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:0c49a11":"What did you want me to do again?","line:0afc8d9":"Tell me about large fish.","line:03252b9":"Tell me about mammals.","line:002fddc":"Tell me about birds.","line:016c4a4":"Tell me about reptiles.","line:01771da":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:08d5fcf":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I suspect you're more knowledgeable in this particular area than I am!","line:0ee4f93":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: There are a few shark species around, most notably the huge [C0]Whale Shark[/C0]. They tend to prefer the warmer waters around [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0].","line:0657ee6":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: They're completely harmless, as I'm sure you know, but do be careful around them. You wouldn't want your propellors causing them any injury.","line:0f57986":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: While still relatively scarce, I believe a few Cetaceans - that's Whales and such - can be found in the deeper waters around here.","line:0faf7c8":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: You might be lucky enough to spot a pod of [C0]Bottlenose Dolphins[/C0] or [C0]Killer Whales[/C0] - they've been known to swim alongside boats.","line:07c48c8":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: As for the larger Whales, I've heard [C0]Humpbacks[/C0], [C0]Sperm Whales[/C0] and even the odd [C0]Blue Whale[/C0] have been sighted in the area.","line:047f4bf":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: It doesn't surprise me to hear that their numbers have dwindled, what with Ingfell's Whaling endeavours. Hopefully their populations will recover, in time.","line:0b10fce":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: You'll hear quite a wide variety of birdsong from the islands, though I suspect they're all too small to spot from your boat.","line:04824ba":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: There's sure to be a few larger species - [C0]Gulls[/C0] and [C0]Ravens[/C0] - loitering around the more active docks looking for morsels of food.","line:0959284":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: The ruins in [C0]Devil's Spine[/C0] host a few breeding pairs of [C0]Sea Hawks[/C0]. You're bound to hear them calling to each other, though they're quite elusive.","line:02fc48d":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I'm glad you asked! Not many consider reptiles when they think of the ocean.","line:0c0d6ca":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: [C0]Loggerhead Turtles[/C0] are a common sight in the temperate waters around [C0]The Marrows[/C0] and [C0]Gale Cliffs[/C0], though they can be hard to spot in the water.","line:09cfb5f":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: When it comes to larger reptiles, they don't get any bigger than [C0]Salt Water Crocodiles[/C0]. The mangroves of [C0]Twisted Strand[/C0] are the perfect environment for them.","line:0aaf3fc":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: You were going to try to [C0]find my case of extra lenses[/C0]. It must've fallen overboard when I hit some coral to the [C0]West[/C0], towards [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0].","line:0262ccd":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I'll mark on your map where I think I lost them.","line:0919e81":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Good day, fisherman. How can I help you?","line:08ac003":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: Fisherman! Have you run into a [C0]Photographer[/C0] on your travels? She docked here a few days ago for supplies.","line:0b027fb":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: I suggested that she take some pictures of the town - for promotional purposes - but she didn't seem too interested.","line:003d125":"MAYOR_NAME_KEY: She mentioned she was heading [C0]South[/C0] - perhaps you should introduce yourself.","line:0468dd7":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Say, have you met the [C0]Photographer[/C0]? She stopped by my pontoon a little while back.","line:0378800":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: She's loaded up with fancy camera equipment to take pictures of all the wildlife.","line:0215365":"She sighs wistfully.","line:0b089f1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I wish I had my own [C1]camera[/C1]. Wouldn't it be nice to be able to document everything you do? You'd never forget anything...","line:0fe351b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Anyway, she said she was setting up on a small island to the [C0]South[/C0] of [C0]The Marrows[/C0]. If you're in the area, maybe you could check on her.","line:0c88abb":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: What can I help you with today?","line:0c200a4":"\\[Back.\\]","line:07aa6cb":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: What color do you want to paint the [C0]roof[/C0]?","line:0c6dad2":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Alright, now let me prepare my brushes...","line:0001e01":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Mmm, much better. That color looks good.","line:08add0d":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: I don't have the right pigment to make that color. You'll need to bring me these [C3]crabs[/C3]:","line:03949a5":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: A different color, perhaps?","line:05e56b6":"Deliver Flag.","line:059dc76":"Deliver Flag.","line:09dffaf":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: As you wish...","line:0a67ffb":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: So, you've found a scrap of fabric eh? Let me see...","line:0d160cf":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: A unique design. Do you want to attach it now?","line:0fc6f52":"Yes.","line:075f7ba":"No.","line:078f808":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: You don't seem to have any new flags with you. Come back when you find some.","line:0058363":"Sharp Mint.","line:018a747":"Maple Orange.","line:0ecdf4a":"Royal Purple.","line:05b50a3":"Golden Treasure.","line:017a9d2":"Black Abyss.","line:04e7b03":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Ah, the fisherman...I had thought you might stop by. Welcome to my humble studio.","line:064bd43":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: If you're wanting to...experiment with some decorations...yes, I'm the person to talk to.","line:0da5798":"What sort of decorations?","line:003b528":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: I can attach [C0]flags[/C0] and [C0]bunting[/C0] to add some style to your boat. I have a design here already that you might like.","line:0922039":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: If you [C0]find any others[/C0] on your travels, [C0]bring them back to me[/C0] and I can rig them up for you.","line:0899e7b":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Of course, I can also add a splash of [C0]colour[/C0] to your hull. I'm sorry to say that [C2]my selection of pigments limited at the moment[/C2], though...","line:01600ad":"Could I help find more pigments?","line:0690647":"\\[Back.\\]","line:014ce2b":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Hmm...","line:09ddffc":"He thinks for a short while.","line:02135c7":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: The other day, down by the shoreline, I saw a [C3]strange crab[/C3] with the most strikingly vibrant coloration.","line:0b2385e":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: My knees aren't suited to clambering over rocks and chasing crustaceans, you see, but if you caught such a creature...","line:09eb2c2":"He clears scraps of cloth and paper from his workbench, revealing a large pestle & mortar.","line:06e52f3":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: With the right binding agent...we can grind them together for a new mixture...","line:010ed0b":"He turns back to you, a cunning plan formed in his mind.","line:04ed5ec":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Fisherman. Bring me some of those [C3]strange crabs[/C3]. We'll turn your vessel into a work of art!","line:0a280f8":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Yes, of course. As I mentioned previously, if you're able to [C3]bring me crabs of the most unusual colors[/C3], we can grind them up for their pigment.","line:0b2844b":"What do you do here?","line:03c9fd7":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: That should be all we need...let me grind them together...","line:0d0ad00":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: That flag's been taken down for you now.","line:0485378":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Okay, I've removed the bunting for now.","line:09994bf":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: But, ah, for now...","line:04c240d":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Have you tried searching to the [C0]North[/C0] of [C0]The Marrows[/C0]?","line:08f58e6":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Have you tried searching to the [C0]South[/C0] of [C0]The Marrows[/C0]?","line:08a461c":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Have you tried searching around [C0]Gale Cliffs[/C0]?","line:03c25cd":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Have you tried searching around [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0]?","line:0554f08":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Have you tried searching around [C0]Twisted Strand[/C0]?","line:02765dd":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Have you tried searching around [C0]Devil's Spine[/C0]?","line:032c7ba":"PAINTER_NAME_KEY: Although...you already have so many - I'm not sure there are any more out there...","line:02f2313":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Down here to investigate the ice field too? It seems to have appeared out of nowhere - my best guess is that it drifted up from the south.","line:0afa5d2":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Either way, I thought I should set up a pontoon here - but when I went to stake my claim, I noticed some old equipment on the ice...","line:08eb2d1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Come and check it out when you get a second.","line:0715f07":"The Travelling Merchant has crossed over to the nearby iceberg and is inspecting some old pieces of metal. You approach.","line:0b081b6":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: It's so weird, this stuff seems old. Like, really old.","line:071a60b":"She kicks a large sheet of metal, half-embedded in the ice. A thin layer of snow dislodges, revealing lines of rivet holes.","line:0584486":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: And come in here - look!","line:0021e70":"You follow her into a small makeshift shelter, ruined by years of harsh weather. Inside are some schematics nailed to a table, still barely legible.","line:03c62e5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: See how they angled these sheets...and the lining of the metal around the bow...","line:053c549":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Whoever was here, I think they were constructing an [C0]Icebreaker[/C0]!","line:076492d":"Could you make another one using these plans?","line:04d700c":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Probably! But...ah, let me see...","line:043ea98":"What's an Icebreaker?","line:00d1eb5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: It's a reinforced structure attached to the front of ships to help them [C1]safely cut a path through ice[/C1].","line:0a305a3":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: With these plans, I could probably make another...hmm...","line:080cebe":"She trudges outside again and paces out the length of the metal scraps on the ice.","line:006c885":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: We've got most of the basic materials here already, but of course, we're [C2]missing the most crucial pieces[/C2].","line:09bccb9":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: An [C0]Icebreaker[/C0] needs [C0]specially tempered, angled metal[/C0], as well as [C0]components designed to minimize the impact[/C0] to your hull.","line:01bb4fd":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I can't see any of those here, but...whoever left all this stuff here, maybe they left other pieces elsewhere?","line:0c6b2fb":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Or maybe you'll be able to find their old ship and salvage the [C0]Icebreaker[/C0] they already built? That would be convenient! Anyway...","line:05fac64":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: To build a new [C0]Icebreaker[/C0], these are the parts we'll need.","line:080c4b6":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That's everything! Let me just warm my hands up a little, then I'll get started...","line:06475b2":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Alright, I think that should do it. [C0]The front of your ship can now break through chunks of ice[/C0]!","line:02f4dde":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Go ahead and test it out! I'll be watching from here.","line:012010e":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Oh, I forgot to mention - just let me know if you want to [C0]temporarily remove that Icebreaker[/C0]. I can swap it out at any of my pontoons.","line:0242d2c":"The worksite is empty.","line:033a5c9":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I've been looking through the schematics we found before, and there are plans here for another device too!","line:03eca1f":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: They're for an [C0]Ice Shaper[/C0] - that's different to your [C0]Icebreaker[/C0], by the way - it's for cutting chunks of ice.","line:004c18d":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: If you find the [C2]missing device[/C2], I'll be able to use the machine to harvest [C0]ice blocks[/C0] for refrigeration!","line:01513d1":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: The [C0]blocks of ice[/C0] can be packed into your cargo to [C1]slow fish spoilage[/C1]. Pretty handy, right?","line:08a5e1b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: This is what the [C2]missing[/C2] [C0]Ice Shaper[/C0] looks like.","line:0827639":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: You really found it! How on earth do you actually locate that stuff down there in the deep? Anyway...","line:030353e":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Let me slot this blade in here and...yeah, that seems right...I think it's ready to start cutting!","line:06edead":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Blocks of ice, coming right up!","line:0a51aac":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: That works pretty well! Here, these are on the house.","line:0d7424b":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: From now on I'll be able to stock some of these ice blocks at my pontoons. Thanks, partner!","line:0576e5d":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Fisherman! I didn't expect to see you this far south. Well, this is a fortunate turn of events.","line:0e77dbf":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Hmm, hello, I don't think we've met. A fisherman, I presume? Please, try to keep your engine noise to a minimum. It tends to frighten the wildlife.","line:0ade360":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: There's a [C0]Narwhal[/C0] somewhere in this ice field. I couldn't get any further in, so I've been trying to take a picture from here with no luck.","line:06308ea":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I tried placing some scraps of fish on that ice sheet over there to entice it, but I didn't have enough to hold its attention for long enough. I only caught a glimpse.","line:04d49f6":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I don't suppose you have any fish you'd be prepared to donate to the pursuit of wildlife photography?","line:0a0a980":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: [C0]Fill the space[/C0] entirely with [C0]any fish[/C0] you like, I can't imagine the [C0]Narwhal[/C0] is too picky.","line:00df493":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: That's perfect. Now, cut your engines - we need to wait in complete silence.","line:01fb653":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Ssh! I think I hear something under the ice...","line:04a297b":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: What on earth was that thing?! I'm not sticking around to find out!","line:0614c2d":"The Photographer is hurriedly packing camera equipment into boxes. She seems very on edge.","line:00815ca":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: You know, that was [C3]no regular Narwhal[/C3]. It seemed voracious and hyper-aggressive.","line:061699b":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: Animals like that tend to be very unpredictable. These ice fields aren't safe with that thing around...you should consider turning back.","line:08fd413":"PHOTOGRAPHER_NAME_KEY: I'll be out of here as soon as I've packed my things away.","line:0ae1bee":"A cold wind whistles through the doorway of the only cabin still standing. Behind it, a frozen-over dig site is littered with tools and debris.","line:0470e77":"You enter the small cabin, the door long since fallen from its hinges. A rotting table sits inside.","line:01b137c":"Fragments of the ice shard litter the floor, filling most of the room. The only thing not covered is an old table in front of you.","line:0303ef8":"A [C0]massive shard of ice[/C0] rises from the floor inside, bursting through the ceiling. It fills the room, engulfing all but an old table in front of you.","line:07c3e87":"What do you want to do?","line:0bc2882":"\\[Open the book.\\]","line:0f99c81":"\\[Inspect the empty table.\\]","line:0023ed4":"\\[Inspect the shard of ice.\\]","line:07ee051":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0b0e157":"You open the book, its frozen spine cracking for the first time in decades. Which entry do you want to read?","line:0c8ba8b":"With great care, you carefully turn to one of the earlier pages.","line:0f6efec":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: The vessel was pursued by a particularly [C2]aggressive Narwhal[/C2]. Some men [C0]placed fish on the ice nearby[/C0] in an effort to distract it.","line:009d70b":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: It appeared to work, though only for a time. It resurfaced and needed satiating repeatedly.","line:0a3e17f":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: If we can't find a more permanent solution to the beast, we'll have to make sure we keep [C0]enough fish on hand to placate it[/C0].","line:04e787c":"A few other entries appear to be legible, so you add them to your cabin to read later.","line:0dce077":"The table is empty, save for some ancient scratches in the rotten wood.","line:0da52e7":"Light pierces through the ice, intensifying and concentrating into a glow in the center. A [C3]dark form[/C3] takes shape against the light.","line:0945e91":"\\[Place an ear to the ice.\\]","line:020d286":"\\[Step away.\\]","line:01c8e89":"A distorted voice echoes from within.","line:0856819":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: Don't... disturb... the ice...","line:028e28e":"You return to the shard of ice, a [C3]dark form[/C3] still shimmering deep within.","line:0ae088c":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: ...","line:099f0bf":"Who are you?","line:0613119":"What happened here?","line:0a10f66":"\\[Break the ice.\\]","line:09aa07d":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:071dd26":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: [C0]Captain[/C0]... the expedition... chart the ice field... appeared suddenly... through the ice...","line:0ceb522":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: It whispered... promised... stones from the stars...","line:0c92608":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: It knew... three would hear... the heart... beneath the ice...","line:0327ac1":"The voice grows louder.","line:0d9edb4":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: It commanded... three listeners... three sacrifices... for three eyes...","line:0529349":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: I obeyed... but... a fourth... now sees... forever... futile...","line:0926921":"The shadow is silent for a time.","line:0afdb62":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: Slumbering... still... should leave... it sees you... before it whispers...","line:017c832":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: Do not... risk breaking... it senses... through the ice... through the shadows... no hope...","line:0436c3d":"You strike hard against the center of the shard where the shadowy shape appears darkest. A deep crack chases upwards, cleaving away fragments that fall and shatter.","line:092de79":"The structure peels open, split to its core. A glistening stone lies cradled by broken shapes, wispy threads of starlight trailing from it.","line:05796ea":"You take the stone and leave.","line:0e1b04a":"You dock against a small platform of ice formed around a gigantic, clawed hand. You are not the first to find this place - remnants of a long-abandoned camp litter the ice.","line:0a15eee":"A pile of icy splinters mark the place where the spire fell.","line:02344fd":"An unnatural spire of ice stands above scraps of snowed-over equipment. A dark shape twists within.","line:0d396f0":"\\[Place an ear to the ice.\\]","line:05e3a53":"Who are you?","line:0b0b84e":"What happened?","line:0ad07f6":"\\[Break the ice.\\]","line:05f056e":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0b3f23c":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: Please... break the ice...","line:01e1ea4":"An anguished voice cries from deep within the ice...","line:04ddedb":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: Help me... frozen... so many years... free me...","line:0f67c8f":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: I was... I am... the [C0]Boatswain[/C0]... the expedition... the Terror...","line:0907a30":"The figure contorts through painful shapes.","line:0a4303a":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: We saw... lights... dancing in ice... dug deep... didn't know... I heard it...","line:0cc56fd":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: The heart... beating... under ice... the cracking... waking... the noises... in the east...","line:0c11245":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: I went... the Captain... brought him here... to find it... the hand... in the night... shadow of claws...","line:09905eb":"The darkness shrinks.","line:08122bc":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: I turned away... just a moment... the pain... the claws... my back... so cold... so dark... under ice...","line:0cf0dde":"SOUL_EAST_NAME_KEY: Silence it... you must... shatter...","line:0db2f20":"Splinters of ice are all that remain.","line:0218805":"A line describing the dock upon your first arrival.","line:087bf5a":"The site of a final escape, and a greater eye closed shut.","line:03389b2":"A spire of glassy ice stands in the shadow of the cliffs. Across the water, a monstrous visage peers from an icy tomb.","line:0b5ba49":"\\[Place an ear to the ice.\\]","line:07e6695":"Who are you?","line:0eeccd7":"What happened?","line:0a45ca3":"What is that thing in the ice?","line:0776de9":"\\[Break the ice.\\]","line:0f4061d":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:036b049":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: [C0]Find the axe[/C0]... undo this... the betrayer...","line:0997439":"A sound of anger lashes from within.","line:047746d":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: Murderer... betray your men... left us here... your sleepless god...","line:03cc7a7":"The voice abates.","line:072b697":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: Wait... your shadow... it speaks... another shape... please... save us all...","line:03ade3e":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: [C0]First Officer[/C0]... safety of the crew... failed them... should have... cursed place...","line:0e4092a":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: The men... saw lights... southern cliffs... at night... Captain and I... would look into... we rowed alone...","line:0059d91":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: He was... restless... sleepless... we passed... walls of ice... finally arrived... the great horn... into view...","line:0da719b":"The words drift in, some carried away on the wind.","line:03bb66c":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: Pulled ashore... quickly... the size of it... the light... somehow... he knew... eyes were wild... he was... whispering... answering...","line:0b078ca":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: He said... it chose him... alone... avert my eyes... could not help... look upon... we fought... cold hands... an iron grip... breathless...","line:0f40770":"The shape in the ice shrinks into itself.","line:03b9b0f":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: I know not... the eyes open... watching... shadow of shadow... through the ice... yet more... closed still...","line:0bdeaea":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: It cannot... arise... break the ice... cull the heart...","line:0b0967d":"SOUL_SOUTH_NAME_KEY: Must not... fully awaken... the eyes... close them... strike the heart...","line:07b472c":"Another makeshift camp constructed in the shadow of a frozen, clawed hand. Someone was seeking these out.","line:03bfe31":"A pile of icy splinters marks the place where the spire fell.","line:0497383":"An unnatural spire of ice stands above scraps of snowed-over equipment. A dark shape twists within.","line:0ae630f":"\\[Place an ear to the ice.\\]","line:0c61224":"Who are you?","line:0eec91d":"What happened?","line:07ec246":"\\[Break the ice.\\]","line:0c24980":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0c3d09a":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: Break it... somehow... free me...","line:07c67c9":"A voice calls out, distant and distorted.","line:08c93e9":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: Trapped... forever... this prison... get me out...","line:059f0ef":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: The [C0]Navigator[/C0]... find safe passage... chart the ice... it came from... beyond...","line:06dd53c":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: The digging... the cracked ice... like a web... awoke... the ice heart...","line:06d8ab4":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: I told him... whispers in the west... took the Boatswain... east... returned alone...","line:055305b":"The dark figure shudders, sending vibrations through the ice.","line:06f6d7c":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: The next day... rowed here... the Captain... saw the claws... grip my soul... he insisted... made camp... shadow of the beast...","line:00c5bab":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: Waiting for the stars... in the night... I saw... his shape... suddenly... swallowed... by the cold... in the dark... he left me...","line:0359a0c":"SOUL_WEST_NAME_KEY: This cold sun... warmth long forgot... no more... break me...","line:0bddb6c":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: The [C0]Boatswain[/C0]... gone... fearful boy... the skies... we remain... the consequences... inherited...","line:07376a4":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: The [C0]Navigator[/C0]... my eyes... for the shadow... closing... you risk... annihilation... annihilation...","line:04ed191":"SOUL_MIDDLE_NAME_KEY: [C0]Officer[/C0]... unworthy... tried to take... turn the men... my expedition... my discovery... his failure...","line:0a77ab2":"A translucent spire of ice stretches down into the darkness. A pulsing glow rises from the deep, illuminating [C0]four round sockets[/C0].","line:0058d4c":"The glowing light intensifies, feeding into the four stones. A web of light grows between them, connecting, rejoining. Uniting.","line:083da6a":"Leaving fish here would probably attract that [C3]monstrous Narwhal[/C3].","line:0ab28b6":"That should keep it [C1]satisfied[/C1] - at least for a [C0]little while[/C0].","line:0d728a0":"No more fish will fit on the pile.","line:08419e6":"What is this place?","line:0bcb642":"I'd like to re-attach the Icebreaker.","line:094d219":"I'd like to remove the Icebreaker.","line:006a2e4":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: In the meantime, I've got some [C0]new rods for sale[/C0]! They'll be perfect for [C0]fishing in the ice[/C0] around here.","line:06e1c77":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: I'm not exactly sure yet, but I have a theory...have you heard the legend of [C0]The Pale Reach[/C0]? It's an old sailor's tale.","line:096a3a3":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: The story goes that when the fog grows thick enough, the ice appears, seemingly out of nowhere. Hours later, or sometimes days, it vanishes again without a trace.","line:0521fd5":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Back in the olden days, they sent a survey expedition in to investigate. Apparently, it returned with half the crew - either from mutiny or madness.","line:027f898":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Travel on the high seas in those days will do that to you, I guess! Anyway, I'm not sure about this place. It could just be regular old ice.","line:00b77ef":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Sure, give me a moment. I've got it stored back here somewhere...","line:0c5887e":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: All done - you're ready to smash some ice!","line:06166e9":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Sure, give me a moment. I'll need to find some space for it onboard...","line:0917372":"TRAVELLING_MERCHANT_NAME_KEY: Alright, that's sorted! I'll keep it with me for when you need it reattached.","line:000149f":"A crudely drawn map of the area has been charted onto a scrap of paper. [C1]You attach it to your own map[/C1].","line:021cf73":"A large book sits on the table. It's well-worn from the passage of time, but you can still read the words \"Captain's Log\" etched into the cover.","line:08541b5":"Which entry do you want to read?","line:0888326":"30th May, 1847","line:0eeab73":"31st May, 1847","line:00985a8":"1st June, 1847","line:0df855c":"2nd June, 1847","line:09c97a5":"4th June, 1847","line:062ab79":"5th June, 1847","line:0fe9803":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0c0d03f":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: Arrived at the floating sea-ice amidst a particularly thick fog. A few channels could be seen leading into the ice, though sizeable chunks float in our way, posing a hazard.","line:0a89748":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: I have ordered us to moor against the outer ice wall while the engineers make adjustments to better prepare the vessel.","line:0d447c1":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: Adjustments were completed and we began maneuvering through the closest channel.","line:05e56a1":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: After a time, the narrow channel opened up into a large lagoon. During the night, some of the men reported seeing lights coming from under the ice.","line:08bd8f7":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: We shall establish a temporary encampment on an island in the center of the lagoon to see if we can excavate the source.","line:07edd65":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: Setup of the encampment is complete, and some surface samples were gathered. No trace of the glowing light could be found.","line:09e5825":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: Perhaps we will dig deeper tomorrow, though I hesitate to spend any more time on this endeavour. Our purview is geographical charting.","line:02adae8":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: As I lay falling asleep, the most almighty voice spoke unto me. It resounded from the thick ice below, at once both powerful and ethereal.","line:096d55f":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: There was no mistaking this as a trick of the wind, nor a jest by the crew. It did not pause for response or acknowledgement, but whispered a [C3]cryptic prophesy[/C3].","line:02c0352":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: At first, I could not make sense of it - \"[C3]Three listeners shall hear the heart[/C3]\", and that I should indulge these \"[C3]listeners[/C3]\".","line:0f66c18":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: It spoke of \"[C1]boundless wealth from the stars[/C1]\" and of \"[C0]eyes opening unto the world[/C0]\".","line:0631371":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: The rest of my sleep was feverish, as my mind was plagued with the sound of the voice. It spun in my head, echoing ever louder.","line:0301947":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: In the morning, the [C0]Boatswain[/C0] and the [C0]Navigator[/C0] came to me separately, claiming to have heard a [C3]sound like a heartbeat[/C3] as the men were digging yesterday.","line:0241d21":"CAPTAINS_LOG_NAME_KEY: They indicated a desire to explore the [C0]Eastern[/C0] and [C0]Western[/C0] reaches of the ice field. I shall indulge them.","line:0b718d6":"You rummage through the small pile of equipment in the snow. Most items are stuck fast in the ice, but inside a small backpack you find an [C0]old journal[/C0].","line:0515cb3":"Which entry do you want to read?","line:054408f":"2nd June, 1847","line:0ff4c7f":"4th June, 1847","line:0980cc2":"5th June, 1847","line:01a3668":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0af2db4":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: Captain ordered us to make camp on the ice in the center of the lagoon. After we saw those lights in the ice, everyone's got [C1]treasure[/C1] on their minds.","line:0d72dca":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: Treasure hunting isn't exactly what the expedition was commissioned for, but given the Captain gets the lion's share of whatever we find...","line:027f45b":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: It doesn't surprise me that he's willing to bend the rules a bit. We'll start digging after the camp's done.","line:00d6a4c":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: Spent the day digging down in the ice. Shovels and ice picks. Can't remember the last time I was this tired.","line:0f85214":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: We were only allowed two short breaks all day. Down in the pit, as I rested with my back against the ice, I started hearing something.","line:0a75dc1":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: It was different to the sounds of the picks. They were short and sharp. This was low, a rumble from deeper down.","line:0034e48":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: On my first break, it was occasional. Only a few each minute. By my second break, it had quickened, like a heartbeat.","line:0b7585e":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: The Captain overheard me telling some others about the sound I heard in the pit. Before I knew it, I was in front of his desk, sure I was about to have my pay docked.","line:0f0bad0":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: To my great surprise, he seemed to know something of it already. He was keen on hearing it described, over and over.","line:03d026a":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: He wants me to help locate the source of it. When he pressed me on it further, I said that it did seem to be coming from the East.","line:0b18892":"TATTERED_DIARY_NAME_KEY: Tomorrow, we are setting off to see if we can find it. Perhaps I shall get a bonus after this is done!","line:05793e5":"There are very few pieces that still remain - whoever made camp here was poorly prepared. Inside a small bag, you find a [C0]leather bound journal[/C0].","line:0fe6c42":"Which entry do you want to read?","line:0384336":"4th June, 1847","line:0351128":"7th June, 1847","line:0fad082":"8th June, 1847","line:022eb53":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:00f637e":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: The men spent the whole day digging. They passed up chunks of ice, some as brilliant as crystal, others of a deepest blue more beautiful than sapphires.","line:06cdcae":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: But none held the glow we had seen in the night. However, I did note a disturbance in the ice to the West.","line:087ba8b":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: It began as a periodic, distant rumble. As the men dug deeper, the pulsing quickened, strengthening until I could see the ice shifting on the surface.","line:01a3216":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: I shall have to inform the Captain. It may well be that Narwhal creature we saw earlier, though this did seem much larger.","line:05ebbf4":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: As I write this, I can already feel my eyes closing. It will have to wait until the morning.","line:0699d81":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: This morning, the Captain appeared out of the fog, rowing alone. Apparently, the Boatswain remains at a camp in the East, waiting for nightfall.","line:05e6d14":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: They were unsuccessful in their search, but it does make sense that the lights would be more visible at night.","line:0a9e362":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: Tomorrow, we're to journey together to the West, towards the shifting ice that I reported.","line:0ce53dc":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: He is on edge, his head turning this way and that, listening for the slightest sound. He is convinced something will happen after dark.","line:0489e82":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: As the last light from the cold sun fades, I have the sense that it will be a long night.","line:0eaec8f":"It looks like someone built a feeding station for that [C3]monstrous Narwhal[/C3]. Perhaps its appetite would be [C1]satisfied[/C1] by an [C0]offering of fish[/C0].","line:02fd705":"You approach a hooded figure. They seem to be frozen to the spot, pale robes frosted over with a heavy rime.","line:0ef54a5":"HOODED_FIGURE_5_NAME_KEY: Fisherman...the ice.","line:03d57c3":"You hear their jaw snap shut again from the cold.","line:030c5bc":"HOODED_FIGURE_5_NAME_KEY: The ice...takes form.","line:0eaf963":"The hooded figure withdraws a scroll from their robes and unfurls it to reveal a drawing of a corrupted fish - an [C3]Aberrated[/C3] [C0]Icefish[/C0].","line:0e7587c":"The hooded figure places the fish on the ice at their feet, kicking loose snow over to cover it.","line:0d306c6":"HOODED_FIGURE_5_NAME_KEY: The stars...leave the sky.","line:0e250df":"Another scroll, another twisted shape. Images of [C3]Aberrated[/C3] [C0]Sea Stars[/C0] cover the paper.","line:026c277":"The [C0]Sea Stars[/C0] are arranged in a circle on the ground. Moments later, a sinewy heel stomps down through each of them.","line:0b2dce2":"HOODED_FIGURE_5_NAME_KEY: Fall...to the deep.","line:0e8ce76":"A final scroll, this one stained in patches by some dark liquid. In the center, the shape of an [C3]Aberrated[/C3] [C0]Stargazer[/C0] peers from the page.","line:0d156f3":"The figure places the body of the [C0]Stargazer[/C0] in the center of the crushed [C0]Sea Stars[/C0]. They angle its cratered eye to the sky.","line:0018cc7":"Attention still fixed on the gruesome pile of fish in front of it, the hooded figure gestures to a [C1]Book[/C1] on a nearby rock. Your payment.","line:0d12b6d":"As you leave, the figure is still focused on the grim fish - adjusting its position, waiting, adjusting, over and over.","line:0fbeb55":"Darkness. The deep. Then, sparks of light as tooth and spine meet horn and nail. Two primeval forces clashing at the bottom of the world.","line:01f9a66":"After an age, a victor triumphs, sundering the other into impossibly large remnants that ascend to the surface, slowly, to be claimed by the sky.","line:03ea3ac":"But the broken body holds power still. Threads of crimson essence reach out through the water, stretching to unite the creature once more.","line:0f34a68":"As the remains break the surface, ice begins to form.","line:038f030":"Intruders. They invade on tiny wooden vessels, shouting and smashing. They cut and slice with angled metal, raking across a skin of ice.","line:05a1451":"Their meagre hearts beat with avarice and pride, desires trivially twisted into new shapes. Shapes that might mend and restore.","line:0855069":"Shapes to replace what was lost, down in the dark.","line:09785a5":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: We are alone on a small island of ice.","line:0c4466f":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: After hours of rowing through narrow channels, it rose through the fog. A gargantuan, monstrous claw, reaching from the deep.","line:06c836c":"LEATHER_JOURNAL_NAME_KEY: Whatever creature it once belonged to must be long dead, as the claw is frozen solid. I wanted to turn back immediately, but the Captain insisted we investigate.","line:079df1e":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: What do you want?","line:06e5de5":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: If you're able to [C1]find any of those crates[C1], I'm sure the corp would let you [C1]use our facilities[/C1]. Once we get the [C0]Generator[/C0] wired up, that is.","line:0a72733":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: That oughta be enough to get the [C0]Generator[/C0] going! I'll get these materials sent up to the main platform.","line:0d2d4a3":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: So, that should be in working order, but, I just checked the storeroom, and it looks like we [C2]never got any fuel deliveries[/C2].","line:09b00be":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Hey there. Welcome to the Factory. I'm the lead engineer here.","line:03f5081":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Because of your help getting things running here, I'm permitted to [C1]improve your equipment with our tech[/C1].","line:0c22a4e":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: These are some designs I've been tinkering with for passive harvesting methods.","line:0fc828f":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: We've got various off-cuts and scraps here, I can usually turn them into something.","line:077a91b":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: We've got what we need.","line:0f23cee":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Let's get to work.","line:0c81365":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: We're making good progress on getting the Factory fully operational.","line:0ac3dfe":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Alright, here's what we'll need to put that together.","line:089527d":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: That should do it.","line:0d689e6":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Hey, you forgot to take this with you earlier.","line:0dff1c3":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: So, this is where we're going to build some sort of machine to repel those tentacles, right? That's what the Scientist said.","line:0e26c07":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: YOU HAVE RETURNED.","line:0476c1c":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: We'll get started.","line:0785bc2":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Defenses are primed. Turning them on now. This had better work.","line:028440e":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: I reckon we can repurpose some of that slag from the Science Lab. Toss it into the water, see what turns up to investigate.","line:0f82a38":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: The Factory's core facilities should be up and running.","line:02b5388":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: The Factory's core facilities have been improved. We can make some more items now.","line:0cca8f6":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Fisherman, I think you're going to like what we can make here now.","line:03bff27":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: That'll do it for the Factory!","line:08aeeda":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: This Factory's running at peak efficiency. We've got all we need.","line:08cb47d":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Fleet Services root. Is this unbuilt?","line:02597b3":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Fleet Services description. This is built, right?","line:059ffef":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Alright, we'll get to work on Fleet Services.","line:02dbc21":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Everything should be operational here, sir.","line:02b6fcd":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Place isn't built yet.","line:0bd9d7e":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Basic materials can be worked here.","line:0979644":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: You find any excess crates, I'm sure we can come to some sort of arrangement.","line:0a94991":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: That's all we need; we can get the Foundry built now.","line:055cd1d":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Good to go.","line:0e8f3d0":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Alright, we'll start upgrading the Foundry.","line:01d4913":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Should be able to make some better stuff now.","line:03f35ef":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: You want that made, I'll be needing some things from you.","line:0339db1":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Mmh. That's done.","line:0a78ca3":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Take your stuff with you next time.","line:093e6b6":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: When the [C0]Tech Lab[/C0] is operational, we'll be able to work on projects of a more technical nature.","line:0740029":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: We're not quite ready for construction yet. Missing materials - can you help?","line:0aadcdc":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: This wing is for the [C1]enhancement[/C1] of boat functions; [C0]lights[/C0], [C0]horn[/C0] and [C0]spyglass[/C0].","line:0a0bc02":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Everything appears to be in order. I'll get the team onto it.","line:08f9f0b":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: At last. I'm excited for you to try some of these out.","line:0f5ee6b":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: That's everything. We'll get to work.","line:038acdc":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: The Tech Lab is fully built now!","line:0ff0334":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: These are a little complex; here's the list of items I'll need.","line:0066d41":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: That one's done.","line:0fa906c":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Oh, you left this here before. I held onto it for you.","line:0fa666b":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Hmm? Who are you? Ah; the angler turned courier, isn't that right? The workers were talking about you.","line:0ad74e3":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: THE SCIENCE LAB REMAINS UNBUILT. IS THIS LINE EVER EVEN SHOWN?","line:0750d7e":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Oh, we've got enough material for the [C0]Science Lab[/C0] now too? We'll get to work.","line:0ee1663":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Yes, more than sufficient for my needs. Thank you, both of you.","line:045d807":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: How can I help you?","line:056ed20":"Stage 2","line:08540a5":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Response.","line:035dfbf":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0ca120a":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: So, it turns out the fuel never got dispatched from Ironhaven at all.","line:0907e32":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: You can add fish or...most other biological material, I suppose, to the hopper here. Once it's filled we ought to be able to start the drill.","line:062b6a3":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: It won't hold any more - I'll fire it up!","line:0809a7c":"The crushing compactor clunks to life. The sound of pneumatic pistons and strained squelching soon gives way to the stuttering sound of distant gears.","line:0906dc7":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:01ac250":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Here for some cutscene testing, eh?","line:0f7806d":"\\[Cutscene 1 (The Marrows)\\]","line:068b666":"\\[Cutscene 2 (Gale Cliffs)\\]","line:0b94eb0":"\\[Cutscene 3 (Stellar Basin)\\]","line:0f03026":"\\[Cutscene 4 (Twisted Strand)\\]","line:07fd3d4":"\\[Cutscene 5 (Devil's Spine)\\]","line:03b301b":"\\[Cutscene 6 (Finale)\\]","line:0709ef1":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0a38cd2":"Stage 3","line:08c73ac":"Stage 4","line:049f242":"Stage 5","line:0c96ff7":"Stage 6","line:053859e":"Stage 7","line:0e4cf83":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Stage 2.","line:023a489":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Stage 3.","line:02e00ac":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Stage 4.","line:09ec88a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Stage 5.","line:0b2542a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Stage 6.","line:0d29dcb":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Stage 7.","line:05afc45":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: While I go and figure out the [C2]fuel situation[/C2], why don't you introduce yourself to the head [C0]Scientist[/C0]? He's always interested to hear about the local fish species.","line:0da6ac9":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: I was planning on conducting [C0]research into fish species[/C0] in the area. But I can't do that without somewhere to study.","line:0a50437":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I think we have a solution for our [C2]fuel problem[/C2] - come see me at the [C0]Generator[/C0] and I'll give you the rundown.","line:0706db4":"You dock at a small metal wharf. Four giant legs stretch down into the deep, lifting a mountain of metal into the sky.","line:0561fb1":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: HERE IS A ROD THAT I PREPARED EARLIER.","line:0a551ee":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Do you have those samples from [C0]The Marrows[/C0] yet?","line:0bc915f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Have you had time to gather samples from [C0]Gale Cliffs[/C0]?","line:037d823":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Have you collected all of those samples from [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0] yet?","line:0984b20":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: The fish...from [C0]Twisted Strand[/C0]...do you have them?","line:0d55052":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Closer...pure...[C0]Devil's Spine[/C0]...the wretches...where are they?!","line:0e7ea88":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: I WILL TRANSFORM HERE.","line:0d5dae6":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Admittedly, the [C2]fissure[/C2] is larger than my models suggested, but it appears to have stabilized. We should consider [C0]halting the drilling[/C0] for now.","line:008039b":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Using that rod, I need you to [C0]collect specimen samples[/C0] from [C0]The Marrows[/C0], just to check that the fish species are unaffected by our operations here.","line:0a5edab":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: YOU HAVE CONSTRUCTED THE FACTORY AND RECEIVED A ROD.","line:02eb480":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: YOU SHOULD GO AND GET SOME SAMPLES FROM THE MARROWS.","line:0dd73bc":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: YOU SHOULD MAKE SOME DEFENCES. TALK TO MY STUDENT IN STELLAR BASIN, SHE HAS THE TECH.","line:0df9179":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: YOU SHOULD GO AND GET SOME SAMPLES FROM STELLAR BASIN.","line:05285b6":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: YOU SHOULD GO AND GET SOME SAMPLES FROM TWISTED STRAND.","line:0af3ed8":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: YOU SHOULD GO AND GET SOME SAMPLES FROM DEVIL'S SPINE.","line:025aac9":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: NOW THAT YOU HAVE AN ADVANCED ROD, YOU CAN COLLECT SAMPLES.","line:0562ce4":"The Scientist is interrupted by the Foreman outside, shouting through his megaphone again. The Foreman bellows an order.","line:06f6105":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Engage reverse gear! Get that drill out of there!","line:00c50f7":"OUTSIDE, YOU HEAR A CLAMOR OF SHOUTING WORKERS. THE FOREMAN SAYS SOMETHING.","line:0518806":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: FIRE UP THE DRILL!","line:0f7fba3":"OUTSIDE, YOU HEAR A CLAMOR OF SHOUTING WORKERS. THE FOREMAN SAYS SOMETHING.","line:093d713":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: FIRE UP THE DRILL!","line:0df1f10":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: What's that noise?","line:0569096":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: FIRE UP THE DRILL!","line:08ad563":"OUTSIDE, YOU HEAR A CLAMOR OF SHOUTING WORKERS. THE FOREMAN SAYS SOMETHING.","line:056e9f1":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: FIRE UP THE DRILL!","line:02a2306":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: ...as I was saying. I'll run some quick tests on these specimens. Though from the sounds of things, you may have some additional samples to gather.","line:024422f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Unfortunately there have been reports of some [C3]contaminatants[/C3] leaking from the fissure in isolated pockets.","line:0e797f2":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Have you collected a canister of that [C3]contaminant[/C3] yet?","line:0848ca8":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Thank you. It's always important to know what we're dealing with in operations such as these.","line:0e138fd":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: There's something gigantic, something incredibly powerful, gripping the rig! So...it's really here.","line:01426e4":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Fisherman. This structure...the people on it...can't stand up to this. I have - well, [C0]I had a student[/C0]. She was developing some [C1]technology[/C1].","line:0b61898":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: IT'S BAD ENOUGH THAT THE FLEET SERVICES BUILDING ISN'T UP AND RUNNING YET. CAN YOU HELP WITH THAT?","line:0ffa918":"Someone from the Ironhaven Corporation sent me.","line:040fb49":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: And we're back on track. While he overstepped his corporate responsibility, it appears the Foreman was right to enlist your assistance.","line:0c013f9":"He walks away, muttering something about modulating voices and waves.","line:018704f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Yes...remarkable...the power spikes. Hmm. Fisherman, don't forget about those samples.","line:0b2f627":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: MAYBE THE EXECUTIVE WILL HAVE SOME DIALOGUE HERE TOO.","line:0d44e7f":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Excellent. Remember Fisherman, I'll permit the workers to [C1]upgrade your hull[/C1] with our tech here.","line:09fccfa":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I didn't expect that name to follow me all the way out here. Perhaps that was naive of me.","line:00528ae":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I couldn't give a damn about the rig, or the corp. But not everyone there deserves to face the consequences of the corp's actions.","line:0123478":"About those defenses on the rig...","line:0cd2fb1":"You walk the perimeter of the tower. One of the electrical panels hasn't been securely fastened.","line:0674606":"You open the panel. Inside, a bundle of cables travels from a [C0]black box[/C0], up into the heights of the tower.","line:06a0d7c":"After finding the loose panel housing the electrical guts of the tower, you pull out the blueprint for the \"[C3]RISE[/C3]\" module.","line:0352fa9":"You remove the old module and insert the new one. As it clicks into place, the sound from the tower changes into a deep rumble.","line:04f47b9":"With the last scraps of metal still falling from the destroyed drill tower, the Executive boards his helicopter, rotors already spinning.","line:06e3a32":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: What do you want?","line:0a7fe37":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: What else? I don't have all day.","line:08b3280":"Why is the Ironhaven corporation interested in this region?","line:0347d03":"What is your Scientist doing with the fish I've been gathering?","line:09b715e":"The Foreman was telling the truth. Something attacked the rig!","line:0b40a1b":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: The corporation has an interest in every region. Over the next few years, you'll come to understand.","line:05e9842":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Whatever he likes.","line:05bfe59":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Well, I don't see it any more, do you?","line:0620d89":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: No. We're close now. And it knows it. How long will it take for the drill to break through to the [C3]next layer[/C3]?","line:0011322":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh? I hope they worked.","line:031b3ff":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: There's one in particular. I've been referring to it by its closest human analogue: \"[C3]RISE[/C3]\".","line:09d65f5":"THE DEFENSES HAVE BEEN BUILT, AND YOU'RE BACK.","line:03c01de":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: These blueprints are confusing...what even is...okay, I think I follow.","line:01ccde5":"EXECUTIVE: DEFENSES POST-CONSTRUCTION DIALOGUE. IS THIS SHOWN?","line:068cb08":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:03f12a3":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Hmm?","line:009aa47":"\\[Return Canister.\\]","line:0b107e6":"\\[Submit Samples.\\]","line:0a68d0c":"\\[Submit Samples.\\]","line:09724ad":"\\[Submit Samples.\\]","line:03dd50d":"\\[Submit Samples.\\]","line:08f6bc2":"\\[Submit Samples.\\]","line:07d5822":"How long have you worked for the Ironhaven corporation?","line:0dbb7d1":"How long have you worked for the Ironhaven Corporation?","line:0b8d6df":"Option 3","line:02f0a4f":"\\[Leave.\\]","line:0547402":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: My whole professional career has been dedicated to scientific research at the corporation. So that's...well, north of half a century now.","line:0d0953a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Well I can't go into specifics, you understand, but the purpose of this platform is to test a crucial hypothesis that I've been working towards for years.","line:0f52af0":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: TODO: FILLER 3","line:074f2a0":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Oh, and don't forget about that other thing I asked you to do.","line:0d763c6":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Fisherman, considering you're not on the corp's payroll, why don't you take this; a small token of my appreciation.","line:0ffeb56":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Remember, you've still got to collect a canister of that [C3]contaminant[/C3] for me.","line:029bba7":"An elevator connecting the docking area to the main platform lies ahead. A man waits nearby, a yellow hardhat strapped to a concerned expression.","line:0a82ee1":"What is this place?","line:044d229":"Who are you?","line:04a6ab4":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Haven't you heard? This is the [C0]Ironhaven Corporation[/C0]'s new drilling rig. Or, it would be, if we were on schedule. Right now it's just a platform.","line:0bd42fa":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: The boss's gonna dock our pay for sure if he shows up and the drill hasn't even started. We've got the foundational stuff laid, but we've been running into some supply issues.","line:059d306":"He glances nervously at the water, large waves rolling underneath the shadow of the platform.","line:0d6a620":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: The ships delivering [C0]crates of materials[/C0] keep [C2]going missing[/C2] - and HQ said they're not able to dispatch any more for a few weeks.","line:092d1ce":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Look, I wouldn't normally ask a civilian for help, but we're already so far behind... Why don't I mark the [C0]last known coordinates of those ships on your map[/C0]?","line:04ea48d":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I did find this though. You can use it to patch things up in a pinch. Keep it, it's the least I can do in return for your help.","line:0493a88":"You approach an old man, pacing back and forth near a cordoned off area on the main platform. He's muttering to himself quietly.","line:0dc34e3":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: All good things, I promise. Say, you must know a great deal about the fish species around here, yes? What've you encountered in these waters?","line:0ad8740":"Just your regular fish species. Nothing special.","line:053cb43":"Why do you want to know?","line:09a3399":"You wouldn't believe me if I told you.","line:0e371fc":"His eyes narrow, and a grimace of disappointment briefly tugs at the corners of his mouth.","line:0d67ead":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Hmm. I have some hypotheses that suggest - ah, we'll see...perhaps.","line:00b1435":"He looks offended.","line:05205bd":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: You may have certain...preconceived notions about the Ironhaven Corporation's modus operandi, but I assure you, everything we do is with the good of the greater ecosystem in mind.","line:033fae6":"Instead of rolling his eyes, as most people do when they sense a fisherman's tale approaching, the Scientist's eyes glisten with an intense curiosity.","line:014c880":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Is that so? Perhaps you'll find me a little more imaginative than others.","line:0eb6f2f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Before we get into all of that though, it seems my laboratory is also a victim of a missing supply shipment.","line:0ed04bd":"The Scientist is waiting inside the lab. You get the sense that he's not very busy at the moment.","line:0742ce0":"The Scientist is standing in front of a map of the area. A line is drawn from the location of the rig, down to The Marrows.","line:07f6d8f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: How's it going out there?","line:03e8319":"The Scientist is standing in front of a map of the area. A line is drawn from the location of the rig, down to The Marrows and Gale Cliffs.","line:06269af":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Can I help you?","line:0d86212":"The Scientist is standing in front of a map of the area. A line is drawn from the location of the rig, spreading out through the southern regions.","line:09159ff":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: What is it?","line:0048b68":"The Scientist is standing in front of a map of the area. A line is drawn from the location of the rig, spreading out through almost all regions.","line:0f8d306":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Yes?","line:0607db5":"The Scientist is standing in front of a map of the area. A line is drawn from the location of the rig, spreading out through all regions.","line:0d2a31b":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: ...?","line:0cb4ff2":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: That should be enough space for your tubes and fluids, eh?","line:071dde2":"The Foreman turns to you.","line:0bd38ef":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I was on the radio to HQ: apparently, this is a [C0]Biofuel Generator[/C0]. It's some new tech the corp wanted to trial out here - and they expected us to supply it ourselves.","line:04b6fe1":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Thing is, they didn't think to outfit us with any gear for harvesting biomass, and the [C0]Fleet Services[/C0] construction is way down the project list.","line:06ad901":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Think you could help us out again?","line:04491c0":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Haha! We've done it!","line:04b79ae":"A large capsule drops down from a chute labelled \"[C2]WASTE[/C2]\". Through its clear walls you can see remnants of the fish you deposited.","line:0275e63":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Er, well, you'd probably be able to use that for chum, right? It's yours if you want it.","line:0e1ed8a":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: What can I do for you?","line:0ba6f5e":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Anything else?","line:085e390":"What happened to the missing material ships?","line:002b5be":"What is this rig for?","line:090abdc":"What can you tell me about the Ironhaven Corporation?","line:06b040b":"\\[Cutscene Tests\\]","line:0e84178":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Ever since we got the legs of the platform seated on the seafloor, the supply ships started going missing. HQ told us they'd left port, but they never showed up.","line:05a8597":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I guess the crews thought they could make some money sailing off with the materials and selling them elsewhere. Doesn't seem worth the risk to me.","line:0b8cdbd":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: The rig is your standard setup, designed to pierce the seabed and collect from fluid reservoirs. It doesn't have much storage capacity though, which is odd. Maybe they're not expecting huge throughput.","line:08c9faa":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I didn't actually think there was an oil field out here, but I suppose the surveyors must have found something - else I wouldn't be here talking to you.","line:068f379":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I've been with the corp for about a decade now; started out as a laborer on projects like this one - not always out to sea, mind you - and I've worked my way up to site foreman.","line:0812a1c":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: The corp itself? It's pretty successful, bit of an institution. It's been around for hundreds of years, in one form or another. They always seem to be diversifying into new areas.","line:07c0402":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: The whole drilling division is guided by the [C0]Scientist[/C0]. He calls the shots when it comes to deciding on sites. Boss seems to listen to him, too.","line:0b998a1":"\\[Back.\\]","line:0a2f0d8":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Initiating drill deployment in 3...","line:03cb6ea":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: 2...","line:0340201":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: 1...","line:0c56499":"The drill descends.","line:0ed70ab":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I'm the site foreman, and this is the [C0]Ironhaven Corporation[/C0]'s new drilling rig. Or, it would be, if we were on schedule. Right now it's just a platform.","line:06f732a":"The Scientist walks over, gripping handrails to counteract the shockwaves from the drill.","line:0ce3600":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: We've broken through! We're underway at last!","line:036137d":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: And what about that [C2]huge crack[/C2] that opened up?! Is the reservoir stable?","line:0472dce":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Also, we would be remiss in our duties to the local population if we didn't [C0]survey the area[/C0] and [C0]gather some data[/C0]. In that vein, fisherman, I have something for you.","line:0784cc3":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: The [C0]Factory[/C0] has recently become operational, allowing us to manufacture [C1]equipment infused with the corporation's latest breakthroughs[/C1]. This is a new design.","line:0b08ca0":"The Scientist looks taken aback. He consults some papers on his desk, then leafs through an old encyclopedia.","line:0988f51":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: This is...remarkable. Some of these species...have you caught these before? They haven't been seen outside the fossil record since...well, ever!","line:00766a7":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: I suppose it could make sense; the fissure opening caused some kind of disturbance in the deep, possibly spooking some of these fish up the water column.","line:06756e8":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: I'll run some tests on these -","line:023dadc":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: We must know...where these creatures entered...where the [C3]blood[/C3]...","line:07f470a":"The Scientist inserts a syringe into each of the creatures, now laying long-dead on the slab. From each, in turn, he draws a vial of fluid.","line:0d5be8d":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: This will only take a moment.","line:0903548":"Some vials contain the type of blood you might expect; deep and red, catching glints of light from the fluorescent bulbs overhead.","line:0380886":"Other corpses yield a [C3]dark, clotted substance[/C3] that seems to crawl up into the vial by itself. It shimmers with a quiet iridescence, as if lit from inside.","line:0a18bc2":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: There was always a chance this might happen. The [C0]Engineer[/C0] at the [C0]Factory[/C0] has been working on a system to siphon such [C3]contaminants[/C3] from the water.","line:0059a0d":"He places the vials of what should be fish blood in a rack in front of him.","line:077f69f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: I'd very much like a [C3]canister[/C3] of it.","line:0099e16":"\\[Open it.\\]","line:0090331":"The [C0]black box[/C0] has a number of [C0]empty slots[/C0] on the top, one of which has a module inserted into it. It's labelled \"[C2]FLEE[/C2]\" in electrical tape.","line:02d6a88":"Considering this is her invention, perhaps the [C0]Researcher[/C0] in [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0] would have some advice.","line:064cbb2":"\\[Ignore it.\\]","line:078b159":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: But I think you know how this works by now. You'll have to gather the materials yourself.","line:01c13d4":"GIVE HULL REPAIR KIT HERE.","line:06a5847":"THERE MAY BE ANOTHER CUTSCENE HERE WHERE THE EXECUTIVE FLIES AWAY.","line:05db8fd":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Uh, is everyone alright?","line:0484eee":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: All accounted for in the Factory.","line:0a714eb":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Mmmh. Yep. Foundry's fine.","line:0a14cd1":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I guess we'll wait for our airlifts outta here. There's no way I'm travelling anywhere by boat.","line:0fd9759":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Yeah, I'll sit tight for now. Fisherman, the main buildings are mostly undamaged, so if you still need stuff made, we can sort you out.","line:000361d":"He holds it up to the light. For a moment, the fluorescent bulbs in the room flicker and buzz, light recoiling in a pattern against the ceiling.","line:0b745b1":"If he saw anything noteworthy about the liquid, he doesn't let on.","line:0ee7ddb":"The Scientist arranges the specimens, now laid out on a metal table in front of him. He connects electrodes and wires to the head of each.","line:0293522":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: The brains of fish are primitive. In many ways, their simplicity is a kind of purity. No burdensome emotions to confuse the data.","line:007c128":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Just as rigor mortis locks the muscles, the final shape of the mind is held by the brain. But it can be...extracted.","line:0edd2a6":"The room is pierced with the sharp sound of capacitors charging. The corpses on the bench jolt in unison, slackened muscles arch and tense before lying still again.","line:06272bd":"The Scientist is already looking at the four monitors behind him. The same vague shape scrolls across each screen; ragged circle, writhing cell, lidless eye, yawning pit.","line:0ac9f7c":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: The difficulty is in reading it.","line:0ac296f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: With the corporation leadership here...I have to focus. There are...pressures acting upon me.","line:0454d29":"He places the specimens into a large metal chamber before sealing the lid. A motor runs briefly, and a pressure gauge on the chamber rises.","line:07a2027":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: The [C3]elder[/C3]...communicates in power...","line:0bda624":"He flips a large switch, and the metal chamber begins to spin. Slowly at first, then accelerating until the whole thing is a blur.","line:0f1496c":"Needles etch onto graph paper, transcribing the ascent of...something, scratched out at speed. A [C3]Dark Fluid[/C3] rises from a tube connected to the chamber.","line:09573d4":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Not yet...pure. We'll need more...down...deeper!","line:098923e":"IS THE SCIENTIST BEHIND THE BLACKBOARD HERE?","line:0049661":"With shocking speed he rushes towards the table, grabbing at the corpses.","line:0b912d2":"The shape that bursts through the blackboard barely resembles the Scientist; no longer meek and cowed, now a frightening visage of stretched skin and sharp teeth.","line:0d32720":"With a sickening crunch, he bites down into the sea scorpion carcass, [C3]black liquid[/C3] dripping from his mouth.","line:0cc5afc":"His terrible head snaps up to lock eyes with yours. A feral cry rises from his lungs, forming an accusatory scream with freshly born claws pointed in your direction.","line:0c081a1":"With limbs overcome by frantic spasms, he stumbles towards the nearest window, slowly at first, then arriving at considerable speed.","line:0e621dd":"GLASS SHATTER HERE?","line:0822ca7":"The aberrated form of the Scientist crashes through the glass, diving out, beyond the deck of the platform, down, hitting the water, then disappearing into the deep.","line:08b5208":"MINI CUTSCENE HERE?","line:0b3484c":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Ah hell...that's enough! Drill is clear - I repeat - drill is clear. Shut it down!","line:0b8cad8":"Down in the deep, something begins to brush against the legs of the rig.","line:0a3d075":"A droning voice begins to sound from the top of the rig, reverberating through the metal, down into the deep.","line:0d10b21":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: But sir, the seafloor here...it shouldn't be disturbed; this whole rig is built on some kind of...living fault! You have to trust me!","line:0b429bf":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Trust you? You, who couldn't even keep shipments in order, who involved locals, just to save your own hide?","line:0e8c1f1":"The Foreman cowers behind a clipboard.","line:087bb56":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: You, who put this whole operation in jeopardy?!","line:0766b4c":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Enough of this! Your concerns end at steel and scaffolding; the future of this corporation is for me alone to decide!","line:021eada":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Fire it up.","line:05ebfb3":"The drill descends once more into the blackness under the rig.","line:027c314":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: We're almost there. Give it another push. How much power can we give this thing?","line:0bc9413":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Sir, I don't think - we really shouldn't...","line:078cc86":"The executive shoots the foreman a glance, disdain and dismissal lacing the muscles on his face. The Foreman backs down, defeated.","line:09e83e8":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Setting the drill to full power, sir.","line:05fbc57":"Machinery in the drill tower steps into overdrive, blurring the air with the sound of gears turning.","line:07e99e9":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: It seems the reservoir is more unstable than we anticipated. Even with the [C1]drill removed[/C1], it appears the [C2]fissure is continuing to expand[/C2].","line:05dd0a0":"The Scientist steps away from the nearby window, knuckles still white from gripping the frame moments before.","line:0da6228":"He turns back and presses his forehead against the glass.","line:0a44b37":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: It was a way of...[C3]communicating[/C3], I suppose. We were working on emulating a language that we didn't fully understand. She began to twist the words.","line:0b08439":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: But she didn't agree with Ironhaven's methods. So, leveraging my role on the board for the Research Society, I pulled some strings and had her posted far away. To [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0].","line:0c450ed":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Please, [C0]go and find her[/C0]. I hope she's progressed her research sufficiently to help us.","line:08ee309":"The man in the suit turns to you.","line:06fc464":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: There's one final building that needs to be constructed on this platform - [C0]Fleet Services[/C0]. Without this building, we're unable to scale our efforts efficiently.","line:0738245":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: I'll cut you a deal. If you assist in the construction of this building, I'll permit the workers to fit your vessel with a [C1]significant hull upgrade[/C1].","line:0e33d85":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Get on with it.","line:0838195":"As the roar of the [C0]giant creature[/C0] fades, it leaves behind a silence on all that witnessed it. Faces stare from windows and hands grip railings, trying to process the spectacle.","line:065c1e5":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Boss, that must have been the thing that got all our material shipments - and [C0]now it's coming for the rig[/C0]!","line:0a4a62b":"A murmur of panic begins to rise from the onlookers.","line:07527cd":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Uh, it still has a little way to go - but you can't be serious, surely? Not with that thing in the water here?! [C2]Our lives are in danger and you want to keep drilling?![/C2]","line:0dab9ef":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Get it done.","line:0e0cb30":"The Executive turns and walks away towards his office, leaving the Foreman shaking his head.","line:017757c":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: He's insane. What the hell are we doing here? This drill...whatever's down there. [S1]We shouldn't be disturbing it[/S1].","line:07e0976":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Fisherman. You've got to help us. He won't listen to reason. But perhaps he'll listen to an...[C0]operational setback[/C0].","line:02bf3a9":"What do you have in mind?","line:03b358f":"What do you mean by \"operational setback\"?","line:0706a4a":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: We can't shut down the drill ourselves - not without [C2]repercussions from the corporation following us for the rest of our lives[/C2].","line:063f0b2":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: But if it were to be damaged by a force of nature or...[C3]force of the deep[/C3], we'd have no choice but to abandon our positions.","line:01cc785":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I know it sounds crazy. But if the [C0]defenses were to stop operating[/C0] suddenly, it would leave the [C1]drill vulnerable[/C1].","line:0ae48fd":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Please. Have a think, see what you can do.","line:0c3dd8a":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: So. What do you want?","line:0246e18":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: What else?","line:0cee1dc":"The Ironhaven Corporation has been constructing a drilling platform.","line:058354d":"Ironhaven Corporation's head Scientist seems to know you.","line:05ee670":"Tell me about the defensive tech you've been working on.","line:0c98658":"We need to protect the rig and its workers.","line:0d8dfc1":"That's all.","line:01fc5b8":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Oh, and you're helping them with that, I suppose? Do you have any idea what they're even doing?","line:0661279":"She turns away and tries to recompose herself with a few deep breaths.","line:059567a":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Of course you don't. You're just trying to help. But you've seen what's happened to the water here - and elsewhere, I imagine.","line:0548d36":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: And I know him. He's the reason I was posted all the way out here, so far from home. He might've mentioned that I studied under him.","line:06e8a5b":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: But I studied him, too. His theories on nature's cycles were...odd. He never went into much detail, but his work had some curious influences.","line:0e61f78":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I heard whispers through the door of his office, saw confusing diagrams that lingered in half-erased chalk dust and on torn up shreds of paper.","line:041d6a5":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Never could make much sense of it.","line:0d1a86e":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Well, it's the same tech used in that Repulsion Machine I gave you.","line:0c7011a":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Strictly speaking, I wouldn't call it a defense system. It doesn't interact with anything on a physical level.","line:0246542":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: You see, Ironhaven's scientific communication division have long been working on projects to further their exertion over the natural world.","line:0490673":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: It's complicated stuff, but essentially they were trying to emit signals to communicate with...well, anything they wanted to, I suppose.","line:0304e30":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: The tech I've been working on is along those lines, but instead of a wide spectrum of communication, it attempts to broadcast a single 'word': \"[C2]FLEE[/C2]\".","line:0edcd9c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: It emits the vocalized panic responses of every animal I was able to gather acoustic data for.","line:030a829":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I'll give you some schematics. I'm sure someone there is smart enough to decipher them and get it built.","line:083000c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Just...don't let them think this means I forgive them. Or that I approve of what they're doing.","line:0e3152b":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Anything else about those defenses?","line:001437f":"Yes, they worked.","line:04730eb":"The workers on the rig want to find a way to sabotage them.","line:07df482":"That's all.","line:0104d98":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Good. It's always nice to have additional data points.","line:03e8a9c":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Found their conscience, have they? I suppose they're wanting it to look like an accident. They wouldn't want to face the corp's wrath if they were found culpable.","line:04cd8dc":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: Hmm, I do have a pleasingly elegant idea, actually. We don't have to sabotage the defenses in a traditional sense.","line:0634e59":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: If you recall, they emit a sort of 'word'. At the moment, they're broadcasting a warning: \"[C2]FLEE[/C2]\".","line:0ef520d":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: But we can change that. I have other recordings, of other words. Instead of a warning, it could broadcast an...invitation.","line:01aa936":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: There's one in particular. I've been referring to it by its closest human analogue:","line:041091a":"RESEARCHER_NAME_KEY: I'll prepare some blueprints for the module. You'll have to assemble it and slot it into the top of the black box.","line:00d4220":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Still around, huh?","line:0ed287b":"A helmeted figure emerges from the shadows by a building site. He lifts his visor.","line:0fef143":"He gestures to a pile of materials behind him.","line:00b2efe":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: We're short on materials. Once they arrive, we can start working. ","line:0f9705e":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Between you and me, the corp has a pretty ruthless reputation of tracking down anyone who moves against them. People tend to just make the one mistake, if you get what I mean.","line:0ac83cb":"A woman is stood just inside the doorway, sketching a design in her notebook.","line:04b22cb":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Welcome back. Hope things have been steady for you out there.","line:09216a6":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Those enhanced rods are treating you well? I worked hard on those designs.","line:0865326":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: We don't fully understand the properties of all the materials we're working with, but it's something the head Scientist is working on.","line:05404c2":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Remember that the things we build here all need different ingredients. It's good to keep a stock of various materials on hand.","line:0e001de":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Most of these projects I'm working on are for the rollout of the corp's new fleet. It'll be cutting edge.","line:0bf1621":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: We're still waiting for a [C0]materials[/C0] shipment before we can [C1]upgrade the factory[/C1]. When it arrives, we'll be able to [C1]make new items[/C1].","line:0055a50":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: HQ said they're not sending any more delivery ships, so if we want to get this place [C1]upgraded[/C1], we'll need [C0]materials[/C0] from elsewhere.","line:09e42c7":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Almost there. One more delivery of [C0]materials[/C0] and we'll be [C1]fully operational[/C1].","line:0edd960":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Don't like these waters. But the corp seems to.","line:03f1fb6":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Some advice, while you're on corp property: don't go poking around.","line:0b4d272":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: The work's hard, but as long as the pay's good, I'll do it. And it is.","line:093c064":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Not much for small talk. Let's get on with it.","line:037fbb6":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Heat and metal. Beats the cold winds out here.","line:0a759d8":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Don't have the materials for this place yet.","line:0654c86":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: I have plans for an interchangeable module system. You'll see; I'll show you when we're set up here. But, uh...","line:014fe45":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: These modules can be attached to your ship. Placement's flexible too, they can be wired up to wherever they need to go.","line:02c59f6":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: One more lot of [C0]materials[/C0], then we'll be able to [C1]upgrade some of your boat's basic functions[/C1].","line:044e9fe":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Can you believe the size of that squid? It's shaking the whole damn rig. Doesn't seem like it should be possible; the legs are anchored pretty deep.","line:04c4f12":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: We're in the planning stages for an [C1]expansion to the Factory[/C1]. Maybe you'd be able to help out?","line:0ce7bb8":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: I've been drawing up some plans for a [C1]new Factory wing[/C1]. Take a look if you get a chance.","line:0b6768e":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: We're about ready to start construction on the [C1]final section of the Factory[/C1].","line:0bc73bb":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: Those tentacles seem angry. Not surprised.","line:091551c":"FOUNDER_NAME_KEY: [C1]Foundry's about to get bigger soon[/C1]. Still waiting on a delivery though.","line:09e1422":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: That squid thing keeps shaking the rig. It's making it pretty damn hard to concentrate in here!","line:042e30a":"ENGINEER_NAME_KEY: Foreman says we're due to start on an [C1]extension[/C1] to the building soon.","line:02548cb":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Don't forget. The rig still needs some kind of defense system constructed. The people here are...depending on you, oddly enough.","line:01c668a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: And...while you're there, try to [C0]catch some of the local specimens[/C0]. I think they hold the key to understanding what we're here for.","line:03297e9":"The defenses are operational, emitting a droning sound that grates at the ears.","line:0c63df7":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: We've gotta get this place operational, or the boss will have my head!","line:0d1973e":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: We can make [C1]improvements to your vessel here[/C1], including some cutting-edge Ironhaven tech that you [C0]won't find anywhere else[/C0].","line:0fb7c65":"Outside, the Foreman is in conversation with a recent arrival to the rig; a stern looking man in a suit.","line:08828d9":"Outside, the Executive is talking to the Foreman.","line:0b716ed":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: After that, I don't want to see you around here any more. Our operation is confidential.","line:05655ac":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Now we can finally get this drill started! [S2]ALL CLEAR![/S2]","line:0e9f064":"What's the purpose of this rig?","line:0c66c58":"Aren't you going to stop the drill?","line:07cc607":"Do you know anything about these mutated fish I've been finding?","line:0162101":"What's going to happen to the fissure that opened up?","line:09111a5":"Do you know anything more about the prehistoric fish I found?","line:0968bb1":"I've encountered strange creatures in the contaminated areas.","line:0b3d8b1":"What's your opinion of your boss?","line:054d061":"Have you learned anything about the Dark Fluid I collected?","line:0d5f904":"You seem concerned.","line:02c6d26":"Are you okay?","line:0d590ec":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Our current executive's father hired me when I was fresh out of college. He must've seen something in me, all those years ago.","line:0ff56b9":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: If my hypothesis proves correct, it'll yield a significant asset for the corporation's business diversification strategy.","line:0532660":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Ah, yes, I believe the drill has already stopped operating. The Foreman should be making preparations to withdraw it from the seabed.","line:045cef6":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: It's not something you can just yank out, apparently. The drill team will take their time to try to ensure minimal disturbance.","line:0047d05":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Mutations are present in almost all species, and fish are certainly no exception. In my years of study I've seen fish with extra fins, eyes, and even heads!","line:04f077e":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Yes, they're a relatively normal part of the development of a species. Occasionally they can be influenced by external factors, but only in exceptional circumstances.","line:0e578ec":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Now that the drill has withdrawn, it should settle down - provided nothing else disturbs the seabed. I expect that, given enough time, it will be filled in with sediment entirely.","line:09f8e27":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: In the meantime, it appears to have opened up some interesting opportunities for research!","line:0b0fcce":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Nothing useful, aside from confirming with some peers that they are indeed species that were previously thought to be extinct.","line:0cbfb6a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: There's even a special name for that, you know. A Lazarus taxon - a species seemingly raised from the dead.","line:0ffc26b":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Oh? What did they look like?","line:0e11594":"You begin to describe the creatures to the Scientist, but as you grasp at the images in your head, they melt away, replaced with a swirling blackness in your mind's eye.","line:0e08154":"After your description trails off, the Scientist looks at you with some concern.","line:08d061d":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Long nights at sea, unusual weather conditions, sleep deprivation - they can all lead to auditory and visual hallucinations. Not to worry, best to get some rest.","line:08f534a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: My...master? Oh, the Executive, yes. It's...he's...everywhere. Very hard working. Always has been. Always will be...","line:0dd455c":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: He needs me...my work. It all has to be correct. Do you understand? We have to be in the right place. Or else...there's not much time left.","line:051915b":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: It's...unlike any substance I've ever seen...touched. It's smooth one moment...silky...and the next...sharp...stabbing.","line:0daebd5":"The Scientist flinches at something in the air above him. A moment later, the lights flicker. The subtle pop of a blown capacitor can be heard somewhere on the nearby bench.","line:0a751c7":"His voice drops to a breathy murmur.","line:0e0ae34":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: It holds...secrets...instructions...whispers...","line:0096a5a":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Concerned...no. Concern implies...","line:0d95803":"He turns to look at you. One of his eyes is bloodshot, the white completely overrun with dark red blood.","line:0dbc79f":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Concern implies...that we didn't know this would happen.","line:014ff93":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: The inevitable...conclusion...","line:0285e4f":"He rocks back and forth, hand shading his eyes from the harsh lights above.","line:05ec5e1":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Our work...almost complete...","line:0e2b1e2":"Is whatever you're here for really worth risking the lives of your people?","line:0bab3d8":"He scoffs.","line:041786b":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: Honestly, even if I cared to know myself, I'm not sure why you think I'd tell you.","line:024b80b":"The Executive makes a show of looking around and peering over a nearby railing.","line:046d010":"EXECUTIVE_NAME_KEY: My \"people\"? These are employees.","line:084494e":"Have there been any patches of contamination sighted in the area?","line:0782495":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: There have been areas of [C3]contamination[/C3] sighted in [C0]The Marrows[/C0].","line:03c7b09":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: There have been areas of [C3]contamination[/C3] sighted in [C0]Gale Cliffs[/C0].","line:0b5d7a9":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: There have been areas of [C3]contamination[/C3] sighted in [C0]Stellar Basin[/C0].","line:049bc64":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: There have been areas of [C3]contamination[/C3] sighted in [C0]Twisted Strand[/C0].","line:0baccf2":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: There have been areas of [C3]contamination[/C3] sighted in [C0]Devil's Spine[/C0].","line:0b2a5ec":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: This hull schematic will add a little [C1]more storage[/C1] to your vessel, but the primary benefit is all the [C1]new slots for fishing equipment[/C1]!","line:0a552c5":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Hope she serves you well, fisherman!","line:0e2a1d6":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Hey, fisherman - thanks again for your help filling that generator. I've reported our new operational status to HQ.","line:05c105e":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: In fact, they've given me a budget to [C1]compensate you for any additional biomass[/C1] you bring in. Just see me at the [C0]Generator[/C0] and I'll pay you.","line:0bc1f10":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I can now [C1]pay you for any biomass you add to the generator[/C1]. The bigger the better, I assume? This isn't really my area...","line:05b56fa":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Generator's always hungry. Any biomass to throw in?","line:08484da":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: Energy levels are good, but I won't say no to a top-up. Add some fish if you've got 'em.","line:07710f6":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: This BioFuel system is great! More places oughta run on fish. And crabs too, I guess. Got any for the hopper today?","line:07316cd":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: [C2]I can't pay a premium for your fish[/C2] here, but it's better than nothing, right?","line:056ae66":"A figure emerges from lower decks and beckons you over into the shadows.","line:0fbae71":"FOUNDER_MARKET_NAME_KEY: If you're going to be hanging around...maybe we can do business. Come see me at the [C0]Undermarket[/C0] - alone.","line:072c390":"FOUNDER_MARKET_NAME_KEY: Got some [C0]items you might be interested in[/C0]. Don't ask where they come from - better off not knowing. Can make some [C0]basic repairs[/C0] too, but it'll cost ya.","line:045d9ed":"FOUNDER_MARKET_NAME_KEY: Don't tell anyone from the corp about this place. I'm doing you a favour, you know.","line:03742b1":"FOUNDER_MARKET_NAME_KEY: Nobody ever does a thorough stocktake at big corporations. Lucky for us.","line:0ef6e18":"FOUNDER_MARKET_NAME_KEY: Things go missing all the time. Who knows where they end up? Doesn't matter in a place like this.","line:0fae400":"FOUNDER_MARKET_NAME_KEY: The bigwigs don't bother with the lower decks and the folks down here. Why would they mingle with people like us? I'm not complaining.","line:08b216e":"What was I supposed to be doing?","line:0b6fb69":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: Locals in The Marrows and Gale Cliffs have reported sightings of a [C3]strange ooze[/C3] on the surface of the water. I need you to collect a canister of it for me.","line:02eb548":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: You'll need to upgrade the [C0]Factory[/C0] and construct a [C0]Siphon Trawler[/C0] before you'll be able to do that, though.","line:08bac2c":"SCIENTIST_NAME_KEY: You'll need to equip the [C0]Siphon Trawler[/C0] and deploy it in [C3]contaminated[C3] areas to extract samples from the water.","line:0fe6f5f":"\\[Cutscene 3.5 (Defenses)\\]","line:042cb1f":"\\[Cutscene 7 (Scientist)\\]","line:0adfce8":"FOREMAN_NAME_KEY: I've been trying to keep a record of where all that [C3]dark liquid[/C3] has been showing up. [C0]Come see me if you need pointing to any contamination patches[/C0]."};
